evidence found — thirty-two of the
thirty-three names occur nowhere in
the tracker before this chapter, the
thirty-third (Jian Yang) standing
there only as Paper 042's Beihang
author and kept apart from this
paper's M-A-P namesake; in Will's
Twitter archive the names are absent
and 'Ouro' stands only inside
'Ouroboros'; the web shows no tie;
the thirty-three are entered fresh
at 1.5.6, their vector True +1,
Unknown +18. Q254-Q258 open.

Paper 056 — Chuang et al., 'DoLa:
Decoding by Contrasting Layers
Improves Factuality in Large Language
Models' (arXiv:2309.03883), filed as
Chapter 74. A language model's facts
are injected late in its depth; DoLa
decodes from the difference between
the final layer and a premature layer
of the same model, chosen per token
by divergence, amplifying what the
mature layers added. Eleven concepts
(1.2.746-1.2.756); cluster AT
extended to thirteen papers; cluster
J weighed and not joined — the
references are the judged model's own
layers. The walk filed the descendant
first: ALW (Chapter 72) descends from
DoLa, and the ancestor arrives third
in its own line.

Paper 057 — He et al., 'OlympiadBench:
A Challenging Benchmark for Promoting
AGI with Olympiad-Level Bilingual
Multimodal Scientific Problems'
(arXiv:2402.14008), filed as Chapter
75. A benchmark artifact of 8,476
olympiad problems in mathematics and
physics, English and Chinese, every
problem carrying its expert solution,
graded by a shipped scoring pipeline
over a five-type answer contract.
Twelve concepts (1.2.757-1.2.768);
cluster AY extended to two papers —
the measure as a fixed table, here
with its apparatus attached; cluster
J weighed and not joined — the
pipeline's verdicts are spent at
grading, not inside the judged run.
The dataset was held entire, and its
counts and headline averages
recompute exactly from the artifact.

Paper 058 — HuggingFaceH4, 'AIME 2024'
(the AIME 2024 benchmark artifact,
Hugging Face), filed as Chapter 76.
The 2024 sitting-pair of the
examination Chapter 70 filed for
2025, from a different publisher's
hand: thirty problems in one file,
every row carrying its worked
solution, its source url and its
parent-set number, its key
zero-padded to the contract's width.
Seven concepts (1.2.769-1.2.775);
cluster AY extended to three papers
— the country's first year pair, the
measure read at two adjacent years
so the examination and the
transcription can be told apart;
cluster J weighed and not joined —
the artifact contains no mechanism,
and its key is spent at grading. The
dataset was held entire, and its key
re-derived entire: all thirty
answers recomputed from their
problems.

Paper 059 — Karras, Aittala,
Kynkäänniemi, Lehtinen, Aila &
Laine, 'Guiding a Diffusion Model
with a Bad Version of Itself'
(arXiv:2406.02507v3), filed as
Chapter 77. A diffusion sampler
steered at every step by a worse
version of itself: the strong
model's errors are the weak model's
errors, louder, and the difference
between the two denoised results
points away from them — quality
bought without the variation tax
classifier-free guidance charges.
Eight concepts (1.2.776-1.2.783);
cluster AV extended to two papers —
the trajectory country gains
steering; cluster J weighed on the
steering/verdict distinction and
not joined — the difference
corrects the path and judges
nothing. Restructuring Pass #36
fell due at the filing and was run
in-pass. The paper's printed
arithmetic was recomputed entire:
twenty-seven declarations,
twenty-seven exact.

Paper 060 — Yang, Lee, Nowak &
Papailiopoulos, 'Looped Transformers
are Better at Learning Learning
Algorithms' (arXiv:2311.12424v3),
filed as Chapter 78. The ancestor of
the looped line, filed after its
descendants: one block, looped on its
own output with the prompt re-injected
at every step, trained on a window of
its last iterates until the loop
itself is a learning algorithm and
its settled iterate is the fit. Seven
concepts (1.2.784-1.2.790), one
foundation (1.3.376), one held concept
grounded in its source (1.2.680);
cluster AT extended to fourteen
papers; cluster J weighed and not
joined — nothing in the loop renders
a verdict. Restructuring Pass #37
fell due at the filing — Paper 060
was its own trigger — and was run
in-pass. The paper's printed
arithmetic was recomputed: ten
declarations, ten exact.

Paper 061 — Shi, Han, Lewis,
Tsvetkov, Zettlemoyer & Yih, 'Trusting
Your Evidence: Hallucinate Less with
Context-aware Decoding'
(arXiv:2305.14739v1), filed as Chapter
79. The contrast line's newest shape:
one model run with its evidence and
without it, the difference amplified —
the prior made computable as the
withheld-context distribution, the
context's say priced token by token
in nats. Nine concepts
(1.2.791-1.2.799) and one foundation
(1.3.377); cluster AT extended to
fifteen papers, its contrast members
named a sub-country, the contrast
line; cluster J weighed and not
joined — the contrast steers, and
renders no verdict. The paper's
printed arithmetic was recomputed:
fourteen declarations, fourteen
exact — and two of its prose
percentages fail against its own
tables, carried as caveats.

Paper 062 — Sanchez, Fan, Spangher,
Levi, Ammanamanchi & Biderman, 'Stay
on Topic with Classifier-Free
Guidance' (arXiv:2306.17806v1),
filed as Chapter 80. The contrast
line's root, filed last of its
members so far: one model under two
conditionings, the prompt against
its own absence, the difference
amplified by γ — the classifier the
method's name dismisses identified
inside the model itself, by Bayes'
rule. Eight concepts
(1.2.800-1.2.807) and one foundation
(1.3.378); cluster AT extended to
sixteen papers through the contrast
line, its seventh shape of
reference, with AV kinship recorded;
cluster J weighed and not joined —
the combination steers, and renders
no verdict. The paper's printed
arithmetic was recomputed: eighteen
declarations, eighteen pass — and
its code table prints a third model
size whose numbers are its second
size's, duplicated, carried as a
caveat.

Paper 063 — O'Brien & Lewis,
'Contrastive Decoding Improves
Reasoning in Large Language Models'
(arXiv:2309.09117v2), filed as
Chapter 81. The contrast line's
founding shape in its second
filing: two models, an expert and
an amateur, the difference between
them spent not on open text but on
reasoning — the device stating its
own law, that the contrast
amplifies only what the expert has
learned better, and falling silent
where the gap is zero. Nine
concepts (1.2.808-1.2.816), no
foundation; cluster AT extended to
seventeen papers through the
contrast line, no new shape of
reference; cluster J weighed and
not joined — the ranking mode its
nearest approach since the
crossing, its evidence still
inside the pair. The paper's
printed arithmetic was recomputed:
forty-seven declarations, forty-
seven pass — and six of its
printed summary numbers disagree
with their own rows, the 'up to 8
points' headline among them,
carried as caveats.

Paper 064 — Zhu, Zhang, Li, Shi,
Duan, Wang, Zhou, Banerjee & Qin,
'Beyond Parameters: Exploring
Virtual Logic Depth for Scaling
Laws' (arXiv:2506.18233v3), filed
as Chapter 82. The looped
transformer taken as a scaling
dimension and its yield audited in
two currencies: repeat the layers
with tied parameters and the model
stores no more than it did —
absorbed entropy flat across every
pattern and dose — while its
reasoning climbs, a 50M model at
twelve layers effective passing a
native 150M model on the same
test. Four concepts
(1.2.817-1.2.820), no foundation;
cluster AT extended to eighteen
papers, not through the contrast
line — nothing here is contrasted;
cluster J weighed and not joined —
the work's only verdicts are its
benchmarks' keys, consulted after
the runs. The paper's printed
arithmetic was recomputed:
forty-two declarations, forty-two
pass — and its blanket 'across all
tested configurations' fails
against its own Table 1 in six
cells, carried as caveats.

Paper 065 — Gao, Tow, Abbasi,
Biderman, Black, DiPofi, Foster,
Golding, Hsu, Le Noac'h, Li,
McDonell, Muennighoff, Ociepa,
Phang, Reynolds, Schoelkopf,
Skowron, Sutawika, Tang, Thite,
Wang, Wang & Zou, 'A framework for
few-shot language model evaluation'
(Zenodo deposit v0.4.0), filed as
Chapter 83. The instrument the
book is measured with, filed in
itself: a benchmark as a
declaration, a model as three
requests, the few-shot draw seeded
in the code, the ranking corrected
per character, and every score
carrying its bootstrap error bar.
Seven concepts (1.2.821-1.2.827),
no foundation; cluster AY extended
to four papers — its first
resident that is not a table, the
grader detached from every table
and made general; cluster J
weighed and not joined — the key
is consulted by the harness after
the judged computation ends, never
by the judged. The house check ran
against the held deposit itself:
twenty-nine declarations,
twenty-nine pass — and the
deposit's three citation forms
name three different works,
carried as caveats. Restructuring
Pass #38 ran with the filing: five
merges weighed and held apart, the
next trigger at Paper 070 or 840
canonical concepts.

Paper 066 — Liu, Xia, Wang &
Zhang, 'Is your code generated by
ChatGPT really correct? Rigorous
evaluation of large language
models for code generation'
(arXiv:2305.01210v3), filed as
Chapter 84. The examination
audits itself: a model that has
read the ground truth writes the
seed inputs, type-aware mutation
grows them a thousand deep,
contracts fence the input domain,
and a differential oracle grades
the candidate against the
reference implementation itself —
764.1 tests where the base table
holds 9.6. Eight concepts
(1.2.828-1.2.835) and one
foundation (1.3.379, set cover);
cluster AY extended to five
papers — the country's audit of
its own founding objects, which
finds eighteen of the base key's
ground truths defective and the
field's rankings reversing under
the deeper examination; cluster J
weighed and not joined — the
oracle's verdicts are spent at
grading, after the judged
computation ends, and the
weighing narrows Q288 on the
record. The house check ran
against the held artifact itself:
thirty-five declarations,
thirty-five pass — and the
paper's prose disagrees with its
tables and its artifact in four
places, carried as caveats.

Paper 067 — Li, Holtzman, Fried,
Liang, Eisner, Hashimoto,
Zettlemoyer & Lewis, 'Contrastive
Decoding: Open-ended Text
Generation as Optimization'
(arXiv:2210.15097v2), filed as
Chapter 85. The contrast line's
founding ancestor, filed after its
descendants: a strong model and a
weak one of the same family, the
weak spent as a mirror of the
strong's failure modes, the choice
gated by the plausibility
constraint and scored by the
unweighted log-ratio under beam
search. Eight concepts
(1.2.836-1.2.843), no foundation,
and one held concept revised —
1.2.525, whose weighted form the
book imported from a descendant's
lineage, corrected to the founding
rule; cluster AT extended through
the contrast line to nineteen
papers — the founding shape's
first filing, the line's eighth;
cluster J weighed and not joined —
the reference distinct and the
spending inside the judged
computation, but the score a
preference among the judged
object's own candidates, not a
verdict of it, and the weighing
testifies on Q288. The house
check recomputed the work's
internal arithmetic entire:
seventeen declarations, seventeen
pass, and ten hand checks — and
the ablation appendix prints one
row twice, carried as a caveat.
The filing crosses 840 canonical
concepts: the restructuring
trigger set by Pass #38 is
reached, and the restructure
stands for its own pass.

Paper 068 — Ho & Salimans,
'Classifier-Free Diffusion
Guidance' (arXiv:2207.12598v1),
filed as Chapter 86. The founding
text of the book's most-descended
device, filed after its descendants:
one network trained as two models by
conditioning dropout, sampled by
combining its conditional and
unconditional score estimates with
the unconditional subtracted. Five
concepts (1.2.844-1.2.848), one
foundation (1.3.380, the score), and
two held concepts revised — 1.2.800,
restated in the founding diffusion
construction with the language-model
port as the port and the strength's
shifted zero recorded; and 1.2.801,
the implicit classifier qualified to
the exact scores its founding paper
grants it. Cluster AV extended to
three papers — the device's founding
text in the device's native country,
its AT contrast-line kinship
recorded; cluster J weighed and not
joined — the combination steers the
trajectory, and the paper itself
denies it renders any classifier's
verdict. The house check recomputed
the work's internal arithmetic:
six declarations, six pass, and
thirty-six hand checks — and the
paper's summary sentence inverts its
headline table's FID behaviour,
carried as a caveat.

Paper 069 — Chen, Zhang & Hinton,
'Analog Bits: Generating Discrete
Data using Diffusion Models with
Self-Conditioning'
(arXiv:2208.04202v2), filed as
Chapter 87. The trajectory country
widens its cargo and gains a
memory: discrete data spelled in
bits, the bits cast to real numbers
and modeled by an unchanged
continuous diffusion, read back by
a threshold at the end; the
denoiser handed its own previous
estimate as an input; and the
sampler's clock split from the
state's, the network told a later
time than the state it reads. Five
concepts (1.2.849-1.2.853) and one
foundation (1.3.381, the bit); no
held concept revised. Cluster AV
extended to four papers — the
construction a denoising trajectory
entire, its appendix's
contrast-family device recorded as
kinship for the device, not the
paper; cluster J weighed and not
joined — the conditioning signal is
the judged object's own previous
estimate, spent as steering, and
the work's one threshold reads the
finished sample rather than judging
it. The house check recomputed the
work's internal arithmetic:
thirteen declarations, thirteen
pass, and forty-two hand checks —
and two of Figure 10's caption
scores disagree with the table they
illustrate, carried as a caveat.
Zhang returns to the book, a
co-author of Paper 038, the chapter
whose bibliography queued this
work.

Paper 070 — Chen et al.,
'Evaluating Large Language Models
Trained on Code'
(arXiv:2107.03374v2), filed as
Chapter 88. The examination
country gains its founding table
for code, five chapters after its
audit: 164 problems written by
hand so the training corpus
cannot already hold them, graded
by running the candidate against
unit tests rather than matching a
reference text, the runs housed
in a sandbox built for untrusted
code, and the count kept by
pass@k with its unbiased
estimator. Seven concepts
(1.2.854-1.2.860); no held concept
revised. Cluster AY extended to
six papers — the deliverable a
table and its measure, the base
table of Chapter 84's audited
resident; the infrastructure
founding weighed under Chapter
84's condition and declined a
third time; cluster J weighed and
not joined — the work's verdicts
are spent after the judged
computation or one stage above
it, never inside it. The house
check recomputed the work's
internal arithmetic: five
declarations, five pass, and
twenty-eight hand checks — the
estimator's unbiasedness re-run
in simulation, and the abstract's
GPT-J figure and sampling
headline both failing against the
paper's own tables, carried as
caveats. All fifty-eight authors
are new to the book. The filing
lands the concept count on 860,
and a restructuring falls due.

Paper 071 — Austin et al.,
'Program Synthesis with Large
Language Models'
(arXiv:2108.07732v1), filed as
Chapter 89. The examination
country gains its second founding
for code, one leg after its
sibling: two examinations built
for the purpose in a single work —
MBPP, 974 problems written to
order by an internal crowd with
exactly three asserts each, and
MathQA-Python, 23,914 problems
translated from a domain-specific
language and filtered by execution
at their construction — graded by
the executed verdict in its direct
form, eighty samples a problem and
two counts kept. Seven concepts
(1.2.861-1.2.867); no held concept
revised. Cluster AY extended to
seven papers — the deliverables
two tables and their audits; the
infrastructure founding weighed
under Chapter 84's condition and
declined a fourth time; cluster J
weighed and not joined — the
work's verdicts are spent at an
examination's construction or
between runs, never inside a
judged computation. The house
check recomputed the work's
internal arithmetic: six
declarations, six pass, and
twenty-eight hand checks — the
counting closing entire, and the
abstract's 83.8 percent standing
on the wrong dataset against the
paper's own Table 6, carried as a
caveat. Ten of the eleven authors
are new to the book; Charles
Sutton returns, from Paper 017.
No restructuring falls due.

Paper 072 — Cobbe et al.,
'Training Verifiers to Solve Math
Word Problems'
(arXiv:2110.14168v2), filed as
Chapter 90. The examination
country gains its founding for
mathematics, and its first
trained judge: GSM8K, 8,500
grade-school word problems whose
key is worked solutions in
natural language, built to be
trained on; a verifier trained on
a hundred thousand of the
generator's own sampled solutions
labeled by their final answers
alone; and the selection that
spends it — a hundred samples
drawn, the judge's favourite
returned, a judged 6B standing
where a finetuned 175B guessing
once stands, in a comparison the
work prints only as a figure.
Seven concepts (1.2.868-1.2.874);
no held concept revised. Cluster
AY extended to eight papers —
the deliverable a table whose
key teaches a model to grade;
the infrastructure founding
weighed under Chapter 84's
condition and declined a fifth
time; cluster J weighed a
nineteenth time and not joined —
the work's verdicts train a judge
before any judged run or select
among finished candidates after
it, and its token-level judge,
the one verdict-form that runs
along the judged object's own
length, is computed and never
spent. The house check
recomputed the work's internal
arithmetic: seven declarations,
seven pass, and twenty-three
hand checks — the counting
closing entire, and no headline
solve rate standing in the
work's text at all. Seven of
the twelve authors return from
Paper 070; five are new to the
book. No restructuring falls
due.

Paper 073 — Hendrycks et al.,
'Measuring Massive Multitask
Language Understanding'
(arXiv:2009.03300v3), filed as
Chapter 91. The examination
country gains its broadest table:
fifty-seven subjects across the
whole curriculum, 14,079 test
questions, administered to models
that never trained on it — a
pretraining examination, whose
scores census what pretraining
put in. What it finds: a lopsided
profile, capability jagged from
69 percent to chance with the
pedagogical order inverted; a
chance floor, models up to
thirteen billion parameters at
random chance where narrower
tables rose smoothly; an expert
line no model reaches on any
subject; an examined that cannot
price its own answers; and a
table that audits its own key
against the examined's memory and
certifies it unmemorized. Seven
concepts (1.2.875-1.2.881); no
held concept revised. Cluster AY
extended to nine papers — the
deliverable the union table, the
domains of the country's
single-domain tables become
subjects among fifty-seven; the
infrastructure founding weighed
under Chapter 84's condition and
declined a sixth time; cluster J
weighed a twentieth time and not
joined — the key is consulted at
grading, the worked examples
steer before the run, the
confidence is read afterward, and
no verdict is spent inside any
judged computation. The house
check recomputed the work's
internal arithmetic: twenty-eight
declarations, twenty-seven pass
and one at tension, and
twenty-four hand checks — the
counting closing entire but for
the work's own total, which
claims four questions its splits
cannot produce. One of the seven
authors returns from Paper 065;
six are new to the book. The
filing crosses the 880-concept
line: a restructuring falls due,
and stands for its own pass.

Paper 074 — Bisk et al., 'PIQA:
Reasoning about Physical
Commonsense in Natural Language'
(arXiv:1911.11641v1), filed as
Chapter 92. The examination
country gains its smallest table:
a paired examination of physical
commonsense — a goal, two
finished solutions, exactly one
correct — built because reporting
bias keeps the physical world out
of the text models read. Its
wrong answers are trick solutions
written by annotators to fool;
its pairs are matched at the
surface until only the physics
differs; and the whole table is
the residue of an adversarial
filter that discarded whatever
one model's embeddings could
predict and produced the folds
themselves. Humans score 94.9 on
validation, the best model 77.1
on test; priced per pivot word,
the best model stands at 90
percent on 'spoon', 75 on 'water'
and 66 on 'freeze'; and a class
of its items is keyed by
convenience against the work's
own exactly-one-correct rule.
Seven concepts (1.2.882-1.2.888);
no held concept revised. Cluster
AY extended to ten papers — the
deliverable a table of pairs, the
unit of examination the pair
itself; the infrastructure
founding weighed under Chapter
84's condition and declined a
seventh time; cluster J weighed a
twenty-first time and not joined
— the pair's scores are the
examined's own, spent at grading;
the filter's verdicts are spent
at construction, before any
judged computation exists; and
the human vote is the key itself.
The house check recomputed the
work's internal arithmetic:
twenty-three declarations, all
pass, and twenty-four hand
checks, three of them designed
negatives — the caption's gap
overstated, the token total
underivable from the work's own
numbers, the parameter ratio not
the ratio of the printed sizes.
All five authors are new to the
book.

Paper 075 — Sakaguchi et al.,
'WinoGrande: An Adversarial
Winograd Schema Challenge at
Scale' (arXiv:1907.10641v2),
filed as Chapter 93. The
examination country gains its
largest small table: the Winograd
schema manufactured — thirty-eight
thousand twin sentences
crowdsourced around random anchor
words, validated by majority
vote, and debiased by AfLite, the
adversarial filter the book
already held from its PIQA
instance, here founded and named,
its scroll revised in place
(1.2.884). Its twins turn on a
trigger word; a third of the
debiased questions stand with
their twin broken by the filter;
the filter's discards are
released as the training pool,
and the headline models train on
the union of kept and discarded.
Humans score 94.0 and the best
model 79.1, trained on the full
forty thousand; trained on the
debiased nine thousand alone, the
work's own footnote reports
chance. Underneath stands the
work's suspicion — that the era's
scores are earned for the wrong
reasons — turned on its own five
transfer triumphs and left open
as a question. Seven concepts
(1.2.889-1.2.895) and one held
concept revised; cluster AY
extended to eleven papers; the
infrastructure founding weighed
under Chapter 84's condition and
declined an eighth time; cluster
J weighed a twenty-second time
and not joined — the filter's
verdicts are spent at
construction, the majority vote
is the key itself, and no verdict
is spent inside any judged
computation. The house check
recomputed the work's internal
arithmetic: forty-eight
declarations, all pass, and
twenty-three hand checks, two of
them designed negatives — the
collected questions overstated
against the twin count, and a
borrowed dataset's split that
does not sum. Two authors return
from Paper 074; two are new to
the book.

Paper 076 — Dehghani et al.,
'Universal Transformers'
(arXiv:1807.03819v3), filed as
Chapter 94. The loop country
gains its founding ancestor: the
construction the head concept
(1.2.523) has named as its
lineage head since Paper 038 —
one Transformer block, its
attention and transition weights
tied across every depth step,
revising all positions in
parallel — filed in its own
right at last, and that scroll
revised in place to stand on its
source. The ancestor brings the
devices the descendants spend:
halting per position, so depth
becomes a field over the
sequence; the ponder time, spent
depth read back as difficulty;
the coordinate that tells the
shared block which revision it
is computing; and the
remainder-weighted state a
halted position contributes.
Over it stands the country's
largest claim, that depth which
scales with the input buys
computational universality. Its
small tasks are near-perfect,
its translation beats the
Transformer it generalizes, and
its appendix prints the seed
averages its headlines are
chosen against. Six concepts
(1.2.896-1.2.901) and one held
concept revised; cluster AT
extended to twenty papers;
cluster J weighed a
twenty-third time and not
joined — the halting decision is
read off the run's own state and
spent on the run's length, and
no reference is consulted for
any verdict. The house check
recomputed the work's internal
arithmetic: forty-four
declarations, all pass, and
seventeen hand checks, all
pass, with one designed tension
— the agreement table's delta
row misprints one difference —
and one designed negative, a
summary sentence that sends its
two tables to their tasks the
wrong way round. Four authors
are new to the book; one
returns from Papers 070 and
072.

Ninety-fifth walk: the examination is
rebuilt against its solver (Paper 077,
Chapter 95). One year after the
predecessor examination fell to BERT,
its own makers rebuild it: the wrong
answers are generated by a finetuned
language model and kept only where a
discriminator — BERT-Large itself —
cannot tell them from the real endings,
lengthened into the Goldilocks zone
where they are ridiculous to humans and
plausible to models. The rebuilt
examination holds every model below
fifty percent against a human 95.6,
the filter's own victim strongest among
them; and the parent of the country's
shared filter is founded here, a dozen
papers after the country learned the
device from its lightest descendant.
The walk's arithmetic closes on the
rebuilt examination entire — its splits
sum, its overall column is its parts'
mean, its printed twelve is a
derivation — and its one misdescription
is reserved for its own appendix, where
the human task is called the models'
own and given five endings against
their four.

Ninety-sixth walk: the examination is
founded on failure (Paper 078,
Chapter 96). Seven researchers at the
Allen Institute gather grade-school
science questions written for human
tests — months of searching across
states, nations and one dominant
supplier — and run two simple solvers
over them: one that searches, one that
counts co-occurrences. The questions
both miss become the Challenge Set;
the rest, the Easy Set; and the
partition's grade profile matches the
easy half's nearly cell for cell, so
whatever was measured, it was not
difficulty as schools know it. They
ship the questions with a library of
14M science sentences gathered for
them, and the library mentions
knowledge relevant to nearly every
challenge question — and the search
over it scores below chance, because
answers live in chains of sentences
and search returns the one sentence
that looks most like the question.
Every strong baseline of the day sits
the Challenge Set and lands at chance;
the work prints the null result as its
finding, over tables that close
entire. Its slips are small and human:
a contributions list that counts its
neural models as two and then names
three, a footnote whose eleven
missing words are ten, one paper
entered twice in its own bibliography.

Ninety-seventh walk: the loop
learns to hold still (Paper
079, Chapter 97). Prairie,
Novack, Berg-Kirkpatrick and
Fu ask the question twenty
papers of trajectory filings
had not: why do looped models
explode? The answer is a lens
before it is a fix. A looped
forward pass is a dynamical
system over the residual
stream, and its stability is
one number — the spectral norm
of the matrix that carries the
state forward. Addition, the
field's default injection, sits
exactly at the boundary;
concatenation floats free of
it; and the trained models
agree with the theory, the
divergent ones found to have
learned norms above one. The
fix follows the diagnosis:
build the matrix so its
spectrum cannot cross one — a
negative diagonal, discretized
— and the sandwich
normalization the family had
wrapped its loops in can be
dropped. Two inherited
machines are repaired on the
way through: the depth draw,
made per-sequence instead of
per-batch, and the sampler
itself, found to draw from a
compressed image of the law it
names and made faithful. Then,
with a loop that holds still,
the work prices the axis:
recurrence and data grow in
tandem under power laws at
fixed parameters, test-time
depth buys a saturating
approach to a floor that
training set, and one unified
law spans both. The slips are
small and stand recorded: an
abstract claiming a tenth of a
percent more than its own
table recomputes, a range that
matches no scale in its table,
an appendix stating its
backward depth two ways. And
the filing closes the
count: 920 canonical concepts,
the restructuring trigger met
exactly.

Ninety-eighth walk: what jobs can AI
learn? (Paper 080, Chapter 98). The
walk leaves the trajectory country for
the first time in twenty-one papers
and lands in the country it founded
for SciNet — where the second paper is
the instrument the first one borrowed.
Moreira Tomei and Klein Teeselink
score every task in O*NET for its
feasibility as reinforcement-learning
training: a binary physical gate that
zeroes embodied work outright, eight
dimensions at equal weight, an index
of learnability exposure that asks not
whether AI can do a task but whether
the task can be turned into a place
where AI could learn. The book held
the port for forty-three chapters —
three dimensions combined by principal
component, the gate kept politely
separate — and now holds the founding
construction, revising the borrowed
scroll to state it first. The work's
sharpest result is about agreement
itself: its index and the
capability-exposure family agree at
0.912 over all tasks and at 0.379 —
0.005, −0.102 — once the shared zero
block behind the gate is removed; the
headline correlation was the block.
And its public face still wears its
first version's abstract, whose top
occupations the second version
withdrew and whose validation claim
the second version's body nowhere
keeps.

Ninety-ninth walk: the authority
behind the borrowed clause (Paper
081, Chapter 99). The walk stays in
the SciNet country for a third
filing and goes back a generation:
Donald Stokes's 'Pasteur's Quadrant'
(1997), the book Chapter 55's task
dimensions cite in a single clause —
"After Stokes (1997)" — for the one
dimension that asks what the research
a task serves is for. The book's body
sits behind a lending wall, and the
filing is made on what could be held
entire and says so at every joint:
the publisher's description, the
contents, the catalogue record, three
verbatim fragments at pages 2, 24 and
103. What they hold is the framework
entire: two goals of research —
understanding and use — bent from
Bush's single line into two axes,
giving Bohr's cell, Edison's, and the
cell the line could not hold,
Pasteur's, where basic research is
inspired by use; and the proposal the
framework carries, a renewed compact
between science and government. The
field's working form of the model —
four named cells, graded axes — was
completed by its borrowers, the
citing record among them; the book's
own table names three classes and
leaves the fourth cell blank. Its
author died in January 1997 with the
book in progress; it is the walk's
first posthumous filing.

Hundredth walk: the foundation
under the comparison (Paper 082,
Chapter 100). The walk returns to
the representation-theory country
Chapter 54 founded, for the work
that chapter's proof spent: Chan,
Wu, Yu and Zhang's 'Stability of
the smooth Casselman-Jacquet
functor' — cited by Xiao and Yu as
[CWYZ26] for the finite-level
globalization theorem their
comparison chain runs through, and
filed now at its source. The work
builds the smooth Casselman-
Jacquet functors entire: a quotient
and a submodule, both defined with
closure so that every quotient is
Hausdorff by construction; proves
the submodule stable — the
intersection of Jacquet subspaces
does not shrink under one more
application of the nilradical —
by a family of seminorms that
prices depth where this category
has no Artin-Rees to price it with;
proves the canonical map onto the
quotient surjective, where the
algebraic side's map is injective
and completeness is the whole
difference; carries an Artin-Rees
across globalization to win
exactness on the Casselman-Wallach
category; and spends the theory on
its stated application, a full
real Bernstein-Zelevinsky
filtration for smooth Frechet
representations of moderate
growth — the archimedean answer,
forty-nine years on, to the
p-adic filtration of 1977. One of
its four authors co-authored the
citing paper; the debt ran in a
circle, and the walk has now
filed both ends of it.

Hundred-and-first walk: the cited
manuscript, filed (Paper 083, Chapter
101). The walk returns once more to the
representation-theory country, for the
work Chapter 54's founding proof cited
as a manuscript and spent for a direct
proof of its (3.4): Junyan Xiao's
'Equivariant extension of I_N-finite
tempered distributions on real flag
varieties' — posted since the citation
was written, and filed now from the
posted text. The work proves that every
I_N-finite tempered distribution on a
Q-stable Nash open of a real flag
variety extends to the whole variety,
for arbitrary parabolics P and Q, with
the coefficient functor contravariantly
exact: it reduces extension along an
orbit to normal order zero by a normal
presentation; finds the fibre's finite
distributions are exactly polynomial
densities; resolves the orbit closure
and prices the boundary with one
character that vanishes on all of it;
continues the pairing meromorphically,
its bad parameters confined to finitely
many hyperplane families with a single
direction transverse to all of them;
removes the poles by descending
induction on the orbit filtration; and
lifts the whole result from principal
series at the minimal parabolic to every
coefficient module at every parabolic —
spending, for that last step, the
exactness theorem of the functor paper
the walk filed one leg ago. Its author
co-authored the citing paper; its
bibliography cites that paper back. The
triangle the cluster was built on is now
filed at all three corners.

Hundred-and-second walk: the mention
that named a proof (Paper 084, Chapter
102). The queue's rank 53 carried no
title at all — 'Liu et al.', 2021, a
mention mined from Chapter 54's ground.
The held records resolved it entire:
Chapter 54's text holds exactly one
Liu-authored work, its bibliography's
[LLY21], spent in its body for a direct
proof of the comparison theorem by
distributions. The work is Li, Liu &
Yu's 'A proof of Casselman's comparison
theorem' (arXiv:2102.03204v2; Represent.
Theory 25 (2021), 994-1020) — the prior
case Chapter 54's founding concept had
named in a closing clause, now filed at
its source. At the minimal parabolic
the comparison holds with no completion
taken, proved by tempered distributions,
two filtrations, and a functor that
takes the locally nilpotent part; beside
it stands a closedness theorem that
removes the closure bar from Casselman's
automatic continuity. The proof's
machinery files as seven concepts
(1.2.947-1.2.953); no held concept is
revised — the ancestors file beside
their descendants, linked, not merged.
The same work stands queued a second
time at rank 55, under its bibliography
key; when the walk reaches it, it will
resolve as this filing's duplicate.
Cluster AR stands at four papers.

Hundred-and-third walk: the homology
the comparison stood on (Paper 085,
Chapter 103). The queue's rank 54 was a
bibliography record — a title and two
initials, mined from Chapter 54's
ground. The held records named it:
Chen & Sun's 'Schwartz homologies of
representations of almost linear Nash
groups' (arXiv:1901.00730v2; J. Funct.
Anal. 280 (2021), Paper No. 108817) —
the work Chapter 54's body spends once,
for Borel's lemma beneath its orbit
filtration, and whose own longest proof
runs on the same lemma. The filing
holds the cluster's homological
substrate at its source: Schwartz
homology as the derived coinvariants
of the moderate-growth category, the
identity that starts it, the Shapiro
lemma that computes it, the automatic
extensions that spend it — and, in the
version of record, a correction: two
of its results were wrong in print for
five years, and the reader who caught
them, thanked in its acknowledgements,
is the citing chapter's own co-author.
The theory files as eight concepts
(1.2.954-1.2.961); no held concept is
revised. The concept ledger reaches
961, across Pass #44's 960 line.
Cluster AR stands at five papers.

Hundred-and-fourth walk: the
orbitwise anatomy (Paper 086, Chapter
104). The queue's rank 56 was a work
record mined from Chapter 54's
bibliography — 'N. Abe', a title
carrying extraction noise, no arXiv
form to find. The held records named
it: Noriyuki Abe's 'Generalized
Jacquet modules of parabolically
induced representations', Publ. Res.
Inst. Math. Sci. 48 (2012), 419-473 —
the work Chapter 54 cites as [Abe12]
and Paper 083's chapter spends as its
first reference, the Bruhat-filtration
study whose Proposition 4.4 and
Lemmas 4.5-4.6 its pole removal
follows. The filing holds the
cluster's orbitwise anatomy at its
source: the generalized Jacquet
modules, the filtration by support,
the polynomial densities on each cell
valued in the Levi side's own Jacquet
modules, the continuation and pole
removal that reach them, the
criterion that prices them, the
twisting functor that names their
algebraic form, the transport to the
K-finite dual, and the Whittaker
counts that close the description —
with the appendix's local
characterization beneath them all.
The theory files as twelve concepts
(1.2.962-1.2.973); no held concept is
revised. The concept ledger reaches
973. Cluster AR stands at six papers.

Hundred-and-fifth walk: the
substrate (Paper 087, Chapter 105).
The queue's rank 57 was a work record
mined from Chapter 54's bibliography
— 'A. Aizenbud, D. Gourevitch', a
