Hundred-and-sixth walk: the
globalization theory (Paper 088,
Chapter 106). The queue's rank 58 was
a work record mined from Chapter 54's
bibliography — 'D. A. Vogan', a title
carrying extraction noise, its LNM
form standing in the citing chapter's
own list and as Paper 084's nineteenth
reference. The held records named it:
David A. Vogan Jr.'s 'Unitary
representations and complex analysis',
in Representation Theory and Complex
Analysis, Lecture Notes in Math. 1931
(2008), pp. 259-344 — the work Chapter
54 spends as [Vog08] for the broader
comparison problem, at its Conjecture
10.3, the conjecture Q180 stands open
on. The filing holds the cluster's
theory of completions at its source:
the four canonical globalizations and
the unitarity problem they serve, the
Casselman-Wallach canonicity of the
norms, the sequence-space forms of the
globalizations, induction in the
compact picture, the measurable flag
varieties, the maximal Hausdorff
quotient, cohomological induction in
its maximal and minimal forms, the
dominance transfer theorem, Serre
duality for Dolbeault cohomology, and
invariant Hermitian forms read as
cohomology classes on the product with
the opposite manifold. The theory
files as twelve concepts
(1.2.985-1.2.996); no held concept is
revised. The concept ledger reaches
996. Cluster AR stands at eight
papers.

Hundred-and-seventh walk: the
Bruhat filtration at its source
(Paper 089, Chapter 107). The
queue's rank 59 was a work record
mined from Chapter 54's bibliography
— 'W. Casselman, H. Hecht, D.
Milicic', a title carrying the
