Hundred-and-twentieth walk: a Will-posted paper, no queue rank — Hongcan Guo and ten co-authors' 'Continuous Latent Diffusion Language Model' (arXiv:2605.06548), a hierarchical latent diffusion language model whose diffusion path transports a prior over a learned semantic latent instead of recovering a corrupted text: the Text VAE that stabilizes the latent; the block-causal flow prior over it; the ELBO read as reconstruction minus information minus prior matching; the total statistical burden that prices the model against autoregression; the three curves that bound where the construction can win; the likelihood that comes apart from generation quality; the latent space that must evolve with its prior; the timeshift that drifts with dimension; the clean condition that beats repaint; and compression that fails at odd boundaries, not at compression. Thirteen concepts (1.2.1107-1.2.1119), no foundation, five questions (Q462-Q466), two machines; the concept ledger reaches 1,119 — one short of the 1,120 line Restructuring Pass #52 set, which is NOT crossed. Cluster AV stands at five papers.

