Paper 027 — "Topological Properties of Cones with
  Small Entropy" (Doan), arXiv:2611.24863 [math.DG],
  submitted 18 November 2026. Lam Doan, of the
  Department of Mathematics, Johns Hopkins
  University. The full text in its HTML form, read
  entire: a regular cone of Colding-Minicozzi
  entropy within epsilon(n) of 1 has a spherical
  link, and the space of such links retracts onto
  the equatorial spheres with vanishing relative
  homotopy — proved through the cone's unique
  self-expander: Ding existence, Yao uniqueness,
  White regularity with Guo's sharpening, the
  Bernstein-Wang compactness, entropy coincidence,
  asymptotic graphicality and trace theory, and the
  strict convexity of the squared distance on the
  expander. Taken in 2026-11-19 as Paper 027 of the
