Paper 029 — "Data Just Wants to Be
Format-Neutral" (Pemberton), Proc. XML Prague
2016, Prague, pp. 109-120, ISBN
978-80-906259-0-7; the full text as posted on
the author's page at CWI, read entire. Steven
Pemberton, of CWI, Amsterdam. Invisible XML:
any parsable format treated as XML by parsing
with a grammar and serialising the parse
tree, keeping the marked nodes;
round-tripping semantically identical but not
character-identical where elided material is
unrecorded; Earley parsing as a serialised
parallel processor; representation neutrality
— representations with the same parse tree
are equivalent; the normalised grammar as a
data schema (unions, structs, lists); subset
of normalised grammars with the same root as
one-way compatibility; conversion by parsing
with one grammar and serialising with
another. Taken in 2026-11-19 as Paper 029, a
paper Will posted in the MOAT chat, outside
the test of the skim fixed in advance (the
strata of the sample complete: Will's posts
at Paper 027, the scan's picks at Paper 028):
10 new canonical concepts (1.2.395-1.2.404,
cluster AK founded), 3 new foundations
(1.3.318-1.3.320), 1 defined word coined
(1.3.321: refinement), 0 canonical scrolls
revised, 0 stated again. Restructure Pass #20
fell in this taking-in (the count at 404,
over the 400 line). Chapter:
1.1.1/1.1.1/46.1.x (synthesis at 46.2.x)

Paper 030 — "The Minimal Background Period
for Infinitely Many Spectral Gaps in
Anderson-Bernoulli Models" (Chen & Li),
arXiv:2611.22703v1 [math.SP], submitted 17
November 2026, read entire in HTML form. Cong
Chen, of Jilin University, and Yong Li. The
least background period for infinitely many
bounded gaps is 3; the explicit period-three
model and its stability; the eight three-step
blocks; the transverse heteroclinic
connection and its Wronskian slope; the
interval towers and the strict window; the
multicone; the common spectrum; exclusion by
uniform hyperbolicity; trace zeros of
periodic words; exact rational verification,
its final comparisons re-run by the house.
Taken in 2026-11-20 as Paper 030, a pick of
