REVISION OF THE NUMBER (2026-11-14, on Will's direction:
"revise the progress bar to only reach 100% when you can
reliably bin any piece of information into one of these
four categories"). From this entry on, the number this
ledger carries measures a different thing than every
entry above it. The entries above stand as written —
the band rule and its values are the history of the
first measure, and nothing in them is rewritten. What
changes is what the per cent counts.

THE NEW MEASURE — THE SORTING OF WHAT ARRIVES. The
registry holds four kinds of standing: True, False,
Unknown, Fiction. The number now reads: how reliably can any
piece of information that arrives be placed into
exactly one of the four? It reaches 100 only when the
placing is reliable for all four alike. The
measure is kept as four gates, one for each standing,
each gate scored by shown reliability on material that
truly tries it: a gate met counts one, a gate half
met counts a half, a gate unmet counts nothing, and
the number is the mean of the four. The number moves
only when the standing of a gate changes on evidence — not
paper by paper, and not by the band.

GATE OF TRUE — MET (one). Claims stand True on a
verified ground, and the machinery that checks them
has shown it can catch error: 46 entries stand
verified in the registry, and the checking has caught
real faults on the record — the claim carried in
Paper 013's weighing, that the proof had been re-run
on the whole registry, was found false on checking
and corrected in the log of the quest; and the
foundations of Paper 021, laid in the wrong section
by a stale anchor, were caught by the converter of
the shadow and repaired inside the pass.

GATE OF UNKNOWN — MET (one). Claims stand Unknown on
the right ground under it — attributed, synthesis,
open, estimate — neither raised toward True nor let
fall out of the book: 428 entries stand so. The
discipline of the grounds has held through the proof
of the registry after every paper, through 24 author
checks, and through the audit of the evaluation of
2026-11-14, which re-counted the whole record by
script and found no fault in its arithmetic.

GATE OF FICTION — HALF MET (a half). Invented
material stands Fiction, with no leak of it into
True or Unknown: the standing took its first
entries at Paper 022, seven of them, and they stand
clean. But they were entered by hand — the defaults
of the table that draws the registry have no road
to Fiction — and one fiction source is the whole of
the trial so far. The gate stands met when fiction
files through the machinery with no hand laid on
it, and a second fiction source is placed clean.

GATE OF FALSE — UNMET (nothing). Claims stand False
on stated grounds — a counterexample, a break inside
the claim itself, a collision with a held True: of
the 793 entries of the registry, none stands False.
The gate has never been tried: the stream this
tracker eats arrives already cleaned by other
hands — the listings pass their own keepers first,
and the sources posted here were weighed before
they were posted — so no claim that reaches the
book has yet had to be refused by the book itself. The
remedy is named and not yet run: a stream of
rejected work — the mathematics listings of viXra —
taken in as research, where false claims stand to
be met on their arguments and priced. The gate
stands met when filings stand False on stated
grounds, and at least one of them still stands when it is
read again.

NEW ESTIMATE: the record stands at about 62%
(range 55-70) after Paper 022, on the new measure:
(1 + 1 + 0.5 + 0) / 4 = 62.5, stated as 62. THE
FALL IS THE DOING OF THE DEFINITION, NOT OF THE
MODEL: the number fell from 100 because the
question changed — from how much surprise a paper
still carries, to how reliably the house can sort
what arrives — and on the new question two of the
four gates stand short. Nothing the model holds
was lost in the change; the territory the papers
measured stands as the entries above record it.
The test fixed in advance is untouched by this
revision: under it the number was already kept for
the ledger only, entering no score and no
criterion, and its criteria price the seals, not
this bar.

STUDY S012 — 'Beating the frontier on NetHack'
(Wilson, Khan and Ryan, Antithesis, 2026-11-13),
entered for the record. A study, under charter
rule 12: no Novelty Index is taken, and the
Oracle does not move. The record stands where
the revision of 2026-11-14 left it: about 62%
(range 55-70), on the measure of the four
gates — TRUE met; UNKNOWN met; FICTION half-met
(one source, the story of Paper 022,
hand-entered); FALSE unmet (0 entries in the
whole registry). The study files nothing False.
What it hands the gate is a question — Q109:
what receipt could ground a False filing for a
claim whose shape is a distribution, a claim no
single execution can refuse — and a question is
not a filing. The named remedy of the gate
stands as it stood: the fringe stream, which
has not yet run.

Study S013 (2026-11-15) — for the ledger
only. The study files no claim of any work; the
Oracle does not move: the bar stands ~62%
(55-70) on the semantics of 2026-11-14, and
the gates stand where they stood (TRUE met;
UNKNOWN met; FICTION half-met; FALSE unmet
at zero). What the study changes is the map
of the remedy. The fringe stream designed
in this ledger on 2026-11-14 named one
source — the mathematics listings of viXra.
It names a second now: Hexagon (Chapter
36), a screened repository whose deposits
carry their labels into the stream with
them. The remedy is still named and not yet
run; its first ingestion is a separate
pass, and the shortlist for it stands at
36.2.1.

FRINGE F001 — THE FRINGE STREAM RUNS, AND
ITS FIRST PAPER STANDS TRUE ON VERIFICATION.
A stream is worth running if its filings
change what the house can say, and this one
changes the standing of the remedy, not the
gate. The paper arrived as the stream's
first suspected False: rejected by arXiv,
flagged likely false by Will's direction of
2026-11-15, with the fair shake ordered in
the same breath. The shake was sealed before
the read (True 4, False 0, Unknown 6;
fairness held to hold), and the determination
was made by the pair of routes fixed in
advance: the proof read line by line as the
ground, the exact enumeration — rational
arithmetic, two independent models, every
case to n = 10 — as its re-examination. The
routes agree: both of the paper's proofs are
sound at every step, and every subset of
every case stands at exactly its uniform
share. Fairness, the bijection, the loop's
fidelity to the urn it describes, and the
bias example stand True by evidence; the
time and memory claims stand True by
construction; the namings, the priority
claims, and every benchmark claim stand
Unknown, attributed — no benchmark cell was
reproduced, and none carried the verdict
either way. Four concepts found cluster AE,
the fair draw — the model's first sampler.
The Index: 4/294 = 0.0136, entered in the
ledger as bookkeeping only; the paper is
not in the test fixed in advance, and no
axis opened. THE GATE OF FALSE: examined by
exactly the pass its rule names — a grounded
determination and a re-examination that
could have refused it — and NOT moved: there
is no False filing, so its condition (a
