degree (Lemma 2.37), the lemma
Paper 084 spends in its
introduction as 'a theorem of
Hecht-Schmid'. The held scroll is
Paper 084's construction, following
Abe: the locally nilpotent part
U^[n'] of a U(n')-module U itself —
not of a dual — with Lemma 3.1's
equivalent form (annihilation by a
power of the augmentation kernel)
and Lemma 3.2's tensor behaviour,
and with the functor's standing
reversed: left exact, and not
right exact in general, its
exactness on the Bruhat sequences
a theorem the work proves by
