- Pass #47 (2026-11-25; standalone
pass — no taking-in; concept-count
trigger — 1,007 canonical concepts
cross the 1000 line set by Pass #46,
crossed at Paper 089's filing):
merges weighed, five, and held apart,
each on its record.
(i) 1.2.998, the transversal degree
filtration of T(Y, E), into 1.2.952,
the transversal degree filtration and
the Bruhat filtration of I(sigma) —
the nearest pair this pass has
weighed: one construction standing at
two grains, the held scroll's own
text naming the newer work as the one
it reviews and refines
(Casselman-Hecht-Milicic, its
reference [8]). Held apart. The newer
scroll defines T(Y, E) for a general
closed subanalytic submanifold Y of
an ambient manifold X, on a
subanalytic neighbourhood of Y and
independently of the choice (Lemmas
2.5-2.6); its filtration F_p is the
annihilator of the sections flat to
order p+1 along Y; its model case is
exact — for Y = {x_n = 0} in R^n,
F_p T(Y) is {T : x_n^{p+1} T = 0},
and T(Y) is the direct sum over i of
the i-th normal derivatives of
F_0 T(Y) — and each step is a
filtered right module over the ring
Diff(E) of E-valued differential
operators, for a general locally
convex E (Lemma 2.10). The held
scroll stands on one Bruhat cell:
its graded form is algebraic (Lemma
2.5), Gr^p T(C(w), E(sigma))
isomorphic as a U(p)-module to
L_p(w) tensor over R(C(w)) of
S(C(w), E(sigma))' — the same graded
shape the newer work states at its
own Lemma 4.3, filed at 1.2.1001 —
and above the cells it carries the
Bruhat filtration of I(sigma) itself
(Lemma 2.1), which in the newer work
is filed at 1.2.999 and 1.2.1000, not
here. And the held scroll holds the
two refinements of [8] it states as
its own work: the stratification
ordered one cell at a time by
dimension, where [8]'s was coarser,
and the coefficient module V_sigma
allowed a nontrivial N-action, where
[8] assumed it trivial — claims about
the difference between the two
works, which neither scroll can hold
for the other. Filing the general
machine inside the cell refinement
would lose the model case, the
neighbourhood independence and the
Diff(E)-module; filing the refinement
inside the machine would lose the
refinements themselves and the
descent the comparison (1.2.947) is
proved by.
(ii) 1.2.1000, the Bruhat filtration
of the smooth principal series, into
1.2.505, the smooth Bruhat filtration
(J_a) and its quotients: the founding
form arriving fifty-three chapters
after its descendant — the newer
scroll names the descent itself:
'This is the founding form of the
Bruhat filtration: the smooth Bruhat
filtration (J_a) of Paper 036
(1.2.505)'. Held apart. The held
filtration runs on J = Ind_P^G sigma,
its steps the sections flat along
the closed unions of Q-orbits, and
its quotients carry Corollary 1.5's
closedness package — closed (co)chain
differentials, Casselman-Wallach
homology, u^k M closed in M for every
k >= 1 — the analytic content the
comparison theorem (1.2.495) spends,
bought by that theorem and standing
nowhere in the newer work. The newer
filtration runs at a minimal
parabolic, its steps closed
G-submodules of Ind^infty(sigma), and
Theorem 4.1 computes its graded
module entire: the direct sum over p
and over the cells of Bruhat length p
of J(w, sigma), the duals of the
tempered distributions supported on
the cells, with their transversal-
degree filtrations — a graded
computation the held scroll never
makes: its quotients carry quotient
topologies and homology, not
distribution duals. Filing the
founding form inside the descendant
would lose the graded computation;
filing the descendant inside the
founding form would lose the
closedness package the whole
comparison cluster spends.
(iii) 1.2.999, the stratification
filtration and its graded object,
into 1.2.963, the Bruhat filtration
by support: one Bruhat shape standing
on the two sides of the duality —
sections against distributions. Held
apart. The newer scroll is a general
machine: a manifold X under a finite
stratification by locally closed
subanalytic submanifolds, C_p^infty(E)
the smooth sections flat on the
unions Z_p of the strata of smaller
dimension, and Theorem 3.1 computes
its graded object entire — the direct
sum over p of the duals of the spaces
T(Z_p - Z_{p-1}, E), the tempered
distributions supported on the open
stratum piece, with the transversal-
degree filtration on each; Theorem
3.4 is its orbit form, and Lemma 3.5
adds that under a compact group of
symmetries the transversal pieces are
invariant subspaces. The held
filtration lives inside one induced
representation: its steps are the
distributions of I(sigma, lambda)
supported on the closed unions of
Bruhat cells, isolated one cell at a
time by the restrictions Res_i, and
its quotients are not duals of
anything — they are the cell's own
contribution, identified with the
orbitwise model (1.2.964) when the
nonvanishing criterion (1.2.967)
prices them. The newer scroll's
graded pieces are duals by
construction; the held scroll's
quotients are submodules by
construction. Filing the machine
inside the representation would lose
the general stratification theorem
and the symmetry lemma; filing the
representation's filtration inside
the machine would lose the model
identification the whole of Paper
086's description hangs on.
(iv) 1.2.1001, the graded pieces over
a Bruhat cell, into 1.2.964, the
orbitwise model: two computations of
what one cell contributes, in two
theories. Held apart. The newer
scroll factorizes the cell's own
distribution space: T(C(w), E) =
T(N cap U^w) tensor E_w^*, the cell's
distributions against the dual fibre
(Lemma 4.2); its transversal graded
piece is L_p(w) tensor over R(C(w))
of S(C(w))' tensor E_w^* (Lemma
4.3), where L_p(w) is the space of
polynomial densities of transversal
degree p along the cell; and L_p(w)
itself carries a finite filtration,
N-equivariant, whose graded pieces
are copies of R(C(w)) (Lemma 4.4) —
the cell's contribution built,
finitely many layers deep, from the
cell's own function ring and its
Schwartz dual, its coefficients the
fixed fibre E_w. The held scroll's
model is representation-theoretic:
I_i^0 is the image under the normal-
derivative operator E of the
polynomial densities on the cell
valued in the Levi side's own
generalized Jacquet module at the
twisted character, J^{w_i^{-1} eta}_0
of sigma tensor e^{lambda+rho},
spread over the cell by delta_i; and
it carries Lemma 2.9's containment —
the restriction Res_i of every
element of I_i lies inside the model —
with exhaustion reserved to Theorem
4.7 (1.2.967), a claim about the
induced representation that the newer
scroll, which computes a graded
module and stops, nowhere makes.
Filing the factorization inside the
model would lose the function-ring
layers; filing the model inside the
factorization would lose the
Jacquet-module values and the
containment.
(v) 1.2.985, the four canonical
globalizations, into 1.2.500, the
smooth completion (-)^infinity —
Casselman-Wallach globalization: the
five-term chain against its middle
link. Held apart. The held scroll is
one functor: for a Harish-Chandra
module W, W^infinity is its
Casselman-Wallach globalization, the
unique Casselman-Wallach
representation (1.2.496) whose
K-finite vectors are W, guaranteed by
the Casselman-Wallach globalization
theorem — and in Paper 036 the
functor is spent on homology, the
hinge of the comparison (1.2.495) and
of its Tor and Ext forms (1.2.501,
1.2.502). The newer scroll is the
chain entire — the minimal
globalization V^omega, the smooth
V^infty, a Hilbert globalization, the
distribution globalization V^-infty,
the maximal V^-omega — each
depending only on the infinitesimal
equivalence class of V_K, never on
the Hilbert space chosen to build it;
and its load-bearing clause stands at
the chain's ends: an invariant
Hermitian form on V_K extends
uniquely to continuous forms on
V^omega and on V^infty, and, unless
V_K is finite-dimensional, admits no
continuous extension to V^-infty or
to V^-omega — Theorem 1.5's last
clause, proved as Theorem 9.16 and
filed at 1.2.996, the fact the
unitarity problem (1.2.986) is
organized around, standing nowhere in
the held scroll. That the chain is
canonical at all is a further claim,
filed at its own scroll (the norm
canonicity, 1.2.987). Filing the
chain inside the functor would lose
the two ends and the forms clause;
filing the functor inside the chain
would lose the uniqueness theorem in
the exact form the comparison spends
it.
Splits: none — no concept of the
twenty-three (1.2.985-1.2.1007)
carries two claims that pull apart;
the compound ones hold one claim
each — 1.2.985's chain and its forms
clause are Theorem 1.5's one
statement, the frame and its engine
in a single scroll; 1.2.992's maximal
form and 1.2.995's minimal form of
cohomological induction are a dual
pair joined by Serre duality
(1.2.994), two constructions, not one
claim in two seats; 1.2.999's
stratification filtration and its
orbit form (Theorem 3.4) are one
machine and its specialization, the
specialization to the flag variety
itself filed at 1.2.1000; 1.2.1003's
dual vanishing and its one-
dimensional Whittaker homology are
one theorem's two clauses, the
nonvanishing stated exactly where
the vanishing stops (Theorem 5.12
with Proposition 5.13). The split of
1.2.884, declined at Passes #43, #44,
#45 and #46, was re-weighed and
stands declined: the filter's text
has not changed since Paper 077 and
nothing in Papers 088-089 touches it
— no new evidence reopens it.
Retired: none. The standoff
companions at 1.5.4 stand at 106.
State machines stand at 346 (309
stated, 37 inferred), unchanged — no
taking-in. Registry entries 2,297
before and after; the pass's trace is
this record and the path entry at
1.5.5. Next
restructuring pass due at Paper 115
or 1020 canonical concepts.
- Pass #46 (2026-11-25; standalone
pass — no taking-in; concept-count
trigger — 984 canonical concepts cross
the 980 line set by Pass #45, crossed
at Paper 087's filing): merges
weighed, five, and held apart, each on
its record.
(i) 1.2.962, the generalized Jacquet
modules, into 1.2.949, the
Casselman-Jacquet module (the locally
nilpotent part) — the nearest pair
this pass has weighed: one name in
two seats. Held apart. The newer
scroll's spaces live inside the duals
— J^eta_0(V) in the continuous dual
V', J^eta_*(V) in the algebraic dual
of the K-finite part — as generalized
eigenvectors for a character eta of
n_0: (X - eta(X))^k x = 0; and at
eta = 0 the Frechet variant is
Casselman's Jacquet module J*(V)
itself, by Wallach's automatic
continuity — a quotient-side object
reached through the dual. The held
scroll selects within a module
itself: U^[n'] = {v : n'^k v = 0},
untwisted, an algebraic subobject
with its tensor behaviour (Lemma
3.2), left exact and not right exact
in general — and the object the
orbit comparison (1.2.508) spends
under the notation D^[u] without
pausing to define. The book itself
keeps the two apart by a theorem:
the dual transport (1.2.970)
identifies the newer scroll's second
variant as the held construction
carried across duality, Gamma_eta of
J(V)* — a transport proved, not a
definition shared. Filing the dual
eigenvectors inside the subobject
would lose the character, the two
duals and the Wallach identification;
filing the subobject inside them
would lose the tensor lemma and the
spend.
(ii) 1.2.963, the Bruhat filtration
by support, into 1.2.505, the smooth
Bruhat filtration: the newer scroll
names the kinship itself — the
distribution-valued sibling of the
held filtration, the same Bruhat
order run on the induced
representation itself. Held apart.
The held filtration's steps are
smooth sections flat along the closed
unions Z_j — vanishing with all
derivatives — closed (q, L)-submodules
whose quotients carry Corollary 1.5's
closedness package: closed
differentials, Casselman-Wallach
homology, u^k M closed in M. The
newer filtration's steps are
distributions supported on the closed
unions, inside I(sigma, lambda)
itself; its quotients are not
homology carriers but the orbitwise
model spaces (1.2.964), priced by the
nonvanishing criterion (1.2.967) and
identified with twisted inductions
(1.2.969). Flatness against support:
dual conditions on dual objects. A
third standing of the shape, the
filtration of 1.2.508 on the dual J',
feeds the generalized-invariant
comparison, not the Jacquet-module
description — three filtrations,
three outputs.
(iii) 1.2.966, the deformation and
pole removal, into 1.2.945, pole
removal along the orbit filtration:
the source arriving after the move it
taught — the held scroll's own text
states that it follows Abe's Lemmas
4.5-4.6 for minimal Q into the
general case. Held apart. The held
scroll deforms along lambda_0 +
tau nu_0, with nu_0 = dDelta_0, one
direction transverse to every bad
hyperplane at once — bought by the
comparison factor (1.2.942),
machinery the newer scroll does not
have; its Laurent coefficients are
I_N-finite tempered distributions
supported on the union of strictly
smaller orbits, already extended by
the induction hypothesis of an
extension theorem, and the output is
existence at the bad parameter, with
no pairing there (Q371). The newer
scroll deforms along lambda + t rho
at a minimal parabolic; its
coefficients lie one Bruhat step
down, in I_{i-1}(lambda); the
deformation respects the equations —
Ex = 0 implies Ex_t = 0 — and its
holomorphicity at t = 0 is bought
under the criterion's three
conditions (1.2.967). Same move,
different filtrations, different
transverse directions, different
theorems bought.
(iv) 1.2.983, the filtration of
supported generalized sections, into
1.2.959, Borel's lemma for Schwartz
sections: one Borel lemma standing
on the theory's two sides — and the
held scroll names its source,
'after Aizenbud-Gourevitch'. Held
apart. The held scroll filters the
quotient of the Schwartz sections by
extension by zero, by order of
vanishing along Z: its exhaustivity
is an inverse-limit isomorphism
(Proposition 8.2), and its graded
pieces are Schwartz sections over Z
of the symmetric powers of the
conormal bundle (Proposition 8.3),
for a general closed Z by
stratification; it is the piece
Paper 036's Section 3 spends for its
orbit filtration's exhaustivity. The
newer scroll filters the supported
generalized sections by transversal
degree: its Lemma 5.5.3 is a
surjectivity — the i-th transversal
derivative maps onto the Schwartz
sections of S^i(CN) — a claim the
held scroll nowhere makes; and its
graded pieces are generalized
sections on Z twisted by the density
bundles D_M|_Z and D_Z*, where the
held scroll's carry no density twist;
it is the exact pair Chapter 54
spends (Lemma 5.5.3 and Corollary
5.5.4). Two citing chains, two sides
of one duality: filing the dual side
inside the section side would
collapse the chain the book exists
to track.
(v) 1.2.973, the polynomial-density
characterization, into 1.2.951, the
regular-density form of the cell's
Jacquet module: the
annihilation-to-density identity in
two regimes — the shape Pass #45
weighed as its (iv), standing here
with its third sibling (1.2.941).
Held apart. The held scroll: on the
nilpotent homogeneous space N/U, a
distribution killed by n^k, untwisted,
is a regular function of bounded
degree times the invariant density —
polynomial and regular function
coinciding there — the general
coefficients reached by a composition
series; it is the bottom of Paper
084's proof, the identity the
exactness of 1.2.950 computes from
and the scalar comparison (1.2.953)
is stated about. The newer scroll:
on a general connected nilpotent Lie
group N, with a character eta, a
tempered L-distribution annihilated
by some power (Ker eta)^k is a
polynomial density, (P(N) eta^{-1}
tensor V') delta, valued in an
arbitrary Frechet dual V' — and its
Corollary A.5 adds the descent,
membership in D^0(U, L) inherited
through the annihilation, a claim
the held scroll nowhere makes. Its
work is to be the local fact under
the orbitwise model (1.2.964), at the
generality the cells need. Different
groups — N against N/U — twisted
against untwisted annihilation,
polynomials against regular
functions, and a descent corollary
standing on one side only.
Splits: none — no concept of the
twenty-three (1.2.962-1.2.984)
carries two claims that pull apart;
the compound ones hold one claim
each — 1.2.962's two variants are one
condition standing in two duals
(Remark 2.2: the condition is one
condition), and their theories'
divergence is carried by the dual
transport (1.2.970), not hidden
inside the definition; 1.2.974's
affine and glued definitions are two
constructions of one space;
1.2.980's two flabbiness statements
are consequences drawn at once from
the characterization, not a second
claim; 1.2.983's lemma and corollary
are one devissage — the derivatives'
surjectivity and the filtration it
stratifies. The split of 1.2.884,
declined at Passes #43, #44 and #45,
was re-weighed and stands declined:
the filter's text has not changed
since Paper 077 and nothing in
Papers 086-087 touches it — no new
evidence reopens it. Retired: none.
The standoff companions at 1.5.4
stand at 104. State machines stand
at 335 (298 stated, 37 inferred),
unchanged — no taking-in. Registry
entries 2,256 before and after; the
pass's trace is this record and the
path entry at 1.5.5. Next
restructuring pass due at Paper 110
or 1000 canonical concepts.
- Pass #45 (2026-11-25; standalone
pass — no taking-in; concept-count
trigger — 961 canonical concepts cross
the 960 line set by Pass #44, crossed
at Paper 085's filing): merges
weighed, five, and held apart, each on
its record.
(i) 1.2.947, Casselman's comparison
theorem at the minimal parabolic, into
1.2.495, Casselman's comparison
theorem: the newer scroll names the
relation itself — the
minimal-parabolic case of the
comparison the book already holds, the
case the held scroll's own closing
clause names as the field's prior held
result (Hecht-Taylor; Li-Liu-Yu),
filed at its source five years before
the general case. A special case
proved first is not the theorem that
later generalizes it. Held apart in
both directions. The held scroll
quantifies over every standard
parabolic Q of a real linear reductive
group, and buys as part of the theorem
that every differential of the
Chevalley-Eilenberg complex has closed
image and the homology is a
Casselman-Wallach representation of L
— conclusions the minimal case nowhere
states. The newer scroll states the
homology and cohomology forms
together, with no completion taken on
either side, and carries its own proof
spine — duality, Hecht-Taylor's
reduction, the two-filtration descent
of 1.2.952 — run on distribution
theory alone, none of the D-module
machinery of the minimal-globalization
proofs. Filing the prior case inside
its generalization would bury which
proof the field held, and for how
long, inside the theorem that
superseded it.
(ii) 1.2.948, the closedness theorem
(n^k V is closed), into 1.2.504,
closedness of u^k M in the (co)chain
spaces — the nearest pair this pass
has weighed: one theorem-shape, the
unclosed span already closed, standing
in two loci. Held apart. The held
scroll's subspaces live inside the
Chevalley-Eilenberg chain and cochain
spaces at a general parabolic, proved
closed as kernels of continuous maps
into a Hausdorff H_0, through the
finite-dimensional-coefficient
comparison; their work is to make the
quotient topologies on homology
Hausdorff, the analytic content behind
the comparison. The newer scroll's
subspace n^k V lives inside the
representation itself, at the minimal
parabolic, proved closed by finite
codimension from 1.2.947 — and it is
the removal of Casselman's closure
bar, the form the automatic continuity
theorem always wanted; its corollary
carries the closedness into the Koszul
complexes of V, not the
Chevalley-Eilenberg complex of the
held scroll. Same shape, different
spaces, different mechanisms,
different theorems bought. The filing
filed them apart on this ground; the
pass confirms the filing.
(iii) 1.2.949, the Casselman-Jacquet
module (the locally nilpotent part),
into 1.2.507, the Casselman-Jacquet
functor: one name, two directions of
construction. Held apart. The held
scroll's functors divide out — CJ_U(V)
the u-adic completion of a
Harish-Chandra module, its smooth form
the inverse limit over the closures —
and Paper 036's comparison chain runs
through the quotient. The newer scroll
divides nothing out: it selects
within, the part of a U(n')-module the
nilradical already kills at finite
order, an algebraic subobject with no
topology and no closure, left exact
and not right exact in general — and
it is the object the orbit comparison
(1.2.508) spends under the notation
D^[u] without pausing to define.
Filing the part inside the quotient
would blur the direction on which the
cluster's exactness questions turn:
1.2.950's exactness is proved for the
selecting functor, 1.2.934's
surjectivity for the dividing one.
(iv) 1.2.951, the regular-density form
of the cell's Jacquet module, into
1.2.941, polynomial densities on the
fibre: the density identity in two
settings — on both sides, the finite
distributions are exactly the regular
densities. Held apart. The newer
scroll characterizes the locally
nilpotent part (1.2.949) of the
tempered distributions on a Bruhat
cell: on the nilpotent homogeneous
space N/U a distribution killed by n^k
is a regular function of bounded
degree times the invariant density,
polynomial and regular function
coinciding there, the general
coefficients reached by a composition
series of the coefficient module; it
is the bottom of Paper 084's proof,
the identity the scalar comparison
(1.2.953) is stated about. The held
scroll characterizes the I_N-finite
vectors along the fibre of a Q-orbit
bundle: polynomials of degree bounded
by k against the invariant density, a
finite-dimensional space, the general
coefficients carried by a base
distribution tensored with the fibre
density; its work is to leave finitely
many scalar integrals for the
continuation (1.2.943). Different
finiteness — annihilation by a power
of n against finiteness under the
group action — different spaces,
different proofs downstream.
(v) 1.2.960, the automatic extension
theorems, into 1.2.939, the
equivariant extension theorem: the
extension shape in two theories — the
newer scroll names the kinship itself,
extension across a stable open, priced
at the boundary. Held apart. The held
scroll extends the distributions
themselves: restriction from the flag
variety to a Q-stable Nash open is
surjective on I_N-finite tempered
distributions, with contravariant
exactness in the Casselman-Wallach
coefficients, proved by the normal
presentation and the Mellin
continuation. The newer scroll extends
homology: the boundary quotient's
Schwartz homology vanishes under
stabilizer-homology conditions,
extension by zero is injective one
degree down and a surjective open map
in its own degree — openness by the
work's own lemma — and the finite-rank
form runs through the vanishing
criterion (1.2.961). One prices the
boundary in the objects, the other in
their homology; a vanishing theorem
about a boundary quotient is not the
surjectivity that extends a
distribution.
Splits: none — no concept of the
fifteen (1.2.947-1.2.961) carries two
claims that pull apart; the compound
ones hold one claim each — 1.2.952's
two filtrations (Bruhat across cells,
transversal within a cell) are one
descent, the machine the comparison of
1.2.947 is proved by; 1.2.954's two
identifications (Theorems 1.8 and 7.7)
are the one theory's placement against
its neighbours, not a second claim;
1.2.956's relative projectivity is the
category's homological engine, the
package its Theorem 5.9 closes;
1.2.960's three theorems are one shape
at three strengths — engine, extension
reading, finite-rank form. The split
of 1.2.884, declined at Passes #43 and
#44, was re-weighed and stands
declined: the filter's text has not
changed since Paper 077 and nothing in
Papers 084-085 touches it — no new
evidence reopens it. Retired: none.
The standoff companions at 1.5.4 stand
at 102. State machines stand at 324
(287 stated, 37 inferred), unchanged —
no taking-in. Registry entries 2,215
before and after; the pass's trace is
this record and the path entry at
1.5.5. Next restructuring pass due at
Paper 105 or 980 canonical concepts.
- Pass #44 (2026-11-25;
standalone pass — no taking-in;
concept-count trigger — 946
canonical concepts cross the 940
line set by Pass #43, crossed at
Paper 083's filing): merges
weighed, five, and held apart,
each on its record.
(i) 1.2.931, the smooth
Casselman-Jacquet functors, into
1.2.507, the Casselman-Jacquet
functor: the newer scroll names
the relation itself — the pair
generalizes the functor the book
already holds; there the
quotient stands at the minimal
parabolic, inside Paper 036's
comparison chain, here it stands
for every standard parabolic,
with its submodule twin, as a
theory in its own right. A
generalization is not the thing
generalized. Held apart in both
directions. The held scroll
states the algebraic functor —
CJ_U(V), the u-adic completion
of a Harish-Chandra module — and
the completion's work in the
comparison chain: E = CJ_U(V)
globalized weight by weight, and
Theorem 5.1, q_pi inducing
isomorphisms on u-homology; the
smooth pair nowhere states the
algebraic completion or the
chain. The newer scroll states
the submodule twin,
CJ^infty_{s,P} — the held scroll
has no submodule functor at all
— and the pair's transitivity
along parabolic inclusion
(Proposition 8.2: the Q-functor
after the P-functor is the
Q-functor), a claim about a
family indexed by all standard
parabolics that a
minimal-parabolic scroll cannot
state. Filing the family inside
the completion would bury the
twin and the collapse along
inclusion inside the one functor
the comparison proof consumed.
(ii) 1.2.934, surjectivity onto
the Casselman-Jacquet quotient,
into 1.2.507 — the nearest pair
this pass has weighed: the held
scroll carries the clause
entire, q_pi the canonical
surjection, and the newer scroll
states that the surjection the
book already holds inside
1.2.507 is this proposition's
special case, here proved for
the whole moderate-growth
category. Held apart: a clause
inside a definition is not the
theorem that proves it. The
proposition carries claims the
held scroll nowhere carries —
the sequence is a strict short
exact sequence, the submodule
exactly the quotient map's
kernel; the contrast the work
marks itself (Remark 1.3): for
(g,K)-modules the corresponding
canonical map is injective, not
surjective, the difference being
completeness; both functors
preserve epimorphisms, and the
quotient functor preserves
surjectivity (Propositions 7.1
and 7.2); and the quotient
functor does not preserve
injectivity, Example 7.3 an
explicit counterexample. And the
held scroll carries the functor
and its chain role entire, which
the proposition presupposes
rather than states. A theorem
about a functor and the
functor's own scroll are two
claims.
(iii) 1.2.940, the normal
presentation, into 1.2.508, the
orbit comparison: the two
filings' shared device — a
supported distribution graded by
its transverse order along an
orbit. Held apart by what the
device is made to do. The held
scroll's normal filtration has
graded pieces tempered
distributions on the orbit
tensored with symmetric powers
of the conormal bundle, and it
stands filed as one machine with
the Bruhat filtration, its
single output the
generalized-invariant comparison
(Theorem 3.1); its scalar
reduction (Section 4) computes
cohomology by central-subgroup
induction. The newer scroll's
presentation is an extension
machine: the local normal
decomposition (Proposition 3.7)
assembled globally with
compatible local sections,
I_N-finiteness surviving the
decomposition (Lemma 3.8), and
the working consequence
(Proposition 3.10) that
extension from an orbit reduces
to normal order zero — its
output an extended distribution,
not a cohomology isomorphism.
The objects differ as well: the
held scroll's distributions are
generalized invariants on the
dual of a principal series; the
newer scroll's are I_N-finite
tempered distributions with
general Casselman-Wallach
coefficients. One device, two
theorems hung on it, in two
categories of object.
(iv) 1.2.927, Pasteur's
quadrant, into 1.2.518, the task
dimensions: the source arriving
forty-four chapters after its
use — the book spent the
quadrant from Chapter 55 as one
clause inside SciNet's dimension
layer (Pasteur's quadrant
(Stokes 1997): how far the
served research seeks
understanding and use). Held
apart: the held scroll's claim
is the dimension layer entire —
three 100-point splits, three
CDR scales scored per substep
and averaged, years of
education, the checks against
O*NET's own measures — and the
quadrant stands in it as one
scored dimension among them, an
operationalization grading both
axes under thresholds of the
citing record's own devising.
The newer scroll holds the
construction the clause names
and nowhere states: two
independent axes where the
opposed paradigm held one line;
three named cells — Bohr's,
Edison's, Pasteur's — and a
fourth cell that stands unnamed
in the work, its 'neither'
supplied by the borrowers. A
mention inside an instrument
cannot hold the source's cells
or its blank fourth; the source
cannot hold the instrument's
scales. Paper 081 weighed
revising the held scroll and
held on this same ground; the
separation stands as a merge
question as it stood as a
revision question.
(v) 1.2.922, the physical
feasibility gate, into 1.2.519,
the RL feasibility index: the
pair Paper 080's revision moved.
Before the revision the held
scroll stated the port only,
where the gate stands as a
separate measure; the revision
put the founding construction
first, and its first stage is
the gate's act — a binary
physical feasibility gate sets
every task that irreducibly
requires a body to zero,
unscored. Held apart: the gate's
scroll carries the rationale the
index nowhere states —
embodiment is a veto and not a
ninth dimension, by the founding
work's stated reason: RL
environments exist in software,
so favourable scores on every
other dimension do not make RL
feasible — and the gate's own
exhibits, 43.9% of scored tasks
failing it and forty-seven
occupations zero entire; and it
carries the gate's hinge role,
the conditioning set of the
correlation collapse at 1.2.925.
The index carries the whole the
gate opens — the three stages,
the equal-weight mean rescaled,
the importance-weighted
occupation scores, and the
port's principal-component
construction with its constants
— which the gate's scroll names
as its frame and nowhere states.
The revision named the stage by
its coordinate rather than
absorbing it; the pass finds the
naming correct.
Splits: none — no concept of the
twenty-six (1.2.921-1.2.946)
carries two claims that pull
apart; the compound ones hold
one claim each — 1.2.932's three
faces (idempotence, the
Schwartz-action closure,
maximality) are corollaries of
the one stability, read off the
one submodule; 1.2.926's two
reliabilities are one shape read
on two objects, the contrast
itself the claim; 1.2.938's
filtration and the theorem that
prices it are one construction
and its price. The revision at
1.2.519 stands in the charter's
in-place form — founding
construction first, the port as
its descendant — a dated
restatement, not two claims
pulling apart. The split of
1.2.884, declined at Pass #43,
was re-weighed and stands
declined: the filter's text has
not changed since Paper 077 and
nothing in Papers 080-083
touches it — no new evidence
reopens it. Retired: none. The
standoff companions at 1.5.4
stand at 100. State machines
stand at 315 (278 stated, 37
inferred), unchanged — no
taking-in. Registry entries
2,182 before and after; the
pass's trace is this record and
the path entry at 1.5.5. Next
restructuring pass due at Paper
100 or 960 canonical concepts.
- Pass #43 (2026-11-25; standalone
pass — no taking-in; concept-count
trigger — 920 canonical concepts
meet the 920 line set by Pass
#42 exactly, reached at Paper
079's filing): merges weighed,
five, and held apart, each on its
record. (i) 1.2.917, the faithful
depth sample, into 1.2.649, the
log-normal Poisson depth law —
the nearest pair this pass has
weighed: the newer scroll's whole
content is the older one's
drawing. Held apart: the law
states a distribution — a Poisson
whose rate is log-normal, set so
the mean depth is the target,
the median draw at about 0.88 of
the mean, the heavy right tail
reaching far past it, one draw
locked across all workers for a
micro-batch. It is a claim about
which depths training should
visit, statable entire without
any truncation machinery, and it
stands as named. The faithful
depth sample states that the
inherited sampler does not draw
from that law: holding the
backward window fixed at
k = μ_bwd, it draws the forward
count from the reduced mean
μ_rec − μ_bwd, so the depths
training actually visits form a
shifted, compressed image of the
named law, the constriction
worsening as μ_rec approaches
μ_bwd; its correction draws the
total first, T ~ Λ(μ_rec), and
lets the truncation fall where
it lands. The two claims pull
opposite ways on the same
object: the law stands true as
named while its drawing stands
corrected. Filing the correction
inside the law would bury,
inside the law's own scroll, the
finding that a held paper's
algorithm misdraws its own
distribution — the defect is a
property of the sampler's
construction (the regime at
1.2.648, the truncation at
1.2.650), not of the
distribution; and the law
carries content the correction
nowhere carries — the median's
discount, the tail's reach —
which a merged scroll would
subordinate to the repair. A
distribution and the fidelity
of its drawing are two claims,
and the book's newest finding
is exactly their separation.
(ii) 1.2.908, the failure
partition, into 1.2.884, the
adversarial filter: both
constitute an examination by
what solvers fail. Held apart
by the solvers, the act, and
the residue. The filter's
solvers are learned — ensembles
of linear classifiers over a
fine-tuned model's embeddings,
in the parent form a
discriminator re-initialized
and re-finetuned at every
iteration — run against a
candidate pool until its
accuracy converges, and what
they solve is discarded: the
marked instances never become
data, the table is the residue
of one model's predictability,
and its folds are themselves
produced by the filtering. The
partition's solvers are two
fixed, non-learned instruments
— a retrieval solver over a
large web corpus and a word
co-occurrence solver — run once
over pre-existing human-authored
items; nothing is generated,
nothing is iterated, and
nothing is discarded: both
halves are published as
co-equal sets, the Easy Set
standing as a test set, to be
measured on, not trained on.
And the partition carries a
claim the filter nowhere
carries — difficulty so defined
is solver-relative and nearly
orthogonal to the human axis,
the two sets carrying nearly
identical grade distributions,
grade 8 the largest share of
both — while the filter's table
is bound to its instrument's
blind spots in a way the
partition's is not (Q333). One
act iterates a learned battery
and throws away what it
catches; the other runs two
fixed solvers once and keeps
everything. (iii) 1.2.918, the
tandem scaling laws, into
1.2.734, the LoopLM scaling
laws: the book's two fitted
price lists for looped models.
Held apart by their variable.
The held laws fit loss in model
size, training tokens and
maximum recurrent step for a
gated family, in Chinchilla
form — the step a cap, the
deepest the blueprint permits —
and the pair is bound by
substitution, the step-wise law
returning the total law's form.
The tandem laws fit at fixed
stored parameters: the
loss-optimal mean recurrence
and the loss-optimal token
count as power laws of the
compute budget (μ_rec* ∝ C^0.40
and D* ∝ C^0.78), a law of a
budget's division over the mean
of a sampled depth, carrying
the tandem claim — neither axis
substitutes for the other — and
a parametric form split by
whether gradients flow, for the
FLOP accounting. A cap and a
mean are different variables;
the division law cannot be
stated in the held scroll's
terms, whose parameters vary;
and the held pair's substitution
identity has no analogue in the
newer scroll. (iv) 1.2.909, the
harvested examination, into
1.2.861, the crowd-written
examination: the examination
country's authorship modes —
Pass #41 held the crowd-written
against the hand-written; this
pass weighs the third mode
against the second. Held apart
by when the items were written
and for whom. The crowd-written
examination's items are
commissioned for the set:
piecework written to order — a
one-sentence description, a
reference function, exactly
three asserts — by workers who
knew they were making an
examination; its price is
piecework unevenness, priced by
its own edited subset at
sixteen points. The harvested
examination's items were
written for people, for stakes,
before the set existed — real
standardized tests for grades 3
through 9, gathered over months
— and the dataset-makers did
not author them: no item
carries the makers' construction
artifacts, and that provenance
is the work's anti-artifact
defense; what selection the set
applies comes afterward, at the
partition (1.2.908), not at the
writing. Filing the harvest
inside the commission would
bury the one claim that makes
it a third mode: authorship
that predates and is
indifferent to the set. And the
harvest carries a concentration
the commission nowhere carries
— one supplier contributing
5,128 of 7,787 items, its
breadth narrower than its
source list suggests. (v)
1.2.903, the co-evolving
benchmark, into 1.2.703, the
measure's half-life: the newer
scroll names its own measure as
double — a score on the current
table, and a half-life whose
founding concept stands at the
held scroll. Held apart: the
half-life is a property of a
single set — its freshness,
published postdating the
training of the models first
scored on it, spent by
circulation (12,318 downloads,
mirrors the counter does not
see, bundles inside harnesses)
down to absorption into
training corpora (1.2.704) —
and the decay is announced
nowhere in the artifact: a
spent measure's rows look
exactly like a fresh one's. It
holds of sets that are never
rebuilt. The co-evolving
benchmark is the succession
itself: a lineage of tables
across a task's life, each
rebuilt harder from the same
task against the very model
that solved the last, the
rebuilding's filter being the
solver itself, offered in the
expectation that it too will
fall and be rebuilt again. The
held scroll cannot hold the
succession — nothing in it
rebuilds anything — and the
newer scroll cannot hold the
invisibility: its whole premise
is that the decay is answered,
by rebuilding. Filing the
disease inside the lineage that
answers it would lose the claim
that an unrebuilt set still
decays, silently, by
circulation alone. Splits:
none — no concept of the
nineteen (1.2.902-1.2.920)
carries two claims that pull
apart; the compound ones hold
one claim each — 1.2.884,
weighed for split now that its
parent form stands filed at
Paper 077, remains the
charter's in-place form, one
filter standing on three
filings, its gap (Q333) common
to all three and narrowed, not
split, by the third: the hand
holding the brush is re-rolled
at every pass, within the one
model family; 1.2.918's
parametric form is the tandem
laws' companion, fitted once
over the same variables, its
claim the training-side price
of looping at fixed parameters;
1.2.903's double measure is one
claim about a succession, its
half-life half already standing
as its own scroll (1.2.703);
1.2.908's orthogonality finding
is the partition's second
exhibit, the same claim —
difficulty solver-relative —
read on the human axis;
1.2.914's two injection forms
sort under the one recasting
that is its claim. Retired:
none. The standoff companions
at 1.5.4 stand at 96. State
machines stand at 299 (262
stated, 37 inferred), unchanged
— no taking-in. Registry
entries 2,120 before and
after; the pass's trace is this
record and the path entry at
1.5.5. Next restructuring pass
due at Paper 095 or 940
canonical concepts.
- Pass #42 (2026-11-25; standalone
pass — no taking-in; concept-count
trigger — 901 canonical concepts
cross the 900 line set by Pass
#41, reached at Paper 076's
filing): merges weighed, five, and
held apart, each on its record.
(i) 1.2.890, the trigger word,
into 1.2.887, the pivot word — the
nearest pair this pass has
weighed: both name the single
word a pair turns on. Held apart:
the pivot is a diagnostic, found
after the fact — a finished table
is repriced per differing word,
and the spread of the prices
(spoon at 90 percent, water at
75, freeze at 66) is the finding,
a map of which knowledge is
missing that the aggregate score
cannot draw. The trigger is
constitutive, fixed before the
fact: the item is built around
the flip, annotators are
instructed to produce it, and a
pair whose flip fails validation
is discarded before it can become
data. And the trigger carries a
claim the pivot nowhere carries:
it is where the bias enters — a
flip readable off word
association (13.5 percent of the
expert original, on the work's
cited authority) makes the twin
solvable without the fact it
tests, and the whole apparatus of
validation and filter exists
because of it. One word is the
examination's smallest unit of
construction; the other is its
finest grain of diagnosis.
Filing the built hinge inside
the found one would bury the
direction of the work — the
trigger is spent making items,
the pivot is spent reading them.
(ii) 1.2.896, per-position
halting, into 1.2.676, the
adaptive loop count: both spend
a looped run's depth per input
rather than fixing it in the
blueprint. Held apart: the held
count is one number per input,
set by the task's own step law
or read off the run by a
run-level stopping rule (1.2.677,
1.2.678) — the whole run deepens
or shallows together. Per-position
halting makes the depth a field
over the sequence: at each step
every position's own halting
probability accumulates from its
own state, positions finish at
different depths inside one
synchronous run, and no single
count names the run's length.
The newer scroll's kin hang on
the per-position form alone —
the ponder time (1.2.897) is a
per-position reading, and the
remainder-weighted state
(1.2.899) exists because
positions halt at different
steps. One decides how long each
position computes; the other,
how long the input computes.
(iii) 1.2.899, the
remainder-weighted state, into
1.2.640, exit-probability
weighting: the same arithmetic
shape — a trajectory's states
weighted by the halting
distribution's own numbers. Held
apart by what the weighting buys
and when it is spent. The held
concept spends the weights at
training time: each loop is
credited the exit head's
probability, and the trajectory's
reward is apportioned by the
model's own halting signal — an
apportionment of credit, as its
scroll states, not a score and
not an output. The newer concept
spends the weights at inference,
inside the run itself: the
position's output IS the blend,
the trajectory's states mixed in
the proportions the halting rule
assigned, remainder and all, and
the mixture is what the next
layer reads. One weighting
decides who is paid for the
trajectory; the other decides
what the trajectory says. The
newer scroll names the kinship
itself — a descendant spends the
same shape at training time —
and the book's practice is kin
named, concepts separate.
(iv) 1.2.892, the residue
release, into 1.2.826, the
decontamination pass: both stand
at the seam between corpus and
examination, over material a
filter has judged. Held apart:
the held pass excises — measured
thirteen-word overlaps cut out
of training text, and what is
cut stays cut; its claim is
mechanical and its act is
removal. The residue release is
the opposite act on the same
seam: the filter's discards —
31,690 of the work's validated
problems, removed as too biased
to examine with — are published
as training data, the full
release's training split the
union of kept and discarded, and
the headline models train on the
union entire. In the held scroll
the removed material never comes
back; in the newer one it
returns as the instrument's own
fuel, carrying a double standing
— too biased to examine with,
good enough to train on — that
the work's own footnote sharpens:
trained on the kept split alone,
its two headline models stand at
chance. An excision weighed
against a republication: filing
the return inside the removal
would bury the double standing
that is the newer scroll's whole
claim. (v) 1.2.889, the twin
schema, into 1.2.882, the paired
examination: the examination
country's two pair-shaped
tables, filed in consecutive
chapters. Held apart: where the
pairing lives. In the held table
the pair stands inside a single
item — a goal and two finished
solutions, chosen between face
to face — and the pairing cannot
be dissolved, because no process
in that work addresses the two
solutions separately. In the
twin schema the pair is two
items — two sentences sharing
one frame, differing only at the
trigger (1.2.890), each filled
separately — and the second
sentence exists to cancel the
first's biases, a discipline of
construction imposed at
authorship. And the twin pairing
is fragile in a way the held one
is not: the work's own filter
acts on instances and can ship
one twin without the other
(1.2.891), about a third of the
debiased questions standing
twinless — the pairing dissolved
by the very instrument that
makes the table hard. What is
examined differs with the form:
choosing the way that works,
between two concrete procedures,
against filling a blank whose
answer the sibling sentence
polices. Splits: none — no
concept of the twenty (1.2.882-
1.2.901) carries two claims that
pull apart; the compound ones
hold one claim each — 1.2.884's
founding revision is the
charter's in-place form, one
filter standing on two filings,
its gap (Q333) common to both;
1.2.889's fragility already
stands as its own scroll
(1.2.891); 1.2.896's remainder
already stands as its own scroll
(1.2.899); 1.2.900's hedge is
its filing form — the claim as
the work states it — and what
would exercise it stands as
Q341; 1.2.893's self-application
to its transfer gains is the
score's second exhibit, its
separation standing as Q339.
Retired: none. The standoff
companions at 1.5.4 stand at 93.
State machines stand at 285 (248
stated, 37 inferred), unchanged —
no taking-in. Registry entries
2,074 before and after; the
pass's trace is this record and
the path entry at 1.5.5. Next
restructuring pass due at Paper
090 or 920 canonical concepts.
- Pass #41 (2026-11-25; standalone
pass — no taking-in; concept-count
trigger — 881 canonical concepts
cross the 880 line set by Pass
#40, reached at Paper 073's
filing): merges weighed, five, and
held apart, each on its record.
(i) 1.2.864, the challenge tests,
into 1.2.828, the differential
oracle — the nearest pair this
pass has weighed: both deepen a
shallow examination by bringing
more tests against the counted.
Held apart: the oracle manufactures
its tests from a reference program
— it stores a program, not answers,
generates the suite by the hundred
(1.2.830), and its verdict stays
mechanical, its evidence a
reference's behaviour on the same
input. The challenge tests have no
reference program and no
generation: a person reads the
counted solutions themselves —
thirty-three passing of fifty
sampled — and writes a few tests
by hand, adversarially, against
exactly where those solutions are
thin; its evidence is the
solutions' own weak places, found
by reading them. One is a verdict
computed from a program; the other
is an audit aimed at answers
already counted. And the newer
scroll's lesson — the second law
(75.2.1) read from the shallow
end: what the unexamined part
conceals is not distributed evenly
among the counted — is a claim
about the counted that the
oracle's scroll nowhere carries.
The newer scroll names the kinship
itself — Chapter 84's deepening
run by hand, a year earlier — and
the book's practice is kin named,
concepts separate. (ii) 1.2.869,
the trained verifier, into
1.2.716, the reference-answer
judge — the book's two judges
that are models. The held judge
is handed a reference answer it
did not produce and reads it at
the moment of judgment; its
verdict is consumed inside the
training loop as reward — the
crossing itself (62.2.2), evidence
beyond the judged object, spent
inside the computation. The
trained verifier consulted the key
once, at its own training, through
the answer-only labels (1.2.872),
and at judgment consults nothing:
the reference survives in it as
weights, and its verdict is spent
after the judged run ends, by the
ranked selection (1.2.870) — the
remove weighed at 90.2.2, its
forward shape named at Q323. One
judge reads a reference; the other
remembers one. Filing the trained
judge inside the reading judge
would bury the distinction the
weighings of Chapters 88-90
turned on. (iii) 1.2.881, the
contamination audit, into 1.2.826,
the decontamination pass: both
stand between the training corpus
and the examination, at the seam
Pass #40 (iv) weighed across. The
held pass is the builders'
instrument on their own corpus,
run before training, and it acts —
measured thirteen-word overlaps
cut out of training text, its
claim mechanical. The audit is the
examiners' instrument, run after
the fact on the examined model's
own scores, and it only reads:
the correlation of a question's
predictability with its accuracy —
r = -0.43 zero-shot, -0.56
few-shot — certifies the key
unmemorized, and nothing is
removed. One guards a corpus by
cutting; the other certifies a
table by reading the pattern of
its results. Their limits differ
as their acts do: the pass is
blind past its definition, to
paraphrase and translation (Q297);
the audit reads the questions
only, and verbatim memorization
only — a paraphrased leak is
invisible to it, as its own scroll
states. (iv) 1.2.861, the
crowd-written examination, into
1.2.856, the hand-written
examination — the examination
country's two tables authored for
the purpose. In the held scroll
the hand is the defense: one
hundred sixty-four problems
written by a person for the set,
never in the wild, so the founding
readings are clean — its claim is
provenance. In the newer one the
hands are a workforce: nine
hundred seventy-four problems
commissioned as piecework from
workers with basic Python, and
its claim is the trade — scale
enough to fine-tune on, and
phrasing no one briefed, bought
with uneven care the work itself
prices: the edited subset of 426,
hand-verified, on which the same
models score sixteen points
higher. Authorship as a wall
against the corpus, against
authorship as commissioning; and
the newer set's three asserts a
problem — the shallowest tried set
the country holds, against the
held set's average of 7.7 — is
part of its claim, the ground its
own audits (1.2.864) stand on.
(v) 1.2.870, the ranked selection,
into 1.2.855, pass@k: a procedure
weighed against the measure it
cashes. The held concept prices an
oracle's pick — from n samples
with c correct, the unbiased
any-of-k estimate; no judge exists
in it, and the count rises with k
by construction. The ranked
selection is that pick made real
with a fallible judge (1.2.869),
and its second half is a claim the
measure nowhere carries: past
roughly four hundred candidates
the pick stops improving and then
worsens, as the search finds the
completions that fool the judge —
the selection carries its judge's
error surface as its own ceiling
(Q325). A measure that can only
rise, against a procedure that
falls; filing the procedure inside
the measure would bury the
inversion that is its reason to
stand. Splits: none — no concept
of the twenty-one (1.2.861-1.2.881)
carries two claims that pull
apart; the compound ones hold one
claim each — 1.2.868's naive
extrapolation is the worked
table's own pricing of its scale,
1.2.870's ceiling is the
selection's second half, 1.2.873's
divergence is one phenomenon with
its management inside it, 1.2.877's
inversion already stands as Q330,
and 1.2.875's four-question gap is
a caveat carried at 91.1.4, not a
second claim. Retired: none. The
standoff companions at 1.5.4 stand
at 90. State machines stand at
275 (238 stated, 37 inferred),
unchanged — no taking-in. Registry
entries 2,027 before and after;
the pass's trace is this record
and the path entry at 1.5.5. Next
restructuring pass due at Paper
085 or 900 canonical concepts.
