W. The verified artifact (Paper 017) — 1.2.206-1.2.222:
AlphaProof Code; the specification as the trusted
artifact; testing a specification; the amendment
protocol; the prover team; the gatekeeper; a formal
semantics of an instruction set; hooks; verification
at the machine-code level; the binary implements the
model; the concretization homomorphism; refinement up
to collisions; reductions as priced programs; PQXDH;
the Triple Ratchet; a key used twice, judged together;
the trusted base, enumerated.
The cluster calls at the founding: cluster Q SUPPORTED
and put to work — its engine and its kernel floor
carry a deployment-grade campaign, and the seat of the human moves from prover to the one who states; the translation
pole of cluster G made into a pair of poles, the
rider standing on 1.2.48; cluster F SUPPORTED — its
floor is here the acceptance test itself; cluster B
SUPPORTED as kin — the harness grown to a crew, with
a gate the harnesses of cluster U lacked; and Q84, the
open question of cluster V, is pressed by a worked
neighbour — the gatekeeper prevents wrong acceptance
as the bench prevents illegal moves — pressed, not
closed. Links outward: 1.2.210 to 1.2.15 (the
harness); 1.2.211 to 1.2.41 (the floor); 1.2.214 to
1.2.48 and to the foundation 1.3.213; 1.2.222 to the
standing record (1.4.1-1.4.6). Restructure Pass #11
fell due inside this taking-in and stands logged
above; the next falls at Paper 020 or 240 concepts,
the count standing at 222. Standoff map for cluster W
(1.2.206-1.2.222): foundations 1.3.212, 1.3.213,
1.3.87, 1.3.162, 1.3.85.

X. Specification engineering — the agreed meaning (Study S010)
— 1.2.223-1.2.229: specification engineering; the agreed
semantic model; validated, not verified; structure lost by
lowering; the envelope of allowed builds; refinement between
two semantics; the loaded definition. The cluster stands in a
dispute, and the dispute is its founding fact: it argues the
pole against cluster W, in the open, and the filing of the two
poles stands whole at 28.2.1. The calls at the founding:
cluster W PRESSURED — its pole argued against as a class, its
cost quoted in its own words, the quotation checked at 28.1.2;
the pressure is recorded, and the claims of W stand as their
paper made them. Cluster G EXTENDED — the rider of this study
on 1.2.48 adds a third resting place for trust beside
translation and the floor. Cluster Q SUPPORTED as the shared
engine of both poles — each proves in Lean and takes only
kernel-checked proof. Cluster I NEIGHBOUR — specification as
control (1.2.57-1.2.64) is the statement used to steer agents;
this cluster is the statement as a field of engineering in its
own right. No restructuring pass fell due at this taking-in;
the next falls at Paper 020 or 240 concepts, the count
standing at 229. Standoff map for cluster X (1.2.223-1.2.229):
foundations 1.3.219, 1.3.87, 1.3.213, 1.3.212, 1.3.85; defined
words 1.3.214, 1.3.220, 1.3.221, 1.3.167.
Y. The dual, computed (Paper 019) — 1.2.237-1.2.247:
the joint numerical range; the determinantal
polynomial; the algebraic Kippenhahn
variety; Katz's test; the Gauss map; sampling the
dual; the candidate degree; completely split primes;
reconstruction across the roots; certification of the
reconstruction; the four certified dual surfaces. The centre of gravity of the cluster is its own: a classical
object of matrix analysis — the range and its
generating dual — made computable by sampling and
interpolation in place of the older striking-out road, every output
carrying an exact certificate. The calls at the
founding: cluster E NEIGHBOUR — projective duality
and determinantal surfaces stand near the algebraic ground of the annex, and the author's own trade is the
computational study of surfaces of the kind the annex holds;
but nothing here is symplectic, no manifold is glued
or counted, and the machinery — sampling, kernels,
lifts — belongs to E in no part. Cluster W KIN IN SHAPE —
a computed object admitted only through an exact
gate, its certification cost printed in the open;
the kinship is recorded at 1.2.246 and priced as
shape, the gate here being the object itself, not a
held-out statement. Cluster Q NEIGHBOUR AT A
DISTANCE — both clusters compute with algebra in
systems (Magma and Singular here; Lean there), and
share nothing else. Links outward: 1.2.246 to
1.2.211 (the gatekeeper); 1.2.237 to 1.2.14 (the
measurement agenda). Restructure Pass #12 fell due
inside this taking-in and stands logged above; the
next falls at Paper 020 or 260 concepts, the count
standing at 247. Standoff map for cluster Y
(1.2.237-1.2.247): foundations 1.3.230-1.3.240,
1.3.30, 1.3.97, 1.3.26; defined words 1.3.241-1.3.243.
S, EXTENDED (Paper 020) — 1.2.248-1.2.259: the piecewise
translation; the piecewise interpretation; provable
equivalence; the semantic dual; ii-morphisms; the dual of an
ii-morphism; composition of piecewise interpretations; the
bicategory of theories; the reflection principle; piecewise
bi-interpretability; the sortal replacement; the
biequivalence. The extension is the second
systematic theory of the cluster: where the essays of
Study S007 read a
logic inside a category, this paper reads translations
between logics as ways in a bicategory and as functors
between the categories of their models — the ground of the
cluster, worked at research depth. The calls at the
extension: cluster S EXTENDED, on its own ground and by its
own machinery — the centre of gravity is interpretations
between theories, and the semantic dual is the functor
ground of 1.2.171 put to work between theories. Cluster F
NEIGHBOUR — theories as objects with ways between them is
the categorical twin of its claims-as-types reading; the
paper is semantics-first throughout, its theorems about
models and functors, not about proofs, and the neighbour
standing is recorded at 1.2.255's link to 1.2.40. Cluster G
NEIGHBOUR — its road is translation trusted by a checking;
here a translation is known by the functor it induces, and
the satisfaction proposition of 1.2.251 is a receipt of the
same shape as the ledger of 1.2.48, at the level of meaning
rather than of trust. Cluster X NEIGHBOUR AT ONE POINT — the
biequivalence is one meaning under two presentations with
its sameness proved, where cluster X holds the agreed
meaning itself; the link stands at 1.2.259 to 1.2.224.
Links outward: 1.2.251 to 1.2.48 (the ledger of translation);
1.2.255 to 1.2.40 (propositions as types); 1.2.259 to 1.2.224
(the agreed semantic model). Restructure Pass #13 fell due
inside this taking-in and stands logged above; the next
falls at Paper 025 or 280 concepts, the count standing at
