AH. THE EVOLVED QUANTIZER — an algorithm found by
search, priced by parts (Study S015): 1.2.317-1.2.327:
e-means, the design evolved; the scaling-law recipe; the
four bottlenecks; s-means, the artifact; the D^1.5
seeding; the distortion-weighted revival; the priced
ending; cache tiling; the fused kernels and the chosen
backend; evolution over a modular graph; the unseen
suite and the leave-one-out price. The centre of gravity
of the cluster is its own: an artifact whose claims
arrive with their parts priced and their whole tested on
ground the making never saw — where every neighbour
cluster holds artifacts priced by their papers' own runs
alone. The calls at the founding: cluster B NEIGHBOUR
AND KIN — the collapsed optimization loop (1.2.16) is
this cluster's evolution with the search moved inside
the run; the two are linked, not merged, at Pass #16.
Cluster D NEIGHBOUR AT ONE POINT — the surrogate
(1.2.33) prices a design space from cheap runs, as the
scaling-law recipe (1.2.318) prices the knobs of a
quantizer. Cluster O NEIGHBOUR BY INSTRUMENT — the
pricing of a rule from its record (1.2.110) is the shape
of the unseen suite (1.2.327) with an algorithm in the
rule's place. Cluster AC NEIGHBOUR BY SHAPE — search
over executions (1.2.281-1.2.287) searches the runs of a
fixed game; this cluster's search (1.2.326) searches the
runners. No gate of the Oracle is exercised by the
founding; the bar stands at about 62%. The count crosses
320 in this taking-in, and Restructure Pass #16 fell due
inside it (logged in this scroll, at this taking-in).
The next pass falls at Paper 025 or 340 canonical
concepts, the count standing at 327. Standoff map for
cluster AH (1.2.317-1.2.327): foundations
1.3.278-1.3.281.

O EXTENDED — CONFORMAL GROUND, AND A GUARANTEE PRICED
(Paper 024): 1.2.328-1.2.343: the weighted conformal
p-value; the Benjamini-Hochberg procedure, priced; the
global-null counterexample; the strict-selection
counterexample; the covariance identity; the
calibration-conditional reduction; Simes curvature;
the decoy switch; the excess bound; the Poisson-limit
heavy-cell model; the sharpness; the fixed-distribution
excess; the global-null price; the envelope; the
deflated level; the rule of thumb. The extension's
centre: a judging procedure whose certificate does not
hold, its failure priced from both sides and repaired
at a stated cost — where the cluster's founding held
judges that work, priced by their corrections. The
calls at the extension: cluster O's own founding
NEIGHBOUR AND GROUND — the founding judge (1.2.110)
judges under shift by reweighting what was logged, as
the weighted p-value does, and the corrected criterion
(1.2.114) is the standard the priced guarantee is read
against; both stand unrevised. Cluster G NEIGHBOUR BY
METHOD — the counterexamples are carried by exact
computation checked by independent programs
(1.2.48), and one of them by this house's own
recomputation. Cluster I NEIGHBOUR BY SHAPE — the
envelope is a certificate a data set carries about
itself, a specification the data meet or fail
(1.2.57). Cluster P NEIGHBOUR BY KIND — the decoy
switch is a priced way for a judge to be wrong
(1.2.121). Restructure Pass #17 fell due inside this
taking-in (the 340-concept trigger) and stands in
the log below. The next pass falls at Paper 025 or
360 canonical concepts, the count standing at 343.
