iled at its source under the partial-text clause, on the publisher's abstract and the citing records entire. The cluster's algebra engine, filed sixteenth.Paper 097 extends the cluster (Chapter 115): 1.2.1070 the filtered ring; 1.2.1071 completion with respect to a filtration, and its exactness (Chapter I, Proposition 5.10); 1.2.1072 the associated graded ring; 1.2.1073 the Noetherian graded ring and its local conditions — the filtered-rings treatise Chapter 54's completion proof spends in the same sentence as Paper 096's Artin-Rees theorem, the middle leg of the founding proof's three consecutive queue ranks, filed at its source under the partial-text clause, on the publisher's record and the citing record entire. The cluster's completion ground, filed seventeenth.Paper 098 extends the cluster (Chapter 116): 1.2.1074 finite generation over U(n) (the restriction theorem, Corollary 1.2); 1.2.1075 the restriction to n — the restriction paper the founding chapter's completion proof spends beside both of the works the walk has just filed, and the finiteness ground of the homology standings, filed at its source under the partial-text clause, on the citing records and the first author's own list entire. The cluster's restriction ground, filed eighteenth.Paper 099 extends the cluster (Chapter 117): 1.2.1076 the k-roots; 1.2.1077 the relative Weyl group; 1.2.1078 quasi-closed sets of roots and their subgroups; 1.2.1079 the product decomposition of unipotent groups (Proposition 3.11); 1.2.1080 Levi decompositions over k; 1.2.1081 conjugacy over k; 1.2.1082 the standard parabolic k-subgroups; 1.2.1083 the Bruhat decomposition over k; 1.2.1084 the maximal split subgroup; 1.2.1085 the relative diagram determined — the founding account of the relative theory the founding chapter's bibliography carries as [BT65] and its body spends once, filed at its source on the full text held entire. The cluster's relative ground, filed nineteenth.Paper 100 extends the cluster (Chapter 118): 1