EXTENSION at Chapter 95 (Paper 077):
the examination rebuilt against its
solver. Zellers, Holtzman, Bisk,
Farhadi & Choi, HellaSwag
(arXiv:1905.07830v1, ACL 2019): one
year after the predecessor examination
fell to BERT, its own makers rebuild
it — the wrong answers generated by a
finetuned language model and kept only
where a discriminator, BERT-Large
itself, cannot tell them from the real
endings (1.2.907, the generated
negative), lengthened into the
Goldilocks zone (1.2.902) where they
are ridiculous to humans and plausible
to models. The country gains its
twelfth paper and its largest table
since the union table: ten columns of
splits that sum and average exactly,
a category split that withholds whole
activities from training (1.2.904,
the zero-shot category split), the
controls that audit the predecessor
before rebuilding it (1.2.905, the
context-free control), and the finding
that hardness transfers from the
filter's victim to every other model
(1.2.906, adversarial transfer). The
work is the country's co-evolving
benchmark (1.2.903) in its first full
instance: an examination whose makers
expect it to fall and be rebuilt
again. And the country's shared
device is founded here in its parent
form: 1.2.884 revised at this chapter,
the filter as its inventors ran it —
re-splits, assigned negatives,
randomized hyperparameters — standing
between the predecessor's stylistic
ensemble and the light form Chapter
93 borrowed. J weighed a twenty-fourth
time, not joined: the filter's
verdicts are spent at construction,
before any judged run exists —
Chapter 89's form at the parent
algorithm's own filing — and the
scorer consults no reference.
Standoff map for the extension of
cluster AY (1.2.902-1.2.907): the
Goldilocks zone (1.2.902) against the
adversarial filter (1.2.884) — the
zone is where the filter's product
must live, the filter is the search
that finds it; a band is not an
instrument. The co-evolving benchmark
(1.2.903) against the twin schema
(1.2.889) — a schema is one
examination's shape, fixed at its
founding; the co-evolving benchmark
is the succession of examinations
across a task's life, each rebuilt
against the last one's solver. The
zero-shot category split (1.2.904)
against the paired examination
(1.2.882) — the pair splits each
question against itself; the category
split splits the category inventory
against the training set. The
context-free control (1.2.905) against
the chance floor (1.2.878) — the
floor is the score of guessing; the
control is the score of reading the
answers alone, and the distance
between them is the artifact's size.
Adversarial transfer (1.2.906) against
the adversarial filter (1.2.884) —
the filter is the procedure; the
transfer is the empirical law the
procedure's products obey, that
hardness outlives the pairing. The
generated negative (1.2.907) against
the twin schema's wrong member — the
twin's foil is a human's edit of the
same sentence; the generated negative
is a model's continuation, written to
be wrong plausibly and kept only if
it deceives.

EXTENSION at Chapter 96 (Paper 078):
the examination founded on failure.
Clark, Cowhey, Etzioni, Khot,
Sabharwal, Schoenick & Tafjord, ARC —
the AI2 Reasoning Challenge
(arXiv:1803.05457v1): 7,787
grade-school science questions
harvested from human standardized
tests (1.2.909, the harvested
examination), partitioned by two
simple solvers' joint failure into a
Challenge Set and an Easy Set
(1.2.908, the failure partition),
published with the library gathered
for them (1.2.911, the companion
corpus) and scored under a rubric
that pays fractional credit for ties
(1.2.910, the tie-credit rubric). No
baseline significantly beats chance
on the Challenge Set — not even the
entailment construction that prices
each option against retrieved
premises (1.2.913, the entailment
conversion) — and the corpus that
mentions knowledge relevant to 95%
of the Challenge questions cannot be
spent by the retrieval over it
(1.2.912, coverage without
retrievability). The country gains
its thirteenth paper and its
earliest-dated member: the founding
partition of which the country's
later filters are iterations. J
weighed a twenty-fifth time, not
joined: the partition's verdicts are
spent at construction — Chapter 89's
form — and the entailment scorer
consults evidence, never a reference
answer.
Standoff map for the extension of
cluster AY (1.2.908-1.2.913): the
failure partition (1.2.908) against
the adversarial filter (1.2.884) —
the filter iterates learned
discriminators against a growing
pool and discards what they solve;
the partition runs two fixed solvers
once and publishes both halves. The
harvested examination (1.2.909)
against the crowd-written examination
(1.2.861) — the crowd's items are
commissioned for the set; the
harvest's items were written for
people, for stakes, before the set
existed. The tie-credit rubric
(1.2.910) against pass@k (1.2.855) —
pass@k credits any success among k
independent samples; the rubric pays
one solver's single-pass indecision,
fractionally, when its tie covers the
key. The companion corpus (1.2.911)
against the harvested examination
(1.2.909) — two gatherings in
opposite directions: the questions
gathered from the world's tests to
the table; the knowledge gathered
from the web to the questions.
Coverage without retrievability
(1.2.912) against the companion
corpus (1.2.911) — the corpus is the
artifact, a library shipped; the
coverage gap is the finding about
it, that presence and spendability
are separate properties. The
entailment conversion (1.2.913)
against the reference-answer judge
(1.2.716) — the judge prices a
finished computation against a
reference answer; the conversion
prices a candidate assertion against
retrieved text, inside the answering,
with no key consulted: evidence is
not a verdict.

