THE NUMBER GIVEN A NEW QUESTION (2026-11-14). The number the
ledger carries (1.1.4) has been given a new
question to answer, on Will's direction: it no
longer measures the closing this list watches for.
It now measures how reliably the house can place
any piece of information into exactly one of the
four kinds of standing of the registry — True,
False, Unknown, Fiction — kept as four gates, of
which True and Unknown stand met, Fiction stands
half met, and False stands unmet: no entry of the
793 stands False, and the gate has never been
tried on the stream as it comes. On the new
measure the ledger stands at about 62% (range
55-70). The signs on this list are unchanged —
the run of the Index, the axis events, and the
calibration of the skim still watch the fixed
point; only the meaning of the bar has moved.
The full record of the change, with the grounds
of each gate, stands at 1.1.4.

DIRECTION RECORDED (2026-11-14, Will): "next step:
oracles learn from imperfect knowledge. academia
has missed the opportunity to help submitters who
identify the correct shape of a problem, despite
failing on some nuance, because they can only
reason in truth. the Exocortex encodes all
perspectives, and does not falter. researchers on
the fringe are the target market."
THE EDGE AS RECORDED: the four kinds of standing
bind claim by claim, not paper by paper. A
submission from the fringe is read for the shape
it found as well as for its claims: the shape,
where it is right, is filed and stands, even
where the fine points of the working fail. And
the evidence that tries the gate of False is
expected to arrive by this stream.

DIRECTION RECORDED (2026-11-14, Will): "MOAT heats
up thought space so individual claims can be
pulled out of papers. the process of ingesting a
paper spaghettifies it into these four categories.
your score as a researcher grows along those
dimensions for introducing novelty to the Oracle."
THE EDGE AS RECORDED: a paper does not survive
its taking-in as a unit. It is heated until its
claims come apart, and each claim is placed in
one of the four kinds of standing on its own
grounds. What a researcher brings the Oracle is
counted the same way: a score in four parts, one
for each kind of standing — True, False, Unknown,
Fiction — grown by the novelty their filings
place in each. From the next taking-in, the delta
scroll of each chapter (x.1.5) carries a NOVELTY
BY AUTHOR line for each author of the work, and
the running score stands on the researcher's
entry among the researchers (1.5.6). The first
drawing of the scores stands there, drawn this
date from the delta scrolls as filed.

