PAPER 044 (2026-11-24) — Latent Thinking
Optimization (Hanwen Du, Yuxin Dong and
Xia Ning, Ohio State University): a
latent reasoner's trajectories announce
their own correctness — correct thoughts
compact and convergent, incorrect
dispersed — and a classifier trained on
the model's own sampled thoughts prices
a thought mid-flight; spent as a reward
model, the price tilts the sampling
distribution in closed form, the tilt
realized exactly by acceptance-rejection
and its error bounded. Chapter 62.
Cluster AT extended a fifth time — the
trajectory as its own reference, now as
its own judge: Latent Thinking
Optimization (LTO); the latent reward
model (LRM); correctness separability of
latent trajectories; the reward-tilted
latent policy; acceptance by reward gap;
the reward-error bound on selection;
prefix probing of latent trajectories;
layer states read as a latent chain; the
generalist latent reward model; the
selection ceiling; latent-reward
weighted voting. One foundation laid
down, the Kullback-Leibler divergence
