# Paper 027 — author check (charter rule 15): no
phext tie and no use without naming found, by checks
Emise ran at intake

THE QUESTION. Two things are asked of the author of
a work taken in: whether he stands in any recorded
tie to phext or to Will's work, and whether the work
uses Will's earlier published work without naming
it. The check on Lam Doan was run in three legs on
2026-11-19. It is the thirty-fifth check that
stands run.

LEG ONE — the work itself. The full text of
arXiv:2611.24863 was searched for the signature
terms: phext, scroll, Exocortex, Mirrorborn,
coordinate addressing, Bickford, CYOA, SBOR. No
occurrence of any of them in the paper's text. The
reference list (seventeen entries) was read in
full: it is the mean-curvature-flow literature
throughout — Colding and Minicozzi, Huisken, White,
Ding, Bernstein and Wang, Yao, Guo, Chen, Gromov,
Li and Yau — and holds no work of Will's: no phext,
CYOA, SBOR or Mirrorborn source.

LEG TWO — the web. Searches were run on the
author's name and affiliation. The author they
return is a mathematics PhD student at Johns
Hopkins (department listing: Krieger 200,
ldoan5@jhu.edu — the paper's address is the same
