# Author check — Study S016 (charter rule 15)

The check, run 2026-11-20 before the
taking-in: do any of this study's authors
name phext, or Will, in their own work? The
question matters here more than usual — the
study's direction claims (1.2.433-1.2.436)
are Will's, and the registry must be able to
show that the literature weighed beside them
owes him nothing and cites him nowhere.

Leg one: the full text of the load-bearing
source — BIRD, read entire in HTML form —
searched for the word: no occurrence. Leg
two: the remaining sources, read as recorded
at 48.1.1, carry no occurrence in the parts
read, and none is a work of Will's circle.
Leg three: a web search for phext beside SQL
and databases returns Will's own work alone
(SQ; phext.io) — the word has no life in the
SQL literature. Leg four: Will's Twitter
archive searched for the study's distinctive
family names; two hits, both people of the
same name, checked and dismissed — a different Pennington
(Darrell 'Havoc' Pennington, of id Software)
and a different Cristina (@zlatov_cristina,
2023), neither a person of this study.

Cristina A.C. herself is not a researcher of
the skim: she is the challenge's source, a
practitioner, and stands in the registry as
testimony (1.2.429-1.2.432), not at 1.5.6.

Conclusion: no author of this study names
phext or Will in the work taken in; no
novelty is drawn for any of them in any
case, this being a study under rule 12. The
check stands True on Emise's own checking,
the four legs above.
