THE STEP, TIGHTENED. None of that steps
1.2.460. Will ruled on 2026-11-21 (22:19
CST) that the step text at 50.1.3 is
tightened: 1.2.460 steps to True/verified
only on independent-kernel checking of
the five endpoints on a post-fix
toolchain — a 4.36.0-class Lean with
nanoda and leanchecker-paranoid,
checkers plural — and not on the
artifact's own build and axiom printout.
The grounds, as ruled: Lean 4.34.0
closed three kernel routes to a proof of
False — #14806 (is_def_eq caching),
#14807 (is_prop skipping the
proof-irrelevance guard; its bogus proof
was also accepted by nanoda), #14838 (a
32-bit refcount overflow) — beside
CVE-2026-72711 (fixed in 4.32.2) and
CVE-2026-72844 (nested-inductive
projection forgery, in versions up to
v4.31.0). The artifact pins Lean
v4.33.1: it carries the CVE fixes and
predates the kernel fixes, so a build on
its own toolchain is blind to exactly
this class of failure, and its axiom
printout — which reports what the kernel
accepted — cannot see it either. The
comparator discipline the book adopted
at this chapter's filing (Q163) always
named independent kernels; the ruling
makes the post-fix version of that
requirement explicit, and this addendum
is where the tightening stands on the
record.

THE CLAIM'S STANDING. 1.2.460 therefore
stands Unknown/attributed, as it stood:
the build leg is complete and recorded,
and the independent-kernel leg has not
been run or scheduled — its named
obstacle is the exporter's peak memory
(163 GB, no ranch home), and its named
route is declaration-level judging with
nanoda inside the 48 GB bin. When that
leg runs and lands, the step will be
recorded against this chapter, as 50.1.5
provided. This addendum is itself one
scroll and one registry entry — the
house's record of a ruling received and
of checks the house ran, standing
True/verified as such; it moves no other
entry, and no concept count changes
under it.
