# Paper 036 — the results, as claimed, and where the paper places itself

THE RESULTS, AS THE PAPER REPORTS THEM.
Theorem 1.1 (1.2.495): nilradical homology
commutes with smooth globalization for
every standard parabolic of a real linear
reductive group. Corollary 1.2: the
cohomological form. Corollary 1.3
(1.2.501, 1.2.502): the Tor and Ext forms
over the augmentation quotients F_k.
Corollary 1.4 (1.2.504): u^k M closed in
the (co)chain spaces. Corollary 1.5
(1.2.505): closedness and Casselman-Wallach
homology on the smooth Bruhat pieces.

WHERE THE PAPER PLACES ITSELF. The minimal-
parabolic comparison was known: Hecht-
Taylor deduced it from minimal
globalization; Li-Liu-Yu (2021, the second
author among them) proved it directly with
distributions and the Bruhat and transverse-
order filtrations. Casselman had claimed a
proof for arbitrary standard parabolics,
unpublished (the broader conjecture stands
at Vogan's Conjecture 10.3). This paper
combines comparison through Casselman-
Jacquet modules (the authors' joint work
[CWYZ26], [WY26]) with the distributional
approach to treat arbitrary standard
parabolics, and extends the comparison from
trivial coefficients to the higher
augmentation quotients. Its limits, stated
plainly: real LINEAR reductive groups only;
the general real reductive case and the
canonical-globalization generality of
Vogan's conjecture are not claimed.
