# Paper 037 — the results, as claimed, and where the work places itself

THE THESIS (the site's About, the authors'
own words in substance). AI is
transforming scientific research faster
than it can be measured; to know which
researchers and fields will benefit, and
where bottlenecks and inequalities will
emerge, the question must be asked of
specific tasks within specific domains,
not of science as a monolith — a
cardiologist and a cosmologist are both
scientists and spend their days on
fundamentally different activities. SciNet
is built to make that task-level analysis
rigorous: which tasks are augmented or
automated, where the gains concentrate,
what follows for careers, specialization,
and the distribution of discovery.

THE VALIDATIONS, AS REPORTED
(METHODOLOGY.md Section 6). Ratings
against O*NET's expert ratings, on 425
tasks of 40 scientific occupations:
correlations 0.66 (importance), 0.63
(relevance), 0.75 (frequency). Times
against protocols.io: 26,404 protocols;
on 769 exact matches covering 383 SciNet
steps, the elapsed-time estimates
correlate with protocol durations at
0.53 — against 0.44 for one protocol
predicting others, and 0.55 for the
estimates predicting them, the difference
not statistically significant: the
estimates agree with protocols about as
well as protocols agree with each other.
The task list against the papers: the
prevalence measurement itself (1.2.516),
with its quote audit clean. The dimension
prompts against O*NET's measures (1.2.518)
and the Elo's internal consistency
(1.2.520) stand as reported there.

ADOPTION, AS REPORTED ELSEWHERE. The
SciNet taxonomy is already in use as
another instrument's skeleton: Anthropic's
'AI for Scientific Discovery' report
(2026-11-05) classifies 207,049 Claude and
Claude Code research sessions by SciNet
field, subfield and task — an external
report, recorded here as its authors
state it, not verified by the house.
# Paper 037 — the delta: what the model takes in

WHERE THE WORK LIVES. Cluster AS is
FOUNDED — the anatomy of research work:
concepts 1.2.509-1.2.522, the tracker's
first science-of-science ground. The
founding argument is the object itself.
The book holds countries of mathematics,
of reasoning, of compression, of format —
but no held concept takes research work
itself as its object: what researchers do,
task by task, had no country. Neighbours
weighed and held apart at the founding:
cluster AK (the format country — its
object is the shape of data, not the shape
of work); cluster AP (reasoning kept as
code — its object is one kind of machine
assistance, not the labour it assists);
the house's own Areas (Chapter 1, Section
5 — the tracker's machinery for keeping
its model, not concepts in the model). No
cross-cluster link is filed: the kinships
are of shape, and shape is not a claim.

THE AXIS JUDGMENT, IN WRITING. (a) The
centre of gravity — the structure of
scientific work as data — is ground the
model held no slot for (toward). (b) No
held concept is re-read to receive it:
the filing's moves are of held kinds — a
taxonomy, a corpus, ratings, an index, an
Elo (against). (c) Its bridges to held
ground run through machinery the
foundations already hold in kind (against).
Two of three legs against: no axis. A
cluster founding is not by itself an axis
(the standing precedent of the far
foundings). This is a Will-posted
taking-in: no seal stands, no score is
computed, and the pre-registered sample,
closed at Paper 036, is untouched.

WHAT IS NEW. Fourteen concepts
(1.2.509-1.2.522), no held concept
revised. Three foundations laid down
(1.3.361-1.3.363) and one defined word
filed (1.3.364). Links: 25 within the
