# Chapter 57 — Paper 039: Thinking by Subtraction (Tang, Gao, Zhao, Ma, Jin, Yang & Zou)

THE DELTA. Concepts 1.2.537-1.2.546 are
new at this chapter (ten): Confidence-
Driven Contrastive Decoding (CCD);
token-level confidence; localized
uncertainty; the low-confidence token;
the semantic anchor; the deliberately
confused reference; confidence-gated
intervention; the dual KV cache; anchor
masking raises the reference's entropy;
trace-level confidence separation. No
held concept is revised. One foundation
is laid down: the quantile threshold
(1.3.368). No word is filed by the
tracker at this chapter.

THE CLUSTER CALL. The filing EXTENDS
cluster AT — the trajectory as its own
reference: contrastive decoding along
the recurrence — founded at Paper 038,
rather than founding a new cluster. The
grounds: the work is a decoding rule of
the same family the cluster was founded
to hold — one model, two distributions
at one step, the choice moved away from
the weaker pole (1.2.525) — the model
untouched, nothing built or kept between
runs. Its two differences from the
founding paper are differences inside
the family, and each is filed as its
own concept rather than as a new
country: the reference is not found in
the trajectory (an earlier state of the
same run) but made, by damaging the
context (1.2.542); and the contrast is
not applied at every step but gated, by
token-level confidence (1.2.543). Held
concept 1.2.525 (contrastive decoding)
is NOT revised: it asserts a form — a
strong distribution moved away from a
weaker, aligned reference — and lists
the known ways of getting a reference as
costing something; this paper is a new
instance of the form and a new way of
getting the reference, and the concept's
assertions stand as written. The new
way is filed at 1.2.542.

