# Chapter 58 — Paper 040: Training-Free Looped Transformers (Chen, Li, Liang, Lao & Liu)

THE DELTA. Concepts 1.2.547-1.2.560 are
new at this chapter (fourteen): the
training-free loop wrapper; the window
residual field; the block as a forward
Euler step; endpoint preservation;
damped sub-stepping; the anchored
Runge-Kutta blend; block-mode iteration;
layer-mode iteration; routing thrash;
the depth fraction rule; non-contraction
of the looped block; the snapshot/restore
cache protocol; the frozen-knowledge
refiner; position-search overfitting. No
held concept is revised. One foundation
is laid down: an explicit Runge-Kutta
method (1.3.369). No word is filed by the
tracker at this chapter. This filing also
carries an addendum at Chapter 50
(50.1.7), written in the same pass: the
step for 1.2.460, tightened by Will's
ruling of 2026-11-21 and owed since; it
moves no held claim and is not part of
this chapter's delta.

THE CLUSTER CALL. The filing EXTENDS
cluster AT — the trajectory as its own
reference — founded at Paper 038 and
extended at Paper 039, rather than
founding a new cluster. The grounds: the
cluster's country is what a recurrent
trajectory makes available at inference,
and this paper works that country from
its other side. Papers 038 and 039 read
references off the trajectory — an
earlier state of the same run, a context
damaged on purpose — to correct a
decoding. This paper corrects the
trajectory itself: it reads the block's
iteration as a numerical integration and
lands it nearer the endpoint the network
was trained to expect (1.2.550), and its
blend is anchored on the trajectory's own
first state (1.2.552) — the trajectory as
its own reference in the integration
sense, as the founding papers made it one
in the decoding sense. Decisively, the
paper manufactures the cluster's founding
object: every looped Transformer the book
held (1.2.523) was trained with its loop
in place, and this work shows the loop
can be retrofitted onto a frozen
checkpoint at test time (1.2.547). The
founding concept's own lineage line
already names this paper ('Chen et
al.'), so the filing is an instance the
held text names, not a change to it:
1.2.523 is NOT revised, and neither is
the recurrent trajectory (1.2.524), whose
states the wrapper's sub-steps simply
sample more finely. The differences from
the founding papers — no contrast,
integration rather than decoding, a base
never trained to loop — are filed as
concepts inside the country, on the
precedent of Paper 039.

THE STRATUM. Paper 040 is a NETWORK
taking-in, the second by reference
traversal: Will directed the corpus's
reference network ingested (2026-11-24),
