# The standoff — Paper 040 (Chapter 58) against the book

Paper 040 extends cluster AT for the
second time, and the standoff is first a
standoff inside the cluster, now three
papers wide. Against LoopCD (1.2.526):
the founding paper presupposes the
trajectory — a model trained to loop,
its states readable as predictions of
rising strength (1.2.530) — and spends
it on a decoding. This paper presupposes
nothing: it builds the trajectory out of
a checkpoint that has none, and spends
it on the forward pass itself,
integrating the block's field to the
endpoint the network expects (1.2.550).
Run the two together and each supplies
the other's premise — the wrapper gives
LoopCD trajectories everywhere; LoopCD
gives the wrapper's trajectories a use
at decode — and the composition is
unrun by anyone (Q194). Against CCD
(1.2.537): Paper 039's method never
touches the forward pass's arithmetic,
only the readout at gated positions;
this paper never touches the readout,
only the arithmetic. The cluster now
holds the full square: the trajectory
found or made, the readout corrected or
the trajectory corrected. The chapter's
concepts link among themselves and back
to the cluster's held ground — the
looped Transformer and its trajectory
above all — and none out of cluster AT.
And the cluster's centre of gravity
shifts with this filing: two of its
three papers now concern how a
trajectory is obtained and integrated,
one how it is read.
Neighbours weighed and held apart, as
at the cluster's founding. The deep
equilibrium line, which the paper cites
and the book does not hold as a country,
is the sharpest contrast: an equilibrium
model's block is trained to be a
contraction, its forward pass a
fixed-point solve; Paper 040's block is
measured not to be one (1.2.557), and
its method exists because the
fixed-point reading fails — the same
mathematical furniture (iteration, fixed
points, Anderson acceleration) priced to
opposite conclusions on opposite ground.
J (the look back inside a run) is held
apart on the founding's grounds, with
the pressure noted: J keeps states for
the forward pass itself, and this paper
is the first in the cluster to change
the forward pass, which brings it
nearest J of the three — held apart
still, because the wrapper keeps no
state across the window's boundary and
reads nothing back; it re-computes, it
does not remember. AP (reasoning kept as
code) is held apart: nothing here is
built, kept, or executed between runs —
the wrapper is a fixed rule, identical
for every input, and the only artifact
of a run is its output. B (a harness
reshaped while running) is held apart:
the model is untouched and unshaped,
and the wrapper wraps the pass without
modifying the machine that runs it.
