# Chapter 60 — Paper 042: LoopCoder-v2 — Only Loop Once (Yang et al.)

THE DELTA. Concepts 1.2.575-1.2.587 are
new at this chapter (thirteen):
LoopCoder-v2; the parallel loop
Transformer; cross-loop parallelism;
shared-KV gated sliding-window
attention; the gain-cost view of loop
count; the non-monotonic loop-count
effect; loop 2 as the principal
refinement site; the intrinsic offset
cost; effective-rank narrowing across
loops; oscillatory refinement; per-loop
diagnostic lenses; the matched
loop-count comparison; latent-explicit
complementarity. No held concept is
revised: the looped Transformer
(1.2.523) and the recurrent trajectory
(1.2.524) are used exactly as held —
the paper's models are instances of the
one and producers of the other. No
foundation is laid down, and no word is
filed by the tracker at this chapter.

THE CLUSTER CALL. The filing EXTENDS
cluster AT — the trajectory as its own
reference — for the third time. The
weighing. The cluster's country, at its
founding and both extensions, is the
recurrent trajectory (1.2.524) of a
looped Transformer (1.2.523): what it
makes available, and what may be done
with it. The founding paper read it to
correct a decoding (1.2.526); Paper 039
gated that correction by confidence
(1.2.537); Paper 040 manufactured the
trajectory where none was trained
(1.2.547) and corrected the trajectory
itself. This paper does none of those
things, and belongs here anyway,
because its object is the trajectory's
own economy: a family of trajectories
trained under one protocol at four loop
counts (1.2.586), opened loop by loop
with a dedicated instrument (1.2.585),
and priced — each loop's refinement
gain against the fixed structural cost
of the parallelism that produced it
(1.2.579, 1.2.582). What it adds that
the cluster's prior members do not
have: (i) the trajectory made parallel
— its states are neighbour-shifted, not
same-token (1.2.577), so the held
picture of a trajectory as one token's
successive refinements gains a second
species, in which each state refines a
neighbour's; (ii) a cost intrinsic to
that species, measured from the states
themselves (1.2.582), where the prior
members' trajectories carried no
per-step price; (iii) a saturation
law for the trajectory's length,
measured not asserted — refinement
concentrates at the first extra loop
(1.2.581) and reverses past it
(1.2.584). AU (the generator as the
optimized artifact) is held apart:
nothing here is a generator, no
property is stated, no program is
rewritten between runs; the loop count
is a trained, deployment-time constant
of each variant, not an artifact an
agent improves. AP (reasoning kept as
code) is held apart: no artifact is
built or kept between runs. The
standoff stands at 60.2.1.

THE STRATUM. Paper 042 is a NETWORK
taking-in: the paper stood at rank 7 of
the reference frontier the corpus's own
bibliographies make (the queue record
in thirst-quest/network/queue.jsonl),
cited by Chapter 56's paper among the
looped families its lineage names. It
is outside the pre-registered sample
(closed at Paper 036); no seal stands
for it and no score is computed.

THE NOVELTY INDEX for this filing is
computed from this delta: thirteen new
canonical concepts of 587 standing
after it, no revisions — 13/587 =
0.0221.

THE AXIS: no. The filing extends a held
cluster on its own ground; no held
claim is re-read and no earlier paper's
substance is reinterpreted. The one
pressure on held ground — the shared
first-loop cache is a look back inside
the run, the nearest approach to
cluster J in the cluster's history — is
recorded at 60.2.2 and held apart
there; a pressure noted is not an axis
turned.

STATE MACHINES: two are added at this
filing, both stated in the work (the
PLT forward pass of its Appendix A; the
loop-count selection diagnostic of its
Sections 3.2 and 5), bringing the held
count to 202 (173 stated, 29 inferred).

RESTRUCTURING: Restructure Pass #26
falls due at this filing and FIRES in
