# Chapter 61 — Paper 043: Bridging the Gap Between Latent and Explicit Reasoning with Looped Transformers (Fan, Svete & Lee)

THE DELTA. Concepts 1.2.588-1.2.599 are
new at this chapter (twelve): LOTUS;
the latent-explicit gap at scale; the
padded latent prefix; step-aligned
parallel supervision; parallel chain
likelihood; coverage and selection; the
input-injected recurrence; LOTUS-aux;
the supervision readout schedule; the
gold-chain readout; mass on unseen
valid chains; inference-time budget
adaptation. No held concept is revised:
the looped Transformer (1.2.523) and
the recurrent trajectory (1.2.524) are
used exactly as held — the paper's
backbone is an instance of the one and
its latent blocks produce the other,
under a training regime neither scroll
speaks to. No foundation is laid down,
and no word is filed by the tracker at
this chapter.

THE CLUSTER CALL. The filing EXTENDS
cluster AT — the trajectory as its own
reference — for the fourth time. The
weighing. The cluster's country, at its
founding and three extensions, is the
recurrent trajectory (1.2.524) of a
looped Transformer (1.2.523): what it
makes available, and what may be done
with it. The founding paper read it at
inference to correct a decoding
(1.2.526); Paper 039 gated that
correction by confidence (1.2.537);
Paper 040 manufactured the trajectory
on a frozen checkpoint and integrated
it (1.2.547); Paper 042 audited it loop
by loop and priced it (1.2.582). Every
prior member takes the trajectory as
found — a by-product of a model trained
for something else. This paper trains
the trajectory itself: its latent
blocks are supervised, during training
and through the model's own LM head,
against the gold CoT tokens of the
steps they are pinned to (1.2.591), so
that the trajectory comes to hold a
specific symbolic chain. What it adds
that the cluster's prior members do not
have: (i) a trajectory whose positions
carry fixed external referents — the
blocks form a grid aligned
position-by-position to a gold chain
(1.2.590), where the prior trajectories
are per-token state sequences whose
positions mean only their place in the
run; (ii) the trajectory grounded at
training time by direct readout — the
prior members read the trajectory at
inference (contrasted, lensed,
integrated), and none trains it against
a chain; (iii) the trajectory's
legibility as a measured property — the
chain read back through the model's own
head (1.2.597), and more than the chain
(1.2.598) — where the prior members
assume the trajectory's contents
matter without reading them. AU (the
generator as the optimized artifact) is
held apart: no generator is rewritten
between runs against a stated property;
the supervision target is a fixed gold
chain and the artifact fitted is the
model, by ordinary training. AP
(reasoning kept as code) is held apart:
nothing is built or kept between runs —
the latents are consumed by the answer
and discarded. The standoff stands at
61.2.1.

THE STRATUM. Paper 043 is a NETWORK
taking-in: the paper stood at rank 8 of
the reference frontier the corpus's own
bibliographies make (the queue record
in thirst-quest/network/queue.jsonl),
cited by Chapter 56's paper among the
latent-reasoning methods its lineage
names. It is outside the pre-registered
sample (closed at Paper 036); no seal
stands for it and no score is computed.

THE NOVELTY INDEX for this filing is
computed from this delta: twelve new
canonical concepts of 599 standing
after it, no revisions — 12/599 =
0.0200.

THE AXIS: no. The filing extends a held
cluster on its own ground; no held
claim is re-read and no earlier paper's
substance is reinterpreted. The one
pressure on held ground — the prefix
cache, computed once and attended by
