CAVEATS ON THIS FILING. (i) Table 3's
printed speedup, 6.9x, stands a
half-step above the ratio of its own
printed latencies: 963.6/140.8 = 6.84.
A mean of per-example ratios would
legitimately differ from the ratio of
means, and the text does not say which
was computed; the filing rests nothing
on the second digit — the claim the
concept (1.2.588) carries is the order
of the speedup, and the math-expression
setting's 2.5x recomputes exactly. (ii)
The contributions bullet's 'within 1
point of explicit CoT' is exact for
LOTUS + CODI (70.6 against 71.5) but
LOTUS alone stands 1.5 points away
(70.0); Section 4.2 states both numbers
carefully — 'within ~1.5 points' for
LOTUS, the tightening to within 1
credited to the CODI-augmented variant
— and the filing's gap concept
(1.2.589) is worded from Section 4.2
and Table 1, not from the bullet. (iii)
Section 4.3.2's training-sweep
paragraph cites Table 6 for the
training-time loop sweep whose numbers
stand in Table 5 (14.6 at R = 2 rising
to 70.0 at R = 6); the inference
sweep's citation of Table 6 is correct.
A mis-pointed reference; the numbers
themselves are consistent in both
tables and in the prose. (iv) All
results stand attributed: the training
runs (385k examples, thirty epochs,
three backbones, latency on one H100)
are beyond house reproduction, and the
released code stands unrun by the
house; only the printed arithmetic was
recomputed. (v) The filing reads v1
(30 June 2026); a v2 stands on arXiv
(13 July 2026), unread here — if the
revision moves a number this chapter
rests on, the delta belongs to a later
pass. No False filing: the one failed
