# Chapter 65 — Paper 047: RLTT (Williams & Tureci)

THE DELTA. Twelve concepts
(1.2.635-1.2.646), no revision of held
concepts, no foundation laid, no word
coined, and a cluster extended: CLUSTER
AT — THE TRAJECTORY AS ITS OWN
REFERENCE — EXTENDED, its eighth
paper.
The paper's iterated object is the
recurrent trajectory (1.2.524), this
time at training time and whole: a
looped model's per-token sequence of
next-token distributions across its
loops — the latent thought distribution
trajectory (1.2.636). Every earlier
member of the cluster works the
trajectory at inference or in
construction: the founding paper reads
its states, Paper 039 gates a contrast
by its confidence, Paper 040
manufactures the recurrence, Paper 042
audits its loops, Paper 043 aligns its
steps to a gold chain, Paper 044 reads
a verdict off its prefixes, Paper 046
constructs its steps. This paper
rewards it. RLTT (1.2.635) takes the
one outcome reward a rollout earns —
its final answer right or wrong — and
distributes it across every loop by
trajectory-level credit assignment
(1.2.637), repairing the defect it
names in the standard objective:
terminal-only credit (1.2.638), which
rewards the last loop as if each token
had been decided in one step. It is
the cluster's second training-time
member, after Paper 043, and its first
reinforcement-learning one. Cluster AV
was weighed and held apart: nothing
denoises and no thought space is
learned — the backbone is a looped
transformer and the trajectory is the
recurrence itself. The J question the
walk carried out of Chapters 62, 63
and 64 is weighed with it at 65.2.2:
the reward is read off the emitted
answer against the answer key, never
off the trajectory, and no loop is
scored — the trajectory is credited as
one object, which is this cluster's
definition, not the oracle's. AU, AP
and AC are also weighed and held apart
at 65.2.2.

THE STRATUM. A network taking-in, leg 9
of the reference walk Will directed on
2026-11-24: the paper stood at rank 12
of the reference frontier, cited by
Chapter 56's paper (LoopCD) in its
bibliography. The queue record carried
no identifier; the paper was identified
by title and authors in one web search
— 'Prioritize the Process, Not Just
the Outcome: Rewarding Latent Thought
Trajectories Improves Reasoning in
Looped Language Models',
arXiv:2602.10520 — and one fetch bought
the paper entire. No rank was skipped.
One correction to the frontier's own
record belongs here: the queue named
three authors, but the byline of the
version filed (v1) carries two —
Jonathan Williams and Esin Tureci;
Olga Russakovsky is thanked in v1's
acknowledgments and stands as third
author of the ICML 2026 proceedings
version (65.1.4). Outside the
pre-registered sample (it closed at
Paper 036): no seal, no score.

NOVELTY INDEX. 12/646 = 0.0186, by the
house method.

THE AXIS. Judged NO, in writing: the
paper deepens a country the map
already holds — the eighth member of
its founding cluster, on the
architecture family the citing chapter
already surveys. That its act is new
to the cluster (no member had trained
the trajectory by reward) makes it a
wide extension, not an axis: the axis
the detector watches is a paper's
relation to the model's fixed point,
and this one's delta is distance
covered inside known ground.

