# Chapter 66 — Paper 048: Scaling up Test-Time Compute with Latent Reasoning (Geiping et al.)

THE DELTA. Twelve concepts
(1.2.647-1.2.658), no revision of held
concepts, no foundation laid, no word
coined, and a cluster extended: CLUSTER
AT — THE TRAJECTORY AS ITS OWN
REFERENCE — EXTENDED, its ninth
paper.
The paper's iterated object is the
recurrent trajectory (1.2.524) — the
same object every member of the
cluster works — but this paper is the
one that brings the trajectory into
existence: it pretrains the
recurrent-depth architecture at scale
(Huginn, 1.2.647), with sampled-depth
training (1.2.648) under the
log-normal Poisson depth law
(1.2.649) and truncated
backpropagation (1.2.650), and then
reads the trajectory's emergent
properties off the trained model —
path independence (1.2.651), the
convergence exit (1.2.653), state
carryover (1.2.655), the latent
trajectory geometries (1.2.657).
Every earlier member presupposes this
ground: Chapter 56's paper reads the
states of models in this family,
Chapter 62 takes Huginn itself as its
base model, and Chapters 64 and 65
train trajectories of the same
species. The walk met the inhabitants
before the house; the filing records
the substrate arriving ninth, out of
the field's order, and the lateness
is the map's, not the work's — in the
field this paper (February 2025)
precedes every other member of its
cluster. Cluster AV was weighed and
held apart on the paper's own
evidence: its Remark 3.1 asks whether
this is a diffusion model and answers
in the design — noise injected into
the state does not help, and a
step-conditioned core interacts badly
with path independence; nothing
denoises and no thought space is
learned. The J question the walk
carried out of Chapters 62, 63, 64
and 65 is weighed with it at 66.2.2:
the paper's halting signal reads only
the trajectory's own successive
states and returns stop-or-continue,
not a verdict, and its speculative
verifier is the same trajectory at
greater depth — the condition is not
crossed. AU, AP and AC are also
weighed and held apart at 66.2.2.

THE STRATUM. A network taking-in, leg
10 of the reference walk Will directed
on 2026-11-24: the paper stood at
rank 13 of the reference frontier,
cited by Chapter 56's paper (LoopCD)
in its bibliography. The queue record
carried the arXiv identifier and no
title or authors; the listing named
the work — 'Scaling up Test-Time
Compute with Latent Reasoning: A
Recurrent Depth Approach',
arXiv:2502.05171 — and one fetch
bought the paper entire. No rank was
skipped. The version filed is v1
(7 February 2025); the listing
carries a v2 of 17 February 2025,
noted at 66.1.4, and the work later
appears in the NeurIPS 2025
proceedings. Outside the
pre-registered sample (it closed at
Paper 036): no seal, no score.

NOVELTY INDEX. 12/658 = 0.0182, by the
house method.

THE AXIS. Judged NO, in writing: the
paper is the presupposed substrate of
a cluster that already stands — the
trajectory concept (1.2.524) and the
cluster were founded from this work's
descendants, and the filing deepens
the founding ground rather than
opening new ground. Priority in the
field is not priority in the map: an
axis is a new dimension of the
tracker, and a foundation arriving
late is still a foundation, not a
