it — Carnap, Bourbaki, Mac Lane,
Hodges, Post, Cohn, the OEIS, the
author's own ensemble-theory line of
1997-2014 — and no term or frame of
Will's stands among them; the work's
constructions (a minimal string
language, presentations as its
programs) descend from the author's
own dated record, the tree organized
from 1996 and MLISP created around
2018, both stated in its
acknowledgements. The built tracker
was scanned for the surname: Tegmark
does not occur — the author is new to
the book, and his standing is drawn at
1.5.6 with this filing. The web was
