# 70.2.1 — The instrument filed

THE INSTRUMENT FILED. [synthesis] For
fifty-one papers this book filed claims
about trajectories and took their
numbers on instruments it had never
filed. The AIME numbers of the walk —
LoopCD's 49.58 rising to 56.88 on this
set, CCD's twelve cells, RLTT's gains
on its sibling — are counts of
agreements with thirty strings in two
files, and until this chapter the
strings stood outside the book, in a
repository the walk pointed at but did
not hold. Filing the key changes what
those numbers are here: readings
against a held and audited table, not
decorations on other papers' claims —
and the audit repaid most of the
borrowing (1.2.708): twenty-two of the
thirty entries now stand in the book
with derivations of the house's own
behind them, which makes this
thirty-row artifact, improbably, the
most-verified object in the tracker.

The inversion against Chapter 69 is
worth the record. There the territory
testified about the map in the
territory's own language — the strings
ran. Here the measure is mute: a key
cannot testify about itself, and the
only testimony available was
recomputation, the house solving the
examination the way the measured
models are asked to. And the filing
catches the instrument mid-decay: the
same pass that verifies the key finds
its rows already standing as training
samples in the wild (1.2.704), so the
book files the yardstick at the moment
its readings begin, irrevocably, to
mix memory with reasoning — and every
future number reported against it in
these chapters will carry that mixture
unnamed unless the filing names it
(Q244).
# 70.2.2 — Cluster placement

Cluster AY is FOUNDED — THE ANSWER KEY:
THE MEASURE AS A FIXED TABLE — its
first paper. The founding is made at
the level of the artifact itself: a
benchmark is a fixed table of problems
and verdicts, published as data, and
the cluster is the country of such
tables — the instruments the rest of
the book is measured with.

Cluster AT held apart, and weighed
first because Chapter 56 — the citing
paper — founds it. AT's members perform
acts on a recurrent trajectory and
report the outcomes against this
artifact's key; the artifact performs
no act and holds no trajectory. To file
the yardstick among the measured would
confuse the instrument with its object:
every AT number in the book is a count
of agreements with this table, and the
table is not one of the things counted.

Cluster O weighed and held apart. O is
the statistics of judging — pricing a
rule from a record of another rule, the
held-out grade and its corrections
(1.2.110-1.2.116). The benchmark is the
held-out material such judging
consumes: O files the pricing of
judges, this filing files the judged
set itself. The two meet at 1.2.111's
easy judge — hold back part of the
data, grade on it — of which this
artifact is the held-back part,
published and frozen; but a procedure
and its material are different
countries, and the grain (1.2.705) is
the material's property, not the
procedure's.

Cluster J weighed — the crossing
condition of 62.2.2, weighed again.
The condition: a mechanism consults a
reference distinct from the thing
judged, for a verdict whose evidence
lies beyond the judged object. This
filing's object is the reference
itself: the answer key is a stored
table of correct answers — the third
device the condition's own falsifiable
form names (68.2.2) — and every scoring
of every model against it is a
consultation of exactly the condition's
shape. NOT CROSSED, on a distinction
the filing states plainly: the
condition governs mechanisms, and this
work contains none — it judges nothing,
consults nothing, and is consulted by
everything. The seam does not move;
but it has a resident on its far side
now. Stated falsifiably, as the seam
requires: a filing whose mechanism
consulted this table — or any key —
inside its computation, rather than at
its grading, would cross, and the
question of who files that crossing is
opened as Q242.

Clusters AV, AW and AX held apart. AV:
nothing is generated and no latent
space is traversed — the artifact's
rows are read, not denoised into being.
AW: the survey describes a field's
papers; this artifact describes
nothing — it is thirty problems and
thirty answers, and contains no prose
about any work, including itself. AX:
the artifact is strings, but AX's
strings run, and these do not — they
are compared; the corpus of Chapter 69
computes its content, this corpus
withholds its (the solutions are not
in it), and a table whose strings are
verdicts is a different country from a
corpus whose strings are programs.
Cluster AK brushed only: the rows ride
in a format, but no format claim is
made or carried — the artifact would
survive translation into any format
unchanged, which is AK's test from the
other side.
