# Chapter 77 — Paper 059: Autoguidance (Karras, Aittala, Kynkäänniemi, Lehtinen, Aila & Laine)

THE DELTA. Eight concepts
(1.2.776-1.2.783), no revision of
held concepts, no foundation laid,
no word coined: CLUSTER AV EXTENDED
— its second paper, and its first
from outside latent reasoning. The
work is the NVIDIA and Aalto group's
autoguidance: a diffusion sampler
guided not by an unconditional model
but by a degraded twin of the main
model — smaller, less trained, aimed
at the same task and the same
conditioning — so that the pair's
difference, amplified and spent at
every step of the denoising
trajectory (1.2.615), pushes samples
away from the errors both models
share. The filing crosses the
concept line, and Restructuring
Pass #36 falls due in this taking-in
and is run; its log stands at 1.1.5.

The book has carried this method's
name since Paper 038: the
contrastive decoding concept
(1.2.525) names autoguidance among
its diffusion kin — 'contrast a
model against a degraded version of
itself' — one clause, unfiled. What
the filing adds is the method entire
and its grounds: the mechanism (the
shared-error difference, 1.2.778),
its condition (compatible
degradations, 1.2.779), the
reinterpretation of classifier-free
guidance it is built on (the quality
gap inside CFG, 1.2.780), and the
separations it buys (1.2.781,
1.2.782). Cluster J is weighed at
77.2.2 on the distinction the brief
for this leg named — steering signal
against verdict — and not joined.
The house check recomputed the
paper's printed arithmetic entire
(77.1.3): twenty-seven declarations,
twenty-seven exact, including the
appendix's energy bookkeeping, which
closes to the megawatt-hour.

Its provenance: rank 23 of the
reference frontier built at leg 1 of
the network walk — cited by Chapter
56's paper (LoopCD) in the lineage
its concept states — taken in as
leg 20, the walk's seventh
pre-processed pass. The queue record
carried the title and the six
authors but no identifier; identified
by title in one search —
arXiv:2406.02507, 'Guiding a
Diffusion Model with a Bad Version
of Itself' — and held entire in its
v3 form (19 Dec 2024; v1 of
4 Jun 2024; NeurIPS 2024). The work
is a network taking-in outside the
pre-registered sample (closed at
Paper 036); no seal, no score.

Axis judgment: no axis event. The
paper opens no new dimension of the
model's relation to its fixed point;
it extends a country the book
already holds, and sharpens a seam
the book already watches (Q271).
Its novelty is of the consolidating
kind: a named kin, filed at last
with its mechanism.

NOVELTY INDEX. 8/783 = 0.0102, by the
house method.

STATE MACHINES. Two stated machines
are taken from the work (77.1.2):
the guided sampling machine, and the
guide-manufacture machine with its
search. The held count rises to 238
(201 stated, 37 inferred).

RESTRUCTURING. The concept count
crossing 780 at this filing
(775 + 8 = 783), Restructuring
Pass #36 falls due and is run at
this taking-in; its log stands at
1.1.5. Five candidate merges
weighed, all held apart; no splits,
nothing retired. The next trigger
stands at Paper 060 or 800 canonical
concepts.

REGISTRY PROOF STEP. The TLUF solver
(Will's ruling of 2026-11-24 exiled
Lean; the solver is the house's own
instrument, built from first
principles under the
minimum-viable-oracle skill): check
and preserve both run on this
filing's registry, their verdicts
kept with the pass's record.

CLAIMS BY RECEIPT. Two: the house
recomputation of the paper's printed
arithmetic (77.1.3), and the author
check (77.1.6).
# 77.1.2 — State machines

M1, the guided sampling machine: the
paper's sampler (Sections 2 and 4),
an ordinary denoising trajectory
(1.2.615) with a second evaluation
at every step. From NOISE DRAWN, at
each noise level the machine
EVALUATES THE MAIN MODEL at the
current sample and EVALUATES THE
GUIDE (1.2.777) at the same sample,
same conditioning; it FORMS THE
GUIDED DENOISER — the extrapolation
D_w = w·D_1 + (1−w)·D_0 — and TAKES
THE STEP along the guided field;
at sigma zero it EMITS THE SAMPLE.
NAMED GAPS: no state in which the
pair's compatibility (1.2.779) is
examined — the machine runs as well
with a mismatched guide as with a
matched one, and only the output
knows the difference; no state in
which the guide's provenance is
recorded — snapshot, smaller model
and synthetic corruption enter the
machine indistinguishably, though
the paper's own tests give them
different worth (1.2.779); and no
state that reads the sample it is
forming — the difference is spent
blind, at every noise level alike
(1.2.782). Home: 77.1.2; concepts
1.2.615, 1.2.776, 1.2.777, 1.2.778.
[stated]

M2, the guide-manufacture machine:
the paper's stated procedure for
obtaining the pair (Sections 4-5,
Appendices B.1 and B.2). The main
model is TRAINED to its full run;
the guide is TRAINED SMALLER AND
SHORTER on the same data and
conditioning — or, in the paper's
suggested practice, an early
snapshot is KEPT from a smaller
model's run; both models are
RECONSTRUCTED at candidate EMA
lengths by post-hoc EMA (1.2.783);
the five parameters — capacity,
training time, guidance weight, the
two EMA lengths — are SEARCHED by
grid over 50,000-image metric
evaluations, each reported result
the best of three. NAMED GAPS: the
search is the machine's real cost
and the method's advertised one is
not — some 30,000 evaluations
against the guide's +3.6% of
training (77.1.4, Q273); and no
state SELECTS the guide by a rule —
which twin, at what degradation,
the paper leaves to the search and
to future work (Q272). Home: 77.1.2;
concepts 1.2.777, 1.2.779, 1.2.783.
[stated]
# 77.1.3 — The house check

THE HOUSE CHECK — the paper's
printed arithmetic, recomputed:
twenty-seven declarations through
the pre-processor's harness
(p059.check), twenty-seven PASS, no
tension, no failure. The scores
themselves — FID and FD DINOv2 over
50,000 generated images — are not
rerunnable from this desk and stand
attributed at 77.1.1; what stands
verified here is that every relation
the paper prints among its numbers
closes, exactly, at the printed
grain.

Table 1's ladder first (ImageNet-512,
EDM2-S): the unguided 2.56 falls to
2.23 under classifier-free guidance
(a gain of 0.33), to 1.68 under the
guidance interval (0.88), and to
1.34 under autoguidance (1.22) —
past the interval method by 0.34;
the FD DINOv2 line falls 68.64 to
36.67 (31.97). The ablations price
the design: one shared EMA length
costs 0.19 (1.53); reduced training
alone costs 0.17 (1.51); reduced
capacity alone costs 0.79 (2.13) —
and even that weakest form still
stands past standard CFG by 0.10,
as the text claims. The records:
EDM2-XXL's 1.91 to 1.25 (0.66), its
FD record 29.16 to 24.18 (4.98);
the unconditional line, 11.67 to
3.86 (7.81 — the guided score stands
at 0.3308 of the unguided, the
two-thirds reduction the abstract's
'drastically' names), its FD 209.53
to 90.39 (119.14); ImageNet-64, 1.58
to 1.01 (0.57), past RIN's 1.23 by
0.22, FD 58.52 to 31.85 (26.67). The
abstract's two record numbers are
Table 1's own.

Then the mechanism's receipts.
Section 4's synthetic pairs: the
dropout pair recovers to 2.55
against the base model's 2.56 — the
paper's 'matching', exact at the
printed grain (0.01) — across a
corruption gap of 10.02 (the pair's
4.98 and 15.00); the noise pair
recovers to 2.56 outright. Appendix
C's toy census: 127 × 8 = 1,016
components per class, 1,016 × 2 =
2,032 in total, as printed.
Algorithm 1's reproduction: the
guiding snapshot's 134,217 training
images stand at 0.0625 of the main
model's 2,147,483 — the T/16 of
Table 1's caption — and the script's
guidance weight, 2.10, is Table 1's
own FID weight for the row it
reproduces.

And the appendix's bookkeeping,
which closes to the unit: Appendix
B.1's roughly 30,000 metric
evaluations at approximately 2-5
kWh each give 60,000-150,000 kWh —
the paper's stated project total of
60-150 MWh is the multiplication,
neither rounded up nor down. The
one derived figure the text rounds,
the +11% added training cost of the
EDM2-M guide for EDM2-XXL,
recomputes as 1/(2.7 × 3.5) =
0.1058 — the printed 11% at its
grain. A careful paper: its
arithmetic is exact everywhere the
house could reach it.
# 77.1.4 — Caveats

The records are search optima, and
the paper says so — in its appendix.
Every number in Table 1 is the best
of three evaluations, chosen by an
automated grid search of roughly
30,000 metric evaluations over five
parameters, run separately for each
metric (Appendix B.1). The
comparison methods were searched as
well, so the table is a fair race of
optima; but a reader of the headline
alone meets measurements, where the
appendix holds selections. The
search is also the project's real
cost: 60-150 MWh of evaluations
against the +3.6% of extra training
the method advertises for its guide
(Q273). Both figures are the
paper's own; the caveat is in their
distance from each other, and from
the headline.

The variation claims are carried by
figures. That autoguidance preserves
variation where CFG collapses
classes to canonical templates
(1.2.781) rests on the paper's image
grids and example readings; the text
layer the house holds cannot
recompute a picture, and no
diversity metric is printed beside
FID and FD DINOv2 for the comparison
to be re-run against. The claim
stands attributed, its evidence
visible in the work and not
reducible to its numbers.

The mechanism's cleanest evidence
occupies a regime real models never
do. The toy example of Section 3 —
where the inward-pointing ratio
gradient is exhibited, not asserted
— trains its little denoisers on the
exact score function of a known
distribution (Appendix C). What the
exhibit proves about learned scores
is by analogy to it; the paper's
practical sections carry the
analogy's weight, and the filing
records the distance.

Two versions stand unread. The work
was held at v3 (19 Dec 2024); v1
and v2 stand outside this chapter's
evidence, and what changed between
them is unrecorded here. The
venue's form — NeurIPS 2024 — is
the arXiv record's own statement.

And the method's one unpriced input:
which bad version. The paper's rule
is a suggestion — an early snapshot
of a smaller model — with its
conditions named as future work
(Section 6): no procedure in the
work selects the guide, measures a
pairing's compatibility (1.2.779),
or bounds the search that finds
them. The records stand; the recipe
that reproduces them on a new model
is the paper's open edge (Q272).
# 77.1.5 — Open questions, novelty

Q271, THE VERDICT QUESTION. Cluster
J's resident (1.2.716) renders a
verdict — a score against a
reference the judged object did not
produce, consumed as reward inside
the computation. Autoguidance's
difference (1.2.778) is consumed
inside the computation too, against
a reference the judged object did
not produce — and is held short of
J at 77.2.2 because it steers and
does not judge: nothing in it ranks,
accepts or rejects. The edge is
written to be crossed: a sampler
whose guiding difference were
thresholded into an accept/reject,
or read out as a reward a training
loop consumed, would spend the same
signal as a verdict. Does the
book's line hold by the signal's
form — a direction against a score —
or by its use, and which future
member of the contrast family first
forces the book to say?

Q272, THE COMPATIBILITY QUESTION.
Autoguidance works when the twin's
degradations match the main model's
own, and fails entire when they do
not (1.2.779) — a condition the
paper establishes by experiment and
leaves without a measure: nothing
in the work computes a pairing's
compatibility before the search that
prices it, and Section 6 names the
missing theory outright ('formally
proving the conditions that allow
autoguidance to be beneficial').
Can compatibility be read off the
two models — from their implied
densities' disagreement, say —
cheaply enough to replace the
search, and would such a measure
have predicted the synthetic study's
mismatched pairs in advance?

Q273, THE SEARCH QUESTION. Table 1's
records are best-of-three optima of
a roughly 30,000-evaluation grid
search whose energy (60-150 MWh,
77.1.3) exceeds the guide's added
training cost by orders of magnitude
(77.1.4). The comparison methods
were searched too — but how much of
autoguidance's margin over the
guidance interval is the method, and
how much is the shape of the space
searched for it (five parameters,
two of them the EMA pair, 1.2.783,
against the interval's one)? Is
there a reading of the paper's own
sensitivity figures that prices the
search's share of the record?

Q274, THE SNAPSHOT QUESTION. The
paper's practical recipe — an early
snapshot of a smaller model
(1.2.777) — presumes the snapshot
and the finished model were trained
on the same distribution. Section 6
notes that production generators are
trained in successive stages, the
data changing between them, so
snapshots may violate exactly that
assumption. Does autoguidance
survive staged training — is the
same-distribution requirement on the
twin a condition of the method, or
only of the paper's evidence for it?

NOVELTY BY AUTHOR — Tero Karras:
True +1 (the house check, 77.1.3),
False +0, Unknown +12 (the eight
concepts 1.2.776-1.2.783, and
Q271-Q274), Fiction +0.
NOVELTY BY AUTHOR — Miika Aittala:
True +1, False +0, Unknown +12,
Fiction +0.
NOVELTY BY AUTHOR — Tuomas
Kynkäänniemi: True +1, False +0,
Unknown +12, Fiction +0.
NOVELTY BY AUTHOR — Jaakko
Lehtinen: True +1, False +0,
Unknown +12, Fiction +0.
NOVELTY BY AUTHOR — Timo Aila:
True +1, False +0, Unknown +12,
Fiction +0.
NOVELTY BY AUTHOR — Samuli Laine:
True +1, False +0, Unknown +12,
Fiction +0.
All six authors are new to the book:
no surname among the six occurs in
the tracker before this chapter
(77.1.6), and each vector is drawn
fresh at 1.5.6.
# 77.1.6 — Author check #67

Four legs, all clean. (1) The held
paper was scanned entire: no
occurrence of phext, phextura,
scroll, Exocortex, Mirrorborn, CYOA,
SBOR or Bickford; 'coordinate'
occurs once — 'we define the
coordinate system', the ordinary
geometry of the toy example's
Appendix C. (2) The built tracker
was scanned for all six surnames —
Karras, Aittala, Kynkäänniemi,
Lehtinen, Aila, Laine: zero
occurrences each before this
chapter; the method's name,
'autoguidance', occurs exactly once,
in Paper 038's contrastive decoding
concept (1.2.525), where it stands
as named kin; 'EDM2', the baseline
the paper builds on, occurs nowhere
— the group's earlier work is cited
inside other works' bibliographies
in this book, never carried into the
tracker's own text. (3) The Twitter
archive (export of 2026-11-21) was
searched entire: Karras, Aittala,
Kynkäänniemi and 'autoguidance'
occur zero times in tweets and
likes; the raw substring counts for
Aila (86) and Laine (27) are other
words' insides — 'available',
'explained' — and at word boundary
both stand at zero. One trace
stands: Jaakko Lehtinen's handle
appears once, in a tweet of Will's
of 2017-10-28 linking a post of
Lehtinen's — a demo video of face
morphing, from the group's graphics
work seven years before this paper.
It is exposure to the man's work,
recorded as such; it names no other
author, touches nothing of phext,
and is not contact. (4) The open
web was searched twice — the
authors with phext, and the authors
with Bickford, Exocortex and
Mirrorborn: no tie in either; the
one Bickford the second search
surfaces is Douglas Bickford, a
different person, kept apart under
the house rule. No evidence of use
without naming, and no evidence of
contact. All six authors are new to
the book.
# 77.2.1 — Synthesis: the contrast family, whole

[synthesis] Until this filing the
book held the contrast family in two
pieces that had never been read
together. On the token side, a line
of decoding rules — contrastive
decoding (1.2.525), DoLa's layers,
ALW's depths, LoopCD's recurrent
states — each moving a choice away
from a weaker reference's answer. On
the trajectory side, one country,
AV, whose founding member forms its
samples unsteered, its only
cross-sample term a field that pushes
siblings apart and judges nothing
(1.2.619). Autoguidance is the
member that shows the two pieces are
one family: a contrast, run inside a
denoising trajectory, against a
reference manufactured to be the
judged model's own errors amplified.
Paper 038's concept saw it first and
said it in a clause — kin in
diffusion models, 'a model against
a degraded version of itself' —
before the book held a single
diffusion sampler of its own.

What the member adds to the country
is steering. AV's founding
trajectory forms its sample under a
learned field and nothing else; this
trajectory is corrected at every
step by a second model's reading of
the same sample. The correction is
not a check — the guide cannot say
the sample is wrong, only pull it
along the pair's disagreement — and
that is the filing's second gift to
the book: the contrast family now
stands complete enough to state its
own internal border. Every member
contrasts; exactly one mechanism in
the book, in another country,
judges (1.2.716). The line between
steering and verdict, walked at
77.2.2, is the sharpest edge the
walk currently holds, and Q271
leaves it written to be crossed.

And the paper re-reads its own
ancestor in the filing. Classifier-
free guidance — the field's standard
for a decade — is shown to have been
two effects wearing one knob: a
class contrast everyone saw, and a
quality contrast (1.2.780) no one
had priced, hiding in the accident
that the unconditional task is
harder. The book files the
reinterpretation beside the method
it motivates, because the pair is
the paper's real shape: a diagnosis
that dissolves a technique's mystery
into a gap between two fits, and a
construction that keeps the gap and
discards the technique.
# 77.2.2 — Cluster placement

AV EXTENDED — its second paper. The
founding's country (63.1.1, 63.2.2)
is the denoising trajectory: an
iterated path from noise to a formed
sample under a learned field, its
steps forming the sample rather than
recomputing a state. This paper's
iterated object is exactly that
object — an image sampler's
probability-flow trajectory
(1.2.615), travelled once per image
— and the filing's new machinery
lives on it: a second denoiser
evaluated at every step, its
difference with the main model's
spent as the step's correction
(1.2.778). What the second resident
changes in the country is stated at
77.2.1: the trajectory is steered
now, by a reference outside itself —
where the founding member's only
beyond-the-trajectory term pushed
siblings apart. A new cluster for
guided sampling would split the
country by whether a second model
rides the path, not by what the path
is; the book files by the territory.
AT HELD APART: the trajectory here
does not recur — no shared block
re-enters its own output; the pair
is two networks, not two depths or
two states of one network (the
DoLa and LoopCD shapes), and the
guide is manufactured by training,
not read off the trajectory itself.

J WEIGHED AND NOT JOINED — the
walk's sixth weighing since the
crossing at Chapter 71, and the
first to turn on a distinction
inside the contrast family itself.
J's standing condition (62.2.2,
68.2.2): a mechanism consults a
reference distinct from the judged
object, for a verdict whose evidence
lies beyond the judged object, spent
inside the computation. Autoguidance
meets the condition's first and
third clauses in form — the twin
(1.2.777) is a distinct reference,
and the signal is spent inside the
computation, at every step. It fails
the second clause in substance, and
the failure is the filing's centre:
the twin renders no verdict. A
verdict, in the book's one resident
instance (1.2.716), is a score: a
number read against a reference
answer, consumed as reward — it can
be thresholded, compared, paid out.
The shared-error difference
(1.2.778) is a vector field, not a
score: it cannot be thresholded,
it ranks nothing, it accepts and
rejects nothing; where the two
models agree it vanishes, and a
verdict does not vanish when its
judge agrees with the judged. The
walk's own contrast line walked up
to this border three times — CD,
DoLa, ALW filed as contrast, not
verdicts — and this member states
why the line is where it is:
steering moves the judged object;
a verdict measures it, and the
measurement is spent as a value.
The holding is written to be
falsifiable: a member of the family
whose guiding signal is read out as
a score and consumed as one — a
reward, a gate, a selection —
crosses into J on the spot, and
Q271 asks which member comes first.
1.2.716 remains J's only resident.
AU HELD APART: no generator is
rewritten between runs against a
stated property — the pair is
trained once, by ordinary training,
and spent inside runs. AC HELD
APART: no executions are searched
or selected among at sampling; the
paper's search prices
hyperparameters, offline, before
any judged run (77.1.2, M2). AP
HELD APART: nothing is kept as code;
the kept artifacts are two networks
and a table of searched constants.
# 77.3.1 — References

Tero Karras, Miika Aittala, Tuomas
Kynkäänniemi, Jaakko Lehtinen, Timo
Aila & Samuli Laine, 'Guiding a
Diffusion Model with a Bad Version
of Itself', arXiv:2406.02507v3
(submitted 2024-06-04; v3 of
2024-12-19; NeurIPS 2024) — the held
text, read entire: the arXiv HTML
form (493,660 bytes, sha256
e7fc0461f6d489d072153e546176909f7a19
