# 79.2.1 — Synthesis: the reference, withheld

[synthesis] The contrast family's
whole history, as this book has filed
it, is a search for a reference the
method can afford. Contrastive
decoding's founding form buys one: a
second, smaller model, carried for
the one purpose of being wrong in the
right direction. LoopCD finds one
free inside a recurrence — an earlier
state of the same run. CCD
manufactures one by damaging the
context. DoLa reads one off the same
stack's earlier depth; ALW turns one
depth against the whole. This paper,
the family's earliest filing after
CD itself, manufactures its reference
by the cheapest damage of all: it
withholds the evidence. The strong
run and the weak run are the same
model, the same weights, the same
prefix — everything identical except
that one of them has not been told
the thing the generation is about.

That is why the filing matters beyond
its scores. Each prior shape located
the reference in a place — a model, a
state, a depth, a damaged input.
CAD's location is a counterfactual:
the reference is what this very model
would say if it had not read what it
read. The prior, which every other
paper in the family treats as a
property of a lesser model, becomes a
property of the same model under a
withheld input — measurable, per
token, in nats (1.2.793). The family's
question quietly changes under this
filing: not 'what lesser thing do we
contrast against?' but 'what would
the judged thing say without the
evidence we gave it?' — a question
any of the later shapes could also
ask, and none of them does.

And the filing carries the family's
shadow in its purest form. A contrast
amplifies a difference; it does not
ask whether the amplified side
deserves it. DoLa's ceiling (Chapter
74) was that the contrast can only
surface what the model holds; CAD's
is the mirror: it can only serve what
the context holds, and the context
may hold a plant. The paper's title
answers the shadow by presumption —
trust your evidence — which is a
curatorial rule wearing a method's
clothes. The book files the method
and the presumption as separate
concepts (1.2.791, 1.2.799) so that
the next paper to spend the contrast
on unvetted context meets the
presumption named, not inherited in
silence.
# 79.2.2 — Cluster placement

AT EXTENDED — its fifteenth paper.
The country's founding shape (56.2.2)
is the trajectory as its own
reference: a contrast whose two sides
one network supplies. This paper's
contrast is exactly of that kind,
with the pair drawn from a place none
of the country's members had used:
not two models (contrastive decoding
proper, 1.2.525), not two states of
one trajectory (LoopCD), not a damaged
context (CCD), not two depths of one
stack (DoLa), not one depth against
the whole (ALW) — one model under two
inputs, the context present and the
context withheld (1.2.792). The
trajectory here is degenerate — a
dense model's single pass — and the
book files the paper in the country
because the territory is the
contrast's reference, not the
recurrence that first supplied one:
what AT's members share is that the
judged distribution is corrected by a
reference the judged thing itself
provides.

THE CONTRAST LINE, NAMED. [synthesis]
With this filing the country's
contrast members stand at five
chapter filings — LoopCD, CCD, ALW,
DoLa and this one — over six shapes
of reference, counting contrastive
decoding proper's two models, which
the book holds as a concept (1.2.525)
with its paper still queued at rank
31. The chapter names the strand the
contrast line, a sub-country of AT:
the members whose whole method is the
contrast, as against the members that
spend the trajectory on the
computation itself. The naming is
this filing's synthesis act, recorded
here and in the map (1.1.5); it moves
nothing and merges nothing, and it
exists so the next contrast paper is
weighed against a named line with a
shape-count, not against the whole
country at once. The line's open
halves stand at Q281 (a contrast
whose strength is measured, not
chosen) and Q280 (the reference's own
contamination).

J WEIGHED AND NOT JOINED — the walk's
eighth weighing since the crossing at
Chapter 71, and the second to turn on
77.2.2's distinction. J's standing
condition (62.2.2, 68.2.2): a
mechanism consults a reference
distinct from the judged object, for
a verdict whose evidence lies beyond
the judged object, spent inside the
computation. CAD fails the condition
at its first clause and its second
alike. The reference is not distinct
from the judged object: it is the
judged object itself, the same model
under a withheld input — inside the
object along the input dimension, as
DoLa's was inside it along the depth
dimension. And what the contrast
produces is steering, not a verdict:
the PMI-weighted adjustment
(1.2.793) moves the token choice; it
is not a score read against anything,
it thresholds nothing, ranks nothing,
accepts and rejects nothing, and no
reward is paid on it. Steering moves
the judged object; a verdict measures
it, and the measurement is spent as a
value (77.2.2). The context is
genuinely external evidence — the one
element of the filing that lies
beyond the judged object — but CAD
does not consult it for a verdict
about the generation; it amplifies
its influence arithmetically, which
is the steering shape entire. 1.2.716
remains J's only resident.
