# Chapter 82 — Paper 064: Beyond Parameters: Exploring Virtual Logic Depth for Scaling Laws (Zhu et al.)

THE DELTA. Four concepts
(1.2.817-1.2.820), no foundation
laid, no held concept revised, no
word coined: CLUSTER AT EXTENDED —
its eighteenth paper, and the
first filed in the country that
measures the country's founding
object instead of steering by it.
The work is Zhu et al.'s taking of
the looped transformer (1.2.523)
as a scaling dimension: repeat the
layers with tied parameters, count
the depth so bought as virtual
logical depth (1.2.817), arrange
the repetition by pattern
(1.2.818), and measure what the
added depth buys, split into the
two quantities the field's one
word 'capability' merges —
knowledge capacity, which the
repetition leaves flat, and
reasoning, which it raises: the
capacity–reasoning split (1.2.819),
its storage half read by the
absorbed-entropy measure (1.2.820).

The book has held recurrence as a
scaling axis since Paper 048
(1.2.658) and the axis's first
fitted form since Paper 055
(1.2.734, laws priced in loss).
What this filing adds is the
axis's decomposition and its
plainest construction: no readout
device, no guidance, no contrast —
the block repeated and the yield
audited in two currencies, bits
stored and problems solved. The
audit's reasoning half is
tabulated entire and recomputes
clean; its storage half stands in
a figure the text layer cannot
judge, and the filing carries it
attributed (82.1.4). Cluster
placement is weighed at 82.2.2: AT
extended, not through the contrast
line — nothing here is contrasted
— and cluster J weighed and not
joined: the work's only verdicts
are its benchmarks' answer keys,
consulted by the experimenters
after the runs, inside no
computation. The house check
recomputed the paper's printed
arithmetic (82.1.3): forty-two
declarations, forty-two pass — and
the paper's summary prose overruns
its own tables in three places,
carried at 82.1.4.

Its provenance: rank 28 of the
reference frontier built at leg 1
of the network walk — cited by
Chapter 56's paper (LoopCD) in its
bibliography — taken in as leg 25.
The queue record carried the title
and authors entire but a wrong
year (2023); the paper is
identified from its arXiv record
as Ruike Zhu, Hanwen Zhang, Kevin
Li, Tianyu Shi, Yiqun Duan, Chi
Wang, Tianyi Zhou, Arindam
Banerjee & Zengyi Qin, 'Beyond
Parameters: Exploring Virtual
Logic Depth for Scaling Laws',
arXiv:2506.18233v3 (submitted 23
Jun 2025, last revised 12 Oct
2025), and is filed under its own
title, the record's year corrected
at the marking. The work is a
network taking-in outside the
pre-registered sample (closed at
Paper 036); no seal, no score.

Axis judgment: no axis event.
Recurrence as a scaling axis is
the country's held ground (1.2.658,
1.2.734); this filing works the
axis, splitting its yield — it
opens no dimension the book did
not already hold.

NOVELTY INDEX. 4/820 = 0.0049, by
the house method — four new
concepts and no revisions, over
the 820 canonical concepts the
filing leaves.

STATE MACHINES. Three stated
machines are taken from the work
(82.1.2): the VLD scaling machine,
the capacity-measurement machine,
and the iGSM reasoning-measurement
machine. The held count rises to
250 (213 stated, 37 inferred).

RESTRUCTURING. None is run: Pass
#37 set the next trigger at Paper
065 or 820 canonical concepts, and
this filing lands exactly on the
concept count — 820, reached, not
crossed. The next restructuring
pass therefore falls due at Paper
065, one paper early by the
count's own reading.

REGISTRY PROOF STEP. The TLUF
