# Chapter 83 — Paper 065: A Framework for Few-Shot Language Model Evaluation (Gao et al.)

THE DELTA. Seven concepts
(1.2.821-1.2.827), no foundation
laid, no held concept revised, no
word coined: CLUSTER AY EXTENDED —
its fourth paper, and the first
that is not a table. The work is
the Language Model Evaluation
Harness: the apparatus that stands
between benchmarks and models so a
score belongs to the pair and not
to the laboratory (1.2.821). Its
benchmarks are declarations, not
programs (1.2.822); its models are
asked three questions and no more
(1.2.823); its multiple-choice
rankings are corrected per
character (1.2.824); its few-shot
examples are drawn by a seed fixed
in the code (1.2.825); it ships a
guard for the seam between corpus
and test set (1.2.826); and it
reports every score with a
bootstrap error bar (1.2.827).

The book has filed the country's
tables one by one — an answer key
of thirty integers (Chapter 70), a
table with its own grader (Chapter
75), the key's second year
(Chapter 76). This filing is the
grader detached from every table
and made general: the instrument
the rest of the book is measured
with, filed at last in itself.
Cluster placement is weighed at
83.2.2: AY extended — the country
is the examination and its judging,
and this work is the judging
become infrastructure; AT held
apart, its founding object nowhere
in the work; cluster J weighed and
not joined, the work's verdicts
spent at grading, after the judged
computation ends, by the harness
and not by the judged. The house
check ran against the held deposit
itself (83.1.3): twenty-nine
declarations, twenty-nine pass —
and the deposit's citation
apparatus disagrees with itself in
three places, carried at 83.1.4.

Its provenance: rank 29 of the
reference frontier built at leg 1
of the network walk — cited by
Chapter 56's paper (LoopCD) in its
bibliography, reference [14] —
taken in as leg 26. The queue
record carried the title and the
twenty-four-name byline entire and
no arXiv ID; the work is not an
arXiv paper. It is identified from
the record and the web as Leo Gao,
Jonathan Tow, Baber Abbasi, Stella
Biderman, Sid Black, Anthony
DiPofi, Charles Foster, Laurence
Golding, Jeffrey Hsu, Alain Le
Noac'h, Haonan Li, Kyle McDonell,
