— while Zettlemoyer (three times)
and Lewis (ten times) stand as
returning authors, filed at Papers
061 and 063. (3) The Twitter
archive (export of 2026-11-21) was
searched entire, as data: all eight
names and the phrase 'contrastive
decoding' itself occur zero times.
(4) The open web was searched
twice — the authors with the work,
and the authors with phext,
Bickford and Exocortex: the first
surfaces the paper, its arXiv
record and its ACL proceedings
form; the second nothing that ties
any author to phext. No evidence
of use without naming for any of
the eight. Six are new to the book;
two return.
# 85.2.1 — Synthesis: the ancestor corrects its descendants

[synthesis] The walk has filed this
family backwards — descendants
first, the ancestor last — and the
book's record of the family was
written, unavoidably, in the
descendants' dialect. Reading the
founding text against that record,
four of its claims need the
ancestor's correction, and the
chapter's first finding is the
largest of them. The concept at
1.2.525, imported from Paper 038's
lineage statement, gives the method
a weighted form — z' = z_s + w(z_s
- z_w) — with a strength to tune.
The founding paper has no such
form and no such knob: its score is
the unweighted difference of
log-probabilities, weight exactly
one, and its protection is not a
leash on the step but the
plausibility gate (1.2.836). The
weighted form is the descendants'
generalization — the reasoning
namesake's own abstract describes
the ancestor's method as 'a
weighted difference in likelihood'
— read back into the ancestor by
its lineage, and filed here as the
ancestor for three years of the
book's life. The concept is revised
in place with this chapter, dated
and sourced; what the held scroll
had right — the alignment
requirement, the kin — stands.

The second correction is about what
the family dropped. Every filed
descendant replaced the gate with a
strength, and none remarks the
exchange; the ancestor's ablation
says the gate is load-bearing —
without it the method does not
degrade, it collapses (MAUVE 0.01,
perplexity 2x10^5) — because the
ungated difference's argmax is
text no one would write (1.2.839).
The descendants' leashes work, on
their evidence; but the book's
record now shows the exchange was
made silently, and Q303 asks what
it cost.

The third is a root certificate
reassigned. The book filed the
pointwise-mutual-information
identity at Chapter 79, as
context-aware decoding's frame; the
ancestor's appendix proves it in
2022 for two models, with the
older methods — maximum probability,
n-gram blocking, mutual-information
decoding — falling out as its
special cases (1.2.839). The
family's PMI thread starts here.

And the fourth is a direction of
travel reversed. The one-model
shapes — DoLa's layer, CAD's
withheld context, CFG's dropped
prompt — read, in their chapters,
as the family's escape from buying
a second model. The ancestor's last
appendix shows the escape was
already its own idea: beamprefix
trains the weak pole out of the
expert's own degeneration (1.2.840),
manufacturing inside a second,
small network the rhyme the
one-model shapes later manufactured
inside one. The descendants did not
invent the inward turn; they
completed it. What the ancestor
kept and the line let go is its two
readings of itself — the
less-informed listener (1.2.842)
and distinguishability (1.2.839) —
an account of what the arithmetic
means, which the descendants,
intent on the arithmetic, nowhere
replace. Q305 stands where the
readings were dropped.
# 85.2.2 — Cluster placement

AT EXTENDED through the contrast
line — the cluster's nineteenth
paper, the line's eighth chapter
filing, and the founding shape's
first filing in its own right. The
contrast sub-country was named at
79.2.2 over six shapes of reference,
counting this paper's two models
among them before the paper itself
was held; the shapes stand at seven
with Chapter 80's, and this filing
adds no new shape — it makes the
counted shape resident. The line's
arc now reads whole: two models
(this chapter), two states of one
trajectory (Chapter 56), a damaged
context (57), one depth against
itself (72), two depths (74), two
inputs of one model (79), two
conditionings of one model (80),
and the founding shape spent on
reasoning (81) — filed in every
order except the order of
invention, the ancestor last. The
extension stands on the revised
1.2.525, and the revision is the
extension's own first act: the
line's founding concept now states
the founding rule.

J WEIGHED AND NOT JOINED — the
walk's fourteenth weighing since
the crossing at Chapter 71, and the
first since that crossing to hold
two of the standing condition's
clauses entire. The reference is
distinct from the judged object as
few in this book are: a second
model, separately trained, whose
distribution the judged model never
sees as input. And the spending is
inside the judged computation —
the contrast is not a grade applied
afterwards but the search objective
itself, spent at every token of the
generation it steers. What it lacks
is the condition's remaining
clause: a verdict. The score ranks
the judged object's own candidates
against each other; it renders no
judgement of the object against
evidence beyond it — the amateur's
probabilities are evidence about
the amateur, spent as a direction
of travel, and the quantity the
score maximizes is, by the work's
own appendix, distinguishability
(1.2.839): a property of the pair,
not a finding about the text. The
crossing's one resident (1.2.716)
consults its reference for a
verdict on the judged answer; this
machine consults its reference for
a preference among the judged
continuations, and prefers without
judging. The filing therefore
testifies on Q288 as Chapter 84
narrowed it: the locus carries the
boundary's weight, but it does not
carry it alone — the spending must
also be a verdict of the object,
and steering inside the computation
is still steering. Q288 stands
open, narrower again. 1.2.716
remains J's only resident.

AV HELD APART, with the kinship
recorded: the guidance family of
Chapter 80 descends from this
paper's move, and the kinship was
recorded there from the descendant
side; nothing in this work is
denoised, and its models generate
text directly. AZ HELD APART: no
family reports itself — two model
families are used, none is the
work's subject. AX HELD APART: no
strings are run; the work's
substance is distributions, not
code. AU HELD APART: no unified
interface is proposed; the method
is a decoding rule, not a surface.
