# Chapter 87 — Paper 069: Analog Bits (Chen, Zhang & Hinton)

THE DELTA. Five concepts
(1.2.849-1.2.853), one foundation
laid (1.3.381, the bit), no held
concept revised, no word coined:
CLUSTER AV EXTENDED — its fourth
paper. The work asks the question
its country's founding object had
never faced: the denoising
trajectory (1.2.615) was built for
continuous data, and the discrete
world — text, categorical images —
stood outside it, served by
autoregressive models token by
token or by diffusion rebuilt on a
discrete state space. Its answer
changes nothing about the
trajectory and everything about
its cargo: write the discrete
datum in bits, cast the bits to
real numbers, and let the
unchanged continuous model model
the reals (1.2.849), reading the
bits back by a threshold at the
end. Around that move it builds
two techniques the book files as
the trajectory's own news: the
denoiser handed its own previous
estimate as an input, the
trajectory's first memory
(1.2.850); and the sampler's clock
split from the state's, the
network told a later time than the
state it reads (1.2.851). Its
appendix spends the book's
most-descended device inside the
trajectory — the classifier-free
combination (1.2.800) run on the
model's two readings of one state
(1.2.852) — and its three
encodings price the order a binary
code lends a continuous model
(1.2.853). Cluster placement is
weighed at 87.2.2: AV extended,
the construction filed being a
denoising trajectory entire; the
contrast kinship of the appendix
device recorded for the device,
not the paper; cluster J weighed
and not joined — the construction
consults no reference and renders
no verdict, and its one threshold
reads the finished sample rather
than judging it. The house check
recomputed the work's internal
arithmetic (87.1.3): thirteen
declarations, thirteen pass, and
forty-two hand checks, four of
them the check working as designed
against the work's own pages,
carried at 87.1.4.

Its provenance: rank 33 of the
reference frontier built at leg 1
of the network walk — cited by
Chapter 56's paper (LoopCD) in its
bibliography — taken in as leg 30.
The work is identified from its
arXiv record as Ting Chen,
Ruixiang Zhang and Geoffrey
Hinton, 'Analog Bits: Generating
Discrete Data using Diffusion
Models with Self-Conditioning',
arXiv:2208.04202 — submitted
2022-08-08, revised 2023-03-01 —
and the version of record filed is
v2, the record's latest; the work
appeared at ICLR 2023. The queue
record carried the title, the
identifier and the citing chapter;
the byline and the version stand
completed at the marking. The work
is a network taking-in outside the
pre-registered sample (closed at
Paper 036); no seal, no score.

Axis judgment: no axis event. The
trajectory country is held ground
since Chapter 63, and this filing
widens its cargo and gives it a
memory — it opens no dimension the
book did not already hold.

