# 88.1.6 — Author check #78

Four legs, all run first-hand; no
evidence on any of them. (1) The
held paper text was scanned
entire — 162,686 characters: no
occurrence of phext, phextura,
Exocortex, Mirrorborn, CYOA, SBOR
or Bickford, and 'scroll' and
'coordinate' zero times each.
(2) The built tracker was scanned
for all fifty-eight names: every
one occurs zero times — all
fifty-eight authors are new to
the book, the largest single
byline it has taken in; its
surnames here are crowds of other
people and bibliography bylines
entire (a Mark Chen stands
nowhere in it; the book's Chens
are other people). (3) The
Twitter archive (export of
2026-11-21) was searched entire,
as data: eight of the names occur
— Jerry Tworek once, Greg
Brockman eleven times, Alex Paino
twice, Miles Brundage five times,
Mira Murati four, Dario Amodei
six, Ilya Sutskever twice,
Wojciech Zaremba once — every
sampled context a user-mention
record or quoted public discourse
about public figures, none a tie
to Will or his work; the work's
own words occur in their public
senses across the archive's years
('codex' 1,108 times, 'copilot'
64), none in connection with
phext; the remaining fifty names
occur zero times. (4) The open
web was searched twice — the
authors with the work, and the
authors with phext, Bickford and
Exocortex: the first surfaces the
paper, its arXiv record and its
long afterlife; the second
nothing that ties any of the
fifty-eight to phext. No evidence
of use without naming for any
author. All fifty-eight are new
to the book.
# 88.2.1 — Synthesis: the founding filed after the audit

[synthesis] The walk's backwards
filing completes another family.
Chapter 83 filed the grader with
no table of its own; Chapter 84
filed a table audited to eighty
times its depth; this chapter
files the table both of them
presupposed — the 164 hand-written
problems whose shallow form the
audit deepened, and whose name
the harness's catalogue did not
even hold. The examination country
now stands in the order the walk
keeps discovering: descendants
first, because the queue is drawn
from bibliographies, and the
founding last, carrying the
corrections only a founding can
carry. Chapter 86's founder
corrected five chapters of the
book's reading of its device; this
one corrects nothing, and that is
its own datum — the audit read the
table's descendant faithfully
enough that the ancestor, arriving
five chapters later, moves no held
scroll.

What the founding adds, read
against its descendants, is the
country's two-part engine stated
at its source: a verdict that runs
(1.2.854) and a count that prices
a budget of tries (1.2.855).
Everything the country later built
— the oracle that computes the
verdict, the suite distilled from
it, the harness that serves it —
is a variation on those two
decisions, taken here in 2021 by a
laboratory measuring its own
model. And the work's shadow is
filed with it, in its own
appendices: the first operational
measurement of misalignment in the
book (1.2.860), a definition and a
gap, printed as an afterthought
to a benchmark paper and since
grown into a field; and the chain
decay (1.2.859), the earliest
filed law of specification length
— the price of the long docstring,
which every later resident that
writes or reads specifications
pays without naming.
# 88.2.2 — Cluster placement

AY EXTENDED — the cluster's sixth
paper. The extension is made on
the country's own definition, as
the five before it were: benchmark
artifacts — the instruments the
rest of the book is measured with
— filed at the level of the
artifact itself. This work's
deliverable is exactly such an
artifact: a fixed set of 164
problems and their verdicts,
published as data (1.2.856), with
the measure the verdicts are
counted in founded in the same
work (1.2.855). It is the base
table of the country's fifth
resident: the audited HumanEval+
of Chapter 84 is this set,
deepened — so the walk files the
founding after the audit, as it
filed the contrast line's founding
at Chapter 85 and guidance's at
Chapter 86.

THE INFRASTRUCTURE REWEIGH, taken
as Chapter 84 left it. That filing
restated the condition: a third
work whose center of mass is
apparatus itself — claims about an
interface, no table of its own —
reopens the founding of a cluster
for evaluation infrastructure.
This work is weighed against the
condition and does not meet it:
it has a table of its own, and its
apparatus — the sandbox (1.2.857),
the estimator inside the measure —
makes claims about no interface;
it is the table's execution room
and counting rule, filed as the
table's provenance and anatomy
under Chapter 84's rule. The
founding is declined a third time,
and the condition stands restated
unchanged for the next arrival.

AX WEIGHED: the work is about
code — but about code as the
examination's material, programs
as answers to be graded; strings
are the judged objects, not the
work's substance or vehicle (the
ruling of 84.2.2, in its own
terms). AZ HELD APART: no family
reports itself — a laboratory's
model is examined here, not
chronicled; the byline's
institution is not the work's
subject. AT AND AV HELD APART: no
trajectory is travelled, nothing
is denoised, nothing recurs;
sampling here is repeated trial
under a verdict, not a walk along
a path. AU HELD APART: no unified
interface is proposed; the sandbox
is one work's room, not a surface
offered to others.

J WEIGHED AND NOT JOINED — the
walk's seventeenth weighing since
the crossing at Chapter 71, on
77.2.2's distinction as narrowed
at Chapter 84. J's standing
condition (62.2.2, 68.2.2): a
mechanism consults a reference
distinct from the judged object,
for a verdict whose evidence lies
beyond it, spent inside the
computation. The work holds three
verdict-spendings, and each is
weighed. The grading verdict: a
reference as distinct as a
reference can be — tests written
by other hands, whose contents
the judged model never sees —
verdict in form, evidence beyond
the object entire; and it is spent
in the sandbox after the judged
computation ends, on finished
artifacts, the shape Chapter 84
narrowed Q288 against: locus
absent. The oracle reading of
pass@k: the work itself names the
measure an oracle's pick — but an
oracle inside the counting is not
a mechanism inside the run;
nothing in any generation consults
it. The self-filter (88.1.2): the
nearest loop the walk has filed
since the crossing — the model's
own samples are judged by the
tests, and the verdict is really
spent, on the training set of the
next model. But the spending lands
on the curriculum, one stage up
and one run later; inside any
single judged computation no
verdict is consulted, and the
locus clause, as narrowed, is a
clause about the judged
computation. The weighing
testifies on Q288 as narrowed: the
boundary holds at the locus even
when a verdict closes a loop
around the computation entire —
around is not inside. Q288 stands
open. 1.2.716 remains J's only
resident.
