record of the Archive's item
pasteursquadrant00stok, the citing
scholarship that quotes the work
(Ramaley 2007, fetched entire;
Aldulijan et al. 2022, as indexed),
and the reference literature's
rendering of its table. The book's
body stands behind the Archive's
lending wall and is not held.

THE FRONTIER IS UN-WALKED FOR THIS
FILING, AND THE RECORD SAYS SO. The
references leg reads a work's
bibliography; this work's
bibliography stands at its pages
153-173 — inside the restricted
text, named by its catalogue record
and not held. The leg therefore
returned zero, and no hand fallback
exists to exercise: there is no list
to classify. The frontier the book
would open — the postwar
science-policy canon its notes cite,
Bush's report first among them by
the argument's own shape — stands
unenumerated, and any future
reading of the book entire owes the
walk that frontier then. What the
filing can state is the one
bibliographic fact the catalogue
carries: twenty-one pages of
references (pp. 153-173), in a book
whose records disagree on whether
it runs 180, 196 or 200 pages
(Q363).
