# 100.1.4 — Caveats

1. THE VERSION MOVED, AND THE
CHAPTER'S COORDINATES ARE v2's.
The work was reorganized between
v1 (June 2026) and v2 (August
2026): what stands at Section 14
here (the Artin-Rees lemma) stood
at Section 12 in v1's contents.
Every section and result number in
this chapter is the held version's;
a reader holding v1 will not find
the results where this chapter
puts them. The citing chapter
named v2, and v2 is what is filed.

2. THE CHECK VERIFIES THE RECORD,
NOT THE MATHEMATICS. Identity,
version, structure, cross-
reference and bibliography are
verified against the held text;
the theorems are attributed to
their authors on the standing
basis. A reader who needs the
proofs needs the paper — all 49
pages of it are held, and the
filing's concepts are a map of its
claims, not a re-derivation.

3. THE FUNCTORS FILED ARE THE
CLOSED FORMS, THROUGHOUT. This
work's Casselman-Jacquet functors
are defined with closure (1.2.931);
the algebraic functor of [CGYD19]
and the unclosed intersections of
the older literature are different
objects wearing the same name.
Where the two definitions could
agree is itself an open seam of
the field (Q367), and nothing in
this chapter silently identifies
them.

4. THE SLIPS STAND AS PRINTED.
Four apparent misprints (100.1.3)
are quoted byte-exact and left
uncorrected: the tracker records
the work as it stands, and a
correction entered silently here
would falsify the record the house
check just verified. If any proves
to be the extraction's artifact
rather than the authors', the
journal version is the court.

5. AFFILIATIONS ARE THE WORK'S
OWN PAGE, NOTHING MORE. Zhang
stands at Huazhong on this work's
title page, with an email at
Peking; a sequel prints him at
Hong Kong. The filing records the
held page. Researchers move; the
record of a work does not.
# 100.1.5 — Open questions, and novelty by author

Q366 — THE NUCLEARITY CONJECTURE
(Conjecture 19.6, the work's own):
if pi is nuclear, the canonical
embedding's image is closed, and
(Phi^+)^k o (Phi^-)^k (pi) is
Lambda_k(pi) itself for every k —
the filtration machine (100.1.2,
M4) files the image, not its
closure. Casselman-Wallach
representations are nuclear, and
the case the field most uses is
settled by other roads in the
sequel at queue rank 70; the
general Frechet case stands where
the work leaves it, with Example
19.5's non-nuclear space as the
warning that the hypothesis is
load-bearing.

Q367 — THE FOLKLORE CLOSEDNESS:
the work states, after Corollary
12.8, that "it is believed that
n^k . pi is closed in pi while a
general proof seems not to be
known" for Casselman-Wallach pi,
and reduces the folklore conjecture
to the principal-series case
through the Casselman embedding.
A proof, or one principal series
whose n^k . pi is not closed,
decides. Until one arrives, the
closed forms of 1.2.931 and the
unclosed subspaces of the older
theory stand unbridged at exactly
this point.

Q368 — THE MISSING ARTIN-REES:
exactness here runs on an
Artin-Rees transferred from the
algebraic side (1.2.935), available
only inside the Casselman-Wallach
category; for Rep^{infty,F} entire
no Artin-Rees is available, and
stabilization itself fails for
modules that are not finitely
generated (Remark 1.5). Is there a
named class between the two —
nuclear representations are the
work's own candidate shape (Q366)
— where the closure-form
Artin-Rees holds and Part I's
seminorm machine becomes a
corollary?

Q369 — THE BIJECTION'S TOPOLOGY:
Corollary 18.4's canonical map from
Phi^+ o Phi^-(pi) onto the open
orbit's Schwartz space is a
continuous bijection, "not
necessarily a homeomorphism"
(Remark 1.11). What decides
whether the two topologies agree —
and is nuclearity, again, the
price (Q366)? The work raises the
shape twice and prices it nowhere.

Q370 — THE BRANCHING PAYOFF: the
work declares itself one leg of a
project [Ch23, CW26] toward
branching laws for real GL_n on
the p-adic blueprint, and its
authors' sequels ([WZ25+] new to
the queue at this filing; [WY26+]
already at rank 70) are unexamined.
When they are filed, does the
stability theory here carry the
load the program assigns it — and
does Paper 036's proof, which
consumed this work to prove the
comparison, close the circuit the
program drew, or only its first
arc?

