# 101.2.1 — Synthesis: the cited manuscript, filed [synthesis]

[synthesis] Chapter 54 closed the pre-
registered sample by spending a work the
book did not hold: a manuscript, cited
from a bibliography, its proof of (3.4)
taken on the strength of a name and a
year. This filing reverses that debt as
Paper 082's did — the tracker now holds
the spent work at its source. And the
source, read entire, turns out to have
been standing on the book from the other
side: its own bibliography cites the
citing paper for a second proof of its
Theorem B, and the functor paper for the
exactness its last reduction consumes.
Three works, each spending the other
two; the walk has now filed all three
corners of the triangle, and the
cluster's ground is closed under its own
citations at this depth.

[synthesis] The work's subject is
extension — the theorem that nothing
living on an open piece of the flag
variety is lost when the space closes
around it, provided the piece is stable
and the distributions are finite in the
right direction. Its method is the
registry's method wearing analysis:
reduce to order zero, price the boundary
with one character that vanishes on all
of it, continue meromorphically, and
remove the poles by descending induction
— every step labelled with what it cost,
nothing quotiented away silently. It
arrives in the book as the hundred-and-
first chapter: a manuscript the record
once held only as a citation key, now
held whole — the difference between the
two holdings is the whole of what the
walk is for.
# 101.2.2 — Cluster placement: AR extended; J weighed a thirtieth time

