for the theorem (1.2.495) closes by
naming the minimal-parabolic case 'the
prior held result of the field
(Hecht-Taylor; Li-Liu-Yu)'. This filing
holds that case at its source: the
comparison theorem at the minimal
parabolic (1.2.947), proved by
distribution theory alone, and the
closedness theorem that strengthens
automatic continuity beside it
(1.2.948). The proof's machinery files
with it: the Casselman-Jacquet module
as the locally nilpotent part (1.2.949)
— the construction Chapter 54's orbit
comparison spends as D^[u] undefined —
its exactness on the Bruhat sequences
(1.2.950), its regular-density form on
a cell (1.2.951), the transversal
degree filtration and the Bruhat
filtration it descends (1.2.952), and
the scalar comparison on a nilpotent
homogeneous space at the descent's
bottom (1.2.953). No held concept is
revised: 1.2.495, 1.2.504, 1.2.505,
1.2.507 and 1.2.508 were weighed and
held (102.2.2) — each states its own
paper's construction truly, and this
