# 102.2.1 — Synthesis: the prior case, filed [synthesis]

[synthesis] Chapter 54's founding
theorem arrived in the book with its
history attached as a parenthesis:
'the minimal-parabolic case was the
prior held result of the field
(Hecht-Taylor; Li-Liu-Yu)'. Three
filings later the parenthesis is a
chapter. The pattern is the walk's own
rhythm in this cluster — Chapter 100
filed the functor Chapter 54's chain
consumed, Chapter 101 the manuscript
its proof cited, and now Chapter 102
the result its first concept named as
already-known: AR's ground keeps
turning out to have been load-bearing
before it was held, and the walk keeps
paying the debt in the order the
citations present it.

[synthesis] The work's method is the
registry's method wearing analysis, a
second time in this cluster: where
Xiao reduced extension to order zero
and priced a boundary, this work
reduces comparison to a scalar cell
and prices nothing — it computes. The
Jacquet module of the cell's
distributions is the regular functions;
the functor is exact exactly where the
proof walks; the closure bar in a
forty-year-old theorem turns out to
have been removable all along, and its
removal is the paper's quiet headline.
It arrives as the hundred-and-second
chapter: a mention in a bibliography's
wake — 'Liu et al.', no title — that
resolved, on the held records entire,
to the proof the founding chapter had
already told the book was there.
