reference to Borel–Wallach belongs —
an artifact of the held HTML form,
noted as such. None of the six
touches a filed claim: each stands
in narration or in a pointer whose
target the surrounding text fixes
unambiguously.

Attributed, not verified: the proofs
themselves. This is a
pure-mathematics filing: the house
check verifies the record of the
work's claims — identity, version,
structure, internal cross-reference,
the bibliography, and the citation
chain that brought the walk here —
and no computation in the work is of
