# 108.2.1 — Synthesis: the deduction at its source [synthesis]

[synthesis] Read whole, the remark is
the cluster's smallest complete
machine: two pages of held text that
contain a theorem, its premise, and
the transport between them, with the
proof's one hard case named and its
resolution begun. The comparison
country was founded on a chapter that
spends this work twice — once as a
credit line in its opening survey,
once as a working step inside its
main proof — and the walk has now
arrived at the source both spends
point to. What the remark adds to the
country is not another comparison but
the comparison's RELAY form: a
theorem proved for the small
completion, where the D-module
machinery of its decade could reach,
and then carried across an embedding
to the large completion, where the
field actually lived. Every later
chapter of the country replays the
shape at higher power — Paper 084
re-proving the minimal case to feed
its own closedness theorem, Paper 036
closing the general case by filtrations
built on this volume's other chapters —
but the shape itself, theorem-to-
theorem transport along a canonical
embedding, stands first and plainest
here, in eight pages of which the
house holds two. That the held two
are the two that carry the shape —
statement, premise, reduction,
resolution — and that the unheld six
carry only its execution, is the
filing's good fortune, recorded as
fortune and not as method at 108.1.4.
