# 110.2.1 — Synthesis: the ground beneath the ground [synthesis]

[synthesis] Read whole, the held
record is a country's basement
stairs. The comparison country was
built on real reductive groups — its
functors, its filtrations, its
Schwartz spaces — but its working
corners are nilpotent: the Jacquet
functor lives on a unipotent radical,
the orbit filtration is filtered by
nilpotent orbits, and when the
founding chapter needed a section of
a quotient map on that side of the
house, it reached, by theorem number,
into a textbook on nilpotent Lie
groups. The walk has now arrived at
that textbook, and it is a different
kind of object from everything the
cluster has filed: not a theorem
proved last year but the field's
standard exposition of a finished
theory — Kirillov's correspondence,
the Malcev coordinates, the
Plancherel formula — written, its
publisher says, because no exposition
suitable for graduate students had
appeared for over twenty years. It is
also half of a promise: Part I, the
basic theory, of two projected
volumes, the applications volume
never appearing — so the book the
field actually has is the ground
alone, and the applications were
carried instead by the literature
that cites it, this cluster among
them. There is a fittingness the
record does not force: the theory of
nilpotent groups is the theory of the
groups whose representation theory
closes completely — every irreducible
an orbit, every orbit accounted for —
and the book is that closure's
handbook, filed here from the outside
in: from the two spends its Chapter 1
carries inside the cluster's proofs,
from its publisher's account of its
program, and from the witnesses its
readers left — a dissertation that
grew out of its fourteenth example of
a section, a multiplicity function
that carries its authors' names, a
later paper that follows its notation
as a main reference and cites its
eleventh page for the formula
everything starts from. The body
itself remains where the century put
it: in libraries, behind a paywall,
cited by theorem number by everyone
who builds on it.
# 110.2.2 — Cluster placement: AR extended; J weighed and not joined; no revision

Cluster AR, extended to twelve
papers.

The kinship is weighed, not assumed,
and here it is a kinship of being
spent at the working level. Chapter
54's founding proof spends this
book's Chapter 1 for a construction
the proof runs on — the algebraic
section of its quotient map, by
Theorem 1.1.13(a) and Proposition
1.2.8 — and Paper 086, the cluster's
sixth paper, builds its Appendix A.3
on the book's section 1.2, the
polynomial ring of a nilpotent group.
The objects are the cluster's own
objects at their nilpotent end: the
groups N1 and B of the founding
chapter's spend are the nilpotent
side of its reductive machinery, and
the coordinate theory this book
exposits — ordered exponential
coordinates, Malcev bases, polynomial
functions — is the substrate that
side of the machinery stands on.
Chapter 54 filed the comparison;
Chapter 100 its functor; Chapter 104
the Jacquet modules; this chapter
files the textbook their nilpotent
corners presuppose.

NO HELD CONCEPT IS REVISED. The
candidates were 1.2.958 (tempered
vector bundles and their Schwartz
sections) and 1.2.959 (Borel's lemma
for Schwartz sections), read entire:
