# 113.2.1 — Synthesis: the engine room, filed fifteenth [synthesis]

[synthesis] Read whole, the
cluster has been running on this
paper's machinery since its
founding chapter. Chapter 54's
main proof takes its finite
generation from the paper's
Lemma 2.22 and its homology
groups' category standing from
its Proposition 2.24 — working
steps, not decorations. Paper
084's comparison proof quotes
its Lemma 2.37 as 'a theorem of
Hecht-Schmid', the form a field
uses for a result it no longer
argues about. Paper 082 takes
its Frobenius reciprocity from
its Theorem 4.9. What the paper
itself proves is the identity
the whole neighbourhood
presupposes: a character on the
group is an Euler characteristic
of homology on the Levi — the
bridge between the analytic
object (the character, with its
asymptotics) and the algebraic
one (the homology, with its
exponents) that every later
comparison theorem in the
cluster crosses. The authors
prove it ab initio, re-proving
their ingredients as they go,
because — their introduction
says it plainly — the conjecture
turned out to explain the
results it was first deduced
from: Langlands' classification
and Harish-Chandra's tempered
estimates among them. The walk's
order filed the theorem's
descendants first and the engine
room fifteenth, because the
queue's order is the citing
chapters' bibliography order.
What the filing changes is not
any held claim — no scroll is
revised — but the footing: the
three spends now stand on a
filed source whose own
constructions (the identity, the
vanishing, the [n]-part, the
reciprocity) are on the record
in its own dress, and the
crossing the ledger makes at
this filing's sixth concept is
the reciprocity itself — the
oldest tool in the room carries
the count over the line.
# 113.2.2 — Cluster placement: AR extended; J weighed and not joined; no revision

Cluster AR extends to fifteen
papers. The placement is weighed
from the work's own construction,
not its citations: the paper is
the n-homology character theory
of Harish-Chandra modules — the
identity of a character with an
Euler characteristic of homology
on the Levi, its vanishing
theorem, and its reciprocity —
and the citing chain spends it
inside the cluster's proofs, at
the founding proof's finiteness
step, at a comparison proof's
duality step, and at a stability
proof's reciprocity step. No
other cluster's ground touches
it.

Cluster J is weighed a
forty-second time and not
joined, against the standing
test (77.2.2, as narrowed at
Chapter 84; Q323's shape): the
identity computes the judged
object's character from the
judged object's own homology —
the evidence never leaves the
module; Frobenius reciprocity
is an isomorphism of Hom-sets,
proved in the paper, not a
verdict consulted from a
reference distinct from the
judged object; coherent
continuation transports the
identity across a family of the
judged objects themselves. No
mechanism in the work consults
a reference distinct from the
judged object for a verdict
spent inside a computation.
1.2.716 remains J's only
resident.

The infrastructure-founding
alternative is weighed a
twenty-sixth time under Chapter
84's restated condition and
declined: the work is a research
paper of its field — heavily
consulted by the cluster, but a
paper is read, not re-run;
nothing in it is an examination
or an apparatus built to be
re-run by strangers as a
measure.

