Cluster AR extends to seventeen
papers. The placement is weighed
from the work's own construction,
not its citations: the book is
the general theory of filtered
and graded rings — filtrations,
their completions, the graded
objects assembled from them —
and the citing chain spends its
Chapter I inside the cluster's
founding proof, at the
completion step, in the same
sentence as Paper 096's theorem.
It stands where Paper 096
stands, and for the same reason:
an algebra treatise the
cluster's proofs run on, filed
at its source. No other
cluster's ground touches it.

Cluster J is weighed a
forty-fourth time and not
joined, against the standing
test (77.2.2, as narrowed at
Chapter 84; Q323's shape): the
book's mechanisms are a
construction on the judged ring
itself (its filtration and the
completion the filtration
carries) and properties proved
of the judged objects (exactness
of their completion, finiteness
of their graded forms) — the
evidence never leaves the judged
object; no mechanism consults a
reference distinct from it for a
verdict spent inside a
computation. 1.2.716 remains J's
only resident.

The infrastructure-founding
alternative is weighed a
twenty-eighth time under
Chapter 84's restated condition
and declined: the work is a
treatise of its field — heavily
consulted by the cluster, but a
treatise is read, not re-run;
nothing in it is an examination
or an apparatus built to be
re-run by strangers as a
measure.

No revision: 1.2.1066 states the
