# 119.1.4 — Caveats

(1) The held text is the arXiv v3
(1 December 2024), the author's
final preprint; the citing chapter
prints the journal form
(Bernoulli, 2025). Pagination and
small dress may differ between the
forms; the filing reads the arXiv
text entire and files
constructions, not glyphs — and
the text extraction's dress is
TeX-ish (the crude tag-strip
triples some displayed formulas),
so theorem statements are filed
from the readable rendering,
checked against the source HTML
where a constant mattered. (2)
Theorem 1.5's bracket: the bounds
are filed as this paper's result;
the bracket's closure at
(3/4)^{2/3} is Basu and
Bhattacharjee's later work [4],
filed as attributed inside
1.2.1106, not as this paper's
claim. (3) Theorem 3.1 is quoted
from the author's joint work [11]
(Chen–Khoshnevisan–Nualart–Pu,
2023): the filing files the
transfer as this paper's
construction and the SHE
association as [11]'s theorem,
spent by name. (4) The queue
record's 'Pu et al.' was the
mention extractor's standing form
for a surname record; the byline
is solo, and the record is
completed at the marking. (5) Two
of the paper's five theorems rest
on inputs the paper itself takes
from the record — the cubic
covariance decay from [5] for
Theorem 1.1's variance, the
determinant formula from [28] for
Proposition 6.1; the concepts file
those spendings as the paper
states them.
# 119.1.5 — Open questions Q458-Q461

Q458. The Airy_2 constant from
inside (1.2.1106): Basu and
Bhattacharjee [4] closed Theorem
1.5's bracket at its upper end,
(3/4)^{2/3}, by last-passage
methods. Can the association route
— which proves A_2 associated
(1.2.1099) and prices A_1's
maximum exactly — be pushed to the
constant, or is the bracket the
method's ceiling? Q459. The CLT's
variance (1.2.1103): σ² = ∫
Cov(A_1(x), A_1(0)) dx is proved
to lie in (0, ∞) and given no
value, closed form, or variational
identity anywhere in the paper.
What is σ²? Q460. Ergodicity and a
CLT for Airy_2 (1.2.1099,
1.2.1103): the paper proves A_2
associated but states no
ergodicity theorem and no CLT for
it — its Airy_2 results are the
association and the maximum
bounds. Does the same route give
A_2's ergodicity and a CLT with
variance ∫ Cov(A_2(x), A_2(0)) dx,
and is that integral finite on the
Airy_2 covariance's decay? Q461.
The separation scale (1.2.1104):
Theorem 1.3 buys Poisson behaviour
at separations beyond (3 log
N)^{1/3}. Is that scale sharp — do
exceedances at smaller separations
cluster, and at what rate? The
anti-clustering question (Q176) on
this paper's ground.
