three-family comparison, so the
claim files attributed, and the
missing numbers stand as Q462.
(2) The internal evidence (RQ1–RQ3)
runs on three benchmarks only
(LAMBADA, MMLU, SIQA), on sampled
subsets of their test sets, under
a strict-string-matching generative
protocol whose absolute scores the
paper itself calls low; figure-read
values (the timeshift peaks, the
CFG and step curves) file
attributed, not recomputed. (3)
The baselines are the authors' own
retrainings under matched settings
(the paper's stated protocol);
no external checkpoint of AR or
LLaDA is scored, and LLaDA's
denoising length is set to the
generation length by the protocol's
own choice. (4) The multimodal
extension (Section 5.5) is a
preliminary prototype on internal
data, qualitative only, by the
paper's own statement; it files as
the paper's direction, not as a
result (Q466). (5) The held text
is the arXiv v1 HTML; the crude
tag-strip triples displayed
formulas in TeX dress, and table
cells were verified against the
source rendering wherever a filed
number rests on one (Tables 2, 3,
5, 6 recompute entire — 120.1.3).
(6) The paper's Afterword (Section
8) argues a broader
model-environment programme; the
filing files the construction and
its evidence, and the Afterword's
programme stands as the authors'
framing, not as filed claims.
# 120.1.5 — Open questions Q462–Q466

Q462: Section 4.5's scaling
comparison prints no final numbers
— the three families' Task
Averages at the largest budget
(about 2000 EFLOPs) stand only in
Figure 10. What are they, and by
what margin does Cola DLM lead?
Q463: The applicability boundary
(1.2.1114) rests on the
rate-distortion curve D(R) of text
being small at low rate — an
assumption the paper states (3.34)
but nowhere measures. Is D(R) for
natural text actually measured,
here or anywhere?
Q464: Latent compression by patch
size 2 collapses on odd-length
prompts (1.2.1119). Can a patching
scheme — variable grouping, a
length-aware condition — keep the
compression's doubled coverage
without the parity failure?
Q465: The chosen operating point
(CFG scale 7, 16 denoising steps,
schedule loc=1) comes from
three-benchmark curves at about
117 EFLOPs. Does it hold at the
scaling study's budgets and at
other latent dimensions?
Q466: The unified text-image
prototype of Section 5.5 is
qualitative and on internal data.
Does the shared-prior extension
survive a public benchmark — and
does the ELBO decomposition's
restated form (Appendix 14) hold
its terms when the modalities
differ in kind?
