# 120.2.1 — Synthesis [synthesis]: the path moved from the sample to the prior

Read against the book, Paper 102
relocates the diffusion path. The
book's diffusion country was built
on recovery: LaDiR's trajectory
denoises a latent thought toward a
clean one; the CFG founding's
trajectory forms an image from
noise; Plaid, named in this
paper's own table, recovers
token-aligned embeddings. Cola
DLM's path does none of these —
it transports a prior, from a base
Gaussian to the learned
distribution of a semantic latent,
and text appears only afterwards,
at the decoder. The bookkeeping
consequence the paper itself
draws is the ELBO's third term:
prior matching becomes a named,
separately owned job, and its
quality is measurable apart from
reconstruction. The theoretical
consequence is the burden
criterion: a latent model is not
an autoregressive model with an
extra part — it is a different
risk decomposition, and it wins
only where the data's global
structure is cheap to carry
(1.2.1114). The empirical
consequence the paper is honest
about: the two smoothnesses come
apart (1.2.1115), so the class
must be judged on generation, not
likelihood. Filed as the cluster's
extension because the construction
keeps AV's arrangement — learned
latent space, flow path, decodable
blocks — while changing the path's
object; the change itself is filed
as 1.2.1108, where a future paper
can cite it without reopening the
cluster call.
# 120.2.2 — Cluster weighing: AV extends; AT and AW held apart; J declined a forty-ninth time

CLUSTER AV EXTENDS to five papers.
Weighed from the work's own
construction: AV's arrangement,
from its founding filings, is a
sample formed from noise in a
space learned for the purpose,
each block decodable as it forms.
Cola DLM meets the arrangement
term for term — its latent space
is learned for the purpose (the
Text VAE, 1.2.1109); its blocks
form from noise under the flow
prior (1.2.1110); each block is
realized by the conditional
decoder as it forms. What differs
from the founding filings is the
path's object — prior transport,
not observation recovery — and
that difference files INSIDE the
cluster as 1.2.1108, the same
shape of internal difference the
cluster already carries (Paper
059's image-sampler path; Paper
068's guided combination). AT HELD
APART: no state is recomputed at
growing depth anywhere in the
construction; the block-causal
factorization is a factorization
of the prior, not a recurrence,
and the denoising trajectory's
kinship is AV's by the country's
own definition. AW HELD APART:
Cola DLM is a construction with
experiments, not a survey of the
field; its latent is a semantic
prior space, not a reasoning
space. A NEW CLUSTER DECLINED: the
construction does not stand apart
from AV's arrangement on any term
the cluster's own definition
names. J WEIGHED A FORTY-NINTH
TIME, DECLINED: the paper's CFG
spends a conditioning contrast to
STEER the denoising (77.2.2's
steering side of the line, as
filed at Chapter 80 and in AV's
guidance concepts); its CNF
density evaluation scores a latent
by the model's own density — no
reference distinct from the judged
object is consulted, and no
verdict is spent inside a
computation (Q323's shape not
met; the boundary's locus stands
where Chapter 84 put it).
INFRASTRUCTURE FOUNDING DECLINED
A THIRTY-THIRD TIME under Chapter
84's restated condition: a
research construction, not an
apparatus for the field. REVISIONS
WEIGHED AND HELD (0): 1.2.615 (the
denoising trajectory — Cola's path
transports a prior and files
beside it as 1.2.1108; 615's
statement stands as filed);
1.2.612 (the learned latent
thought space — a space learned
for reasoning; Cola's semantic
prior space files as its own
concepts, 1.2.1109–1.2.1110);
1.2.800 and 1.2.801 (the CFG
founding and its
implicit-classifier qualification
— this paper spends CFG as an
inference-time scale and files no
construction of it); 1.2.663
(continuous tokens — Cola's
latents are never token-aligned;
the distinction is the paper's
own Table 1 point against Plaid).
