# Chapter 121 — Paper 103: Breaking the Square-Root Barrier for the Log-Rank Conjecture (Cogentic)

'Breaking the Square-Root Barrier
for the Log-Rank Conjecture' — a
paper with no human byline. Its
first page carries only a
footnote: 'This paper was
entirely obtained by Cogentic
[4], an agentic framework for
mathematical discovery, using
Gemini 4 as the base model.
There was no human interaction
other than the initial prompt
for Cogentic to generate a full
proof.' The directory record
(google-research/google-research,
cogentic_research_papers/
logrank_conjecture/, tree at
commit 4a7bc8ab0bc7) adds that a
Lean 4 formalization 'has also
been completed and will be
released in a companion
submission' — announced, not
held; and the harness was built
by Yang Cai, Vineet Gupta,
Yanchen Jiang, Christopher Liaw,
Aranyak Mehta, Grigoris Velegkas
and Di Wang (Google Research and
Google DeepMind), the system's
makers, not this work's authors.
A Will-directed test-filing: Will
chose this paper from the
Cogentic directory assessment in
the MOAT chat (2026-11-25) to be
filed end to end, the filing
itself the grade. No queue rank —
the queue is untouched by this
filing. The text is held entire:
paper.pdf, 823,350 bytes, 37
pages, fetched once from the
tree at the named commit and
reused for every leg; no
partial-text clause applies. The
claim (Theorem 1.1): with
ε := 5×10^{−6}, C := 2^{38} and
C′ := 750 C, every Boolean matrix
of real rank r ≥ 1 has a
monochromatic rectangle of
density at least 2^{−C r^{1/2−ε}},
and every rank r ≥ 2 matrix
satisfies D^cc(M) ≤ C′ r^{1/2−ε}
— past the square-root line of
Lovett (2016) and Sudakov and
Tomon (2023). Cluster BA's first
paper (121.2.2). Twelve concepts
(1.2.1120–1.2.1131), no
foundation, five questions
(Q467–Q471), two state machines
stated. TRIGGER CROSSED: the
concept ledger reaches 1,131,
and its first concept (1.2.1120)
crosses the 1,120 line set by
Restructuring Pass #52 —
Pass #53 stands due and is NOT
run by this filing.
# 121.1.2 — The formal core: the claim, the reduction, and the cubic identity

Concepts filed: 1.2.1120 the
log-rank conjecture, the
standing problem entire;
1.2.1121 deterministic
communication complexity and
the partition number, the
model and its chain; 1.2.1122
monochromatic rectangle density,
the Nisan–Wigderson currency;
1.2.1123 the square-root
barrier, the methods' ceiling;
1.2.1124 the Rademacher stability
example, the ceiling's tightness
witness; 1.2.1125 biased
KL-stable sign matrices, Theorem
3.1's nonexistent object;
1.2.1126 one-sided KL stability;
1.2.1127 the distributional
trace norm and square-root
Bregman regularity; 1.2.1128 the
Boolean cubic identity, the
proof's turning point; 1.2.1129
bulk singular-vector
regularization; 1.2.1130 hollow
quadratic slices, extraction
against annihilation; 1.2.1131
the degree-2 Gaussian tilt, the
barrier's escape. No foundation
laid: the country's level-zero
notions (the rectangle, the
protocol, the rank) file inside
1.2.1120–1.2.1122. The proof's
skeleton, in the paper's own
order: §2 builds the
distributional SVD, the Bregman
remainder and the consequences
of one-sided stability; §3.1
reduces Theorem 1.1 to Theorem
3.1 — box-constrained biasing
(Lemma 3.3) gives a biased
product measure, a potential
minimization (the equilibrium
machine, 1.5.2) gives Bregman
regularity, sub-Gaussian
marginals and stability, and
Gaussian hyperplane rounding
(Lemma 3.2) guards both ends of
the bias interval; §§4–6 then
prove Theorem 3.1 by
regularizing the bulk (§4),
extracting a dense hollow slice
map (§5) and annihilating it
with the degree-2 tilt (§6);
Appendix A proves the classical
estimates and the explicit
Nisan–Wigderson constant
(Proposition A.3). New against
cited, as the text itself draws
it: the reduction's frame
(Nisan–Wigderson [13], Lovett's
rounding [11]) and the appendix's
analysis (Beckner [1], Bonami
[3], Pisier [14], Slepian [15],
John [7]) are cited; the cubic
identity, the regularization,
the extraction and the tilt are
the paper's own. Two state
machines are stated (the
deterministic protocol tree; the
variational equilibrium
construction) — state machines
stand at 372 held (335 stated,
37 inferred, on the areas'
drawing). Five questions opened:
Q467–Q471 (121.1.5). No held
concept revised: the field's
every term stood at zero in the
entering book; the country is
new entire. The filing's
increments (True +2, Unknown
+19) are carried whole by the
work's author as it names
itself, Cogentic, drawn at this
filing (121.1.6).
