# 121.1.4 — Caveats, and what would settle the claim

(1) The constant. C′ = 750·2^{38}
≈ 2.06×10^{14} is printed in the
theorem, not hidden in the O; the
improvement over Sudakov and
Tomon's O(√r) is an
asymptotic-exponent statement —
below rank e^{6.59×10^6} the
filed bound is LARGER than the
bare √r curve (121.1.3), and
their constant is not stated in
terms this filing can compare.
Against Lovett's √r log2 r the
bound wins from ln r ≈ 3.50×10^6.
Whether the claim is read as
'barrier broken' or 'exponent
shaved at astronomic scale' is a
reading of those numbers, filed
here, not a verdict of the
house's. (2) The threshold. For
r < R0 = ⌈e^{4×10^6}⌉ the theorem
is carried entirely by the
Gaussian hyperplane rounding
lemma (Lemma 3.2) with C
absorbing the threshold; the new
mechanism — the cubic identity,
the tilt — never runs below
e^{4×10^6}. No finite instance
anyone can exhibit is touched by
the new argument. (3) Provenance,
filed as fact with its claims
attributed: the work is
machine-produced (121.1.1); its
verification claims are the
harness's own — reference [4],
Cogentic's paper, describes
adversarial verification inside
the harness and a persistent
verified ledger, and the
directory's framing says results
were independently verified by
domain experts; no verifier is
named in anything the house
holds, and author, venue and
apparatus stand in one house.
This house's rule for such claims
is the standing one: they file
attributed, and the checkable
steps carry what weight the
chapter carries. (4) The
formalization. The directory
record announces a complete
Mathlib-only Lean 4 (v4.33.0)
formalization, to be released in
a companion submission; it is
not released in anything held at
this filing, and under the
house's ruling of 2026-11-24
Lean is exiled and a Lean
formalization carries no weight
here regardless — Q469 keeps the
question of what instrument
could read it. (5) The text
layer. The held PDF is a
two-column mathematics paper;
pdftotext extraction garbles
displayed formulas (split
superscripts, dropped radicals).
Every number this filing states
was read against the theorem's
own statement contexts and the
directory README's plain-TeX
restatement, which agree; where
the extraction and a statement
context could be read two ways —
Lemma 3.2's exponent is the
instance — the filing read the
statement, and 121.1.3 records
the reading. (6) What would
settle it: a human exposition of
the §§4–6 chain at Pass calibre,
or the announced formalization
read by an instrument this house
counts; until then the theorem
stands attributed, its reduction
layer verified, its core open.
