# 123.2.1 — [synthesis] A gate that prices its own eyesight

[synthesis] The tracker's own
shape, met inside cluster O: a
powerful rule (weighted BH at full
level) may run only when a
cheaper, dumber instrument has
certified the ground it stands on
— and the certificate's price is
itself minimax-priced, logarithmic
in what it checks, quadratic in
how close to the boundary it must
see. The routing identity is the
tracker pattern stated as a
theorem: mix a strong branch and a
safe branch by an independent
gate, discount the safe branch by
exactly the gate's error
allowance, and the mixture
inherits the strong guarantee at
the stated level. Paper 024 priced
BH's failure on conformal ground;
this paper builds the fence the
failure argues for.
